const COURSE = [{"n":1,"block":"Primeros pasos","title":"Hello! Saludos y presentarte","emoji":"👋","minutes":25,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás saludar, decir tu nombre, preguntar cómo está alguien, deletrear tu nombre y despedirte en inglés.","sections":[{"h":"Tu primera conversación","body":"Imagina que llegas a Orlando y un compañero de trabajo se acerca. Lo primero que pasa es un saludo. En inglés es muy sencillo.\n\n**Hello** y **Hi** significan *hola*. **Hi** es más informal y lo usas con amigos. **Hello** funciona en cualquier situación, incluso en una entrevista de trabajo.\n\nDespués del saludo, casi siempre viene el nombre y la pregunta **How are you?** (*¿cómo estás?*)."},{"h":"Saludos según la hora del día","table":{"head":["Inglés","Cuándo se usa","Significa"],"rows":[["Good morning","Desde que te levantas hasta el mediodía","Buenos días"],["Good afternoon","Desde el mediodía hasta las 5 o 6 p. m.","Buenas tardes"],["Good evening","Al caer la noche, para saludar","Buenas noches (al llegar)"],["Good night","Solo para despedirte o irte a dormir","Buenas noches (al irte)"]]},"note":"Cuidado: **Good night** NO es un saludo. Lo dices cuando te vas a dormir o te despides de noche."},{"h":"Presentarte y conocer a alguien","body":"Para decir tu nombre usa **My name is...** (*mi nombre es...*). También puedes decir **I'm...** (*soy...*), que es más corto y muy natural.\n\nCuando alguien te dice su nombre, respondes **Nice to meet you.** (*mucho gusto*). La otra persona contesta **Nice to meet you, too.** (*igualmente*).\n\nEjemplo de mini diálogo:\n\n**A:** Hi, my name is Ana.\n**B:** Hello, Ana. I'm Santiago. Nice to meet you.\n**A:** Nice to meet you, too."},{"h":"How are you? y sus respuestas","table":{"head":["Respuesta","Significa","Cómo se siente"],"rows":[["I'm great!","¡Estoy genial!","Muy bien"],["I'm fine, thanks.","Estoy bien, gracias.","Bien (la más común)"],["I'm OK.","Estoy regular / más o menos.","Normal"],["Not so good.","No muy bien.","Mal"]]},"note":"Después de responder, devuelve la pregunta: **And you?** (*¿y tú?*). Es de buena educación en inglés."},{"h":"El alfabeto y cómo deletrear tu nombre","body":"En inglés mucha gente te pedirá deletrear tu nombre: **How do you spell your name?** Por eso es importante conocer las letras. Las vocales suenan así: **A** (ei), **E** (i), **I** (ai), **O** (ou), **U** (iu).\n\nOtras letras que confunden a los hispanohablantes: **G** (yi), **J** (yei), **H** (eich), **W** (dábol-iu), **Y** (uai), **Z** (zi).\n\nPara tu nombre, di las letras una por una: **S-A-N-T-I-A-G-O**. Y si tu apellido tiene una doble letra, di **double** antes de la letra: **double L**."},{"h":"Despedidas y error típico","list":["**Goodbye.** (*Adiós.*) Es la más general.","**Bye.** (*Chao.*) Informal, entre amigos.","**See you later.** (*Nos vemos luego.*)","**See you tomorrow.** (*Nos vemos mañana.*)","**Have a nice day!** (*¡Que tengas un buen día!*) Muy común en Estados Unidos, hasta con los cajeros.","Error típico: decir *I am call Santiago*. Lo correcto es **My name is Santiago** o **I'm Santiago**."]}],"vocab":[{"en":"hello","es":"hola","ex":"Hello, I'm Santiago."},{"en":"hi","es":"hola (informal)","ex":"Hi, Ana!"},{"en":"good morning","es":"buenos días","ex":"Good morning, teacher."},{"en":"good afternoon","es":"buenas tardes","ex":"Good afternoon, everyone."},{"en":"good evening","es":"buenas noches (al llegar)","ex":"Good evening, welcome to Orlando."},{"en":"good night","es":"buenas noches (al irte)","ex":"Good night, see you tomorrow."},{"en":"name","es":"nombre","ex":"My name is Santiago."},{"en":"nice to meet you","es":"mucho gusto","ex":"Nice to meet you, Sam."},{"en":"how are you?","es":"¿cómo estás?","ex":"Hi, Ana. How are you?"},{"en":"fine","es":"bien","ex":"I'm fine, thanks."},{"en":"great","es":"genial","ex":"I'm great today!"},{"en":"thanks","es":"gracias","ex":"Thanks, and you?"},{"en":"and you?","es":"¿y tú?","ex":"I'm fine. And you?"},{"en":"spell","es":"deletrear","ex":"How do you spell your name?"},{"en":"goodbye","es":"adiós","ex":"Goodbye, Mr. Smith."},{"en":"bye","es":"chao","ex":"Bye, Ana!"},{"en":"see you later","es":"nos vemos luego","ex":"See you later, Tom."},{"en":"see you tomorrow","es":"nos vemos mañana","ex":"Good night, see you tomorrow."}],"examples":[{"en":"Hello, my name is Santiago.","es":"Hola, mi nombre es Santiago."},{"en":"Hi, I'm Ana.","es":"Hola, soy Ana."},{"en":"Good morning, Mr. Johnson.","es":"Buenos días, señor Johnson."},{"en":"Nice to meet you, Sam.","es":"Mucho gusto, Sam."},{"en":"Nice to meet you, too.","es":"Igualmente."},{"en":"How are you today?","es":"¿Cómo estás hoy?"},{"en":"I'm fine, thanks. And you?","es":"Estoy bien, gracias. ¿Y tú?"},{"en":"I'm great, thank you!","es":"¡Estoy genial, gracias!"},{"en":"How do you spell your name?","es":"¿Cómo se deletrea tu nombre?"},{"en":"It's S-A-N-T-I-A-G-O.","es":"Es S-A-N-T-I-A-G-O."},{"en":"Good night, see you tomorrow.","es":"Buenas noches, nos vemos mañana."},{"en":"Bye! Have a nice day!","es":"¡Chao! ¡Que tengas un buen día!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"Son las 8:00 a. m. Saludas a tu profesora: Good ___, teacher.","options":["morning","evening","night"],"answer":0,"why":"Por la mañana se dice Good morning."},{"type":"choice","q":"Alguien te dice: Nice to meet you. ¿Qué respondes?","options":["Nice to meet you, too.","Goodbye.","I'm fine."],"answer":0,"why":"Se responde con Nice to meet you, too (igualmente)."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es la mejor respuesta a How are you?","options":["My name is Ana.","I'm fine, thanks.","Nice to meet you."],"answer":1,"why":"How are you? pregunta cómo estás, y se responde con I'm fine, thanks."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál de estas frases es una despedida?","options":["Hello","See you later","Nice to meet you"],"answer":1,"why":"See you later significa nos vemos luego."},{"type":"choice","q":"Te vas a dormir. Dices: ___.","options":["Good morning","Good afternoon","Good night"],"answer":2,"why":"Good night se usa para despedirte de noche o antes de dormir."},{"type":"fill","q":"My ___ is Santiago.","answer":["name"],"why":"My name is... significa mi nombre es..."},{"type":"fill","q":"Nice to ___ you.","answer":["meet"],"why":"La frase fija es Nice to meet you."},{"type":"fill","q":"How ___ you?","answer":["are"],"why":"La pregunta correcta es How are you?"},{"type":"fill","q":"I'm fine, ___. And you?","answer":["thanks","thank you"],"why":"Thanks o thank you significa gracias."},{"type":"fill","q":"How do you ___ your name?","answer":["spell"],"why":"Spell significa deletrear."},{"type":"order","words":["name","My","Santiago","is"],"answer":"My name is Santiago","es":"Mi nombre es Santiago."},{"type":"order","words":["meet","to","Nice","you"],"answer":"Nice to meet you","es":"Mucho gusto."},{"type":"order","words":["you","How","today","are"],"answer":"How are you today","es":"¿Cómo estás hoy?"},{"type":"order","words":["tomorrow","you","See"],"answer":"See you tomorrow","es":"Nos vemos mañana."},{"type":"translate","es":"Hola, me llamo Ana.","answer":["Hello, my name is Ana.","Hi, my name is Ana.","Hello, I'm Ana.","Hi, I'm Ana.","Hello, I am Ana.","Hi, I am Ana."],"why":"Se usa My name is... o I'm... para presentarte."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mucho gusto.","answer":["Nice to meet you.","Nice to meet you","Pleased to meet you."],"why":"Nice to meet you es la frase estándar al conocer a alguien."},{"type":"translate","es":"Estoy bien, gracias.","answer":["I'm fine, thanks.","I am fine, thanks.","I'm fine, thank you.","I am fine, thank you.","I'm good, thanks.","I'm good, thank you."],"why":"I'm fine se dice para responder cómo estás."}],"speak":["Hello, my name is Santiago.","Nice to meet you.","How are you today?","I'm fine, thanks. And you?","How do you spell your name?","S-A-N-T-I-A-G-O.","Good morning, everyone.","Goodbye, see you tomorrow."],"tip":"Error común: decir *I am call Santiago* o *I call me Santiago* porque en español decimos *me llamo*. En inglés no se traduce literal: usa **My name is Santiago** o **I'm Santiago**. Además, no uses *Good night* para saludar: es solo para despedirte."},{"n":2,"block":"Primeros pasos","title":"El verbo to be (ser y estar)","emoji":"🧍","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir quién eres, cuántos años tienes, de dónde eres y cómo te sientes usando am, is y are.","sections":[{"h":"Una palabra para dos verbos","body":"En español tenemos dos verbos: *ser* y *estar*. En inglés solo hay uno: **to be**.\n\nPor eso **I am a student** significa *soy estudiante* y **I am tired** significa *estoy cansado*. El contexto te dice cuál de los dos es.\n\nEste verbo es el más importante del inglés. Lo vas a usar en cada conversación."},{"h":"Los pronombres sujeto","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Significa","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["I","yo","I am Santiago."],["you","tú / usted / ustedes","You are my friend."],["he","él","He is my brother."],["she","ella","She is my teacher."],["it","ello (cosas, animales, ideas)","It is a big park."],["we","nosotros","We are students."],["they","ellos / ellas","They are from Mexico."]]},"note":"En inglés SIEMPRE se dice el pronombre. No puedes decir solo *am a student*: tiene que ser **I am a student**. Y **it** se usa para cosas, nunca para personas."},{"h":"Cómo se conjuga: forma larga y forma corta","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Forma larga","Forma corta","Significa"],"rows":[["I","I am","I'm","yo soy / estoy"],["you","you are","you're","tú eres / estás"],["he","he is","he's","él es / está"],["she","she is","she's","ella es / está"],["it","it is","it's","es / está"],["we","we are","we're","nosotros somos / estamos"],["they","they are","they're","ellos son / están"]]},"note":"Al hablar, casi todo el mundo usa la forma corta: **I'm**, **she's**, **they're**. La forma larga se usa para dar énfasis o al escribir algo muy formal."},{"h":"Edad: I'm 20","body":"En español *tenemos* años. En inglés los *somos*. Por eso se usa **to be**, no *have*.\n\nCorrecto: **I am 20** o **I am 20 years old**.\nIncorrecto: *I have 20 years*.\n\nAsí que Santiago diría: **I'm 20 years old.** Y su hermana: **She's 15.**"},{"h":"Estados y sentimientos","table":{"head":["Inglés","Significa","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["happy","feliz","I'm happy today."],["sad","triste","He's sad."],["tired","cansado/a","We're tired."],["hungry","con hambre","I'm hungry!"],["thirsty","con sed","She's thirsty."],["cold / hot","con frío / con calor","I'm cold in Bogotá."],["busy","ocupado/a","They're busy at work."]]},"note":"Error típico: *I have hungry* o *I have cold*. En inglés usamos to be: **I'm hungry**, **I'm cold**."},{"h":"Ser vs. estar: cómo saber cuál es","body":"No tienes que decidir tú: en inglés siempre es **am / is / are**. Solo piensa en el pronombre.\n\n**I** va con **am**. **He, she, it** van con **is**. **You, we, they** van con **are**.\n\nEjemplos: **She is a doctor** (ser, profesión), **She is at work** (estar, lugar), **She is happy** (estar, sentimiento). Todo con la misma palabra: **is**."}],"vocab":[{"en":"I","es":"yo","ex":"I am a student."},{"en":"you","es":"tú / ustedes","ex":"You are very kind."},{"en":"he","es":"él","ex":"He is my friend."},{"en":"she","es":"ella","ex":"She is from Miami."},{"en":"it","es":"ello (cosas)","ex":"It is a nice day."},{"en":"we","es":"nosotros","ex":"We are in Orlando."},{"en":"they","es":"ellos","ex":"They are at the park."},{"en":"student","es":"estudiante","ex":"I'm a university student."},{"en":"teacher","es":"profesor/a","ex":"She's my English teacher."},{"en":"friend","es":"amigo/a","ex":"He's my best friend."},{"en":"years old","es":"años de edad","ex":"I'm 20 years old."},{"en":"happy","es":"feliz","ex":"We're happy today."},{"en":"sad","es":"triste","ex":"He's sad."},{"en":"tired","es":"cansado/a","ex":"I'm tired after work."},{"en":"hungry","es":"con hambre","ex":"They're hungry."},{"en":"thirsty","es":"con sed","ex":"I'm thirsty."},{"en":"busy","es":"ocupado/a","ex":"She's busy today."},{"en":"ready","es":"listo/a","ex":"I'm ready for the trip."}],"examples":[{"en":"I'm Santiago.","es":"Soy Santiago."},{"en":"I'm 20 years old.","es":"Tengo 20 años."},{"en":"I'm a university student.","es":"Soy estudiante universitario."},{"en":"You're my friend.","es":"Tú eres mi amigo."},{"en":"He's my brother.","es":"Él es mi hermano."},{"en":"She's a teacher.","es":"Ella es profesora."},{"en":"It's a big park.","es":"Es un parque grande."},{"en":"We're in Orlando.","es":"Estamos en Orlando."},{"en":"They're from Mexico.","es":"Ellos son de México."},{"en":"I'm hungry.","es":"Tengo hambre."},{"en":"She's tired today.","es":"Ella está cansada hoy."},{"en":"We're happy.","es":"Estamos felices."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"She ___ a student.","options":["am","is","are"],"answer":1,"why":"She es tercera persona singular: is."},{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ 20 years old.","options":["am","is","have"],"answer":0,"why":"Con I se usa am, y la edad se dice con to be, no con have."},{"type":"choice","q":"We ___ in Orlando.","options":["is","are","am"],"answer":1,"why":"We va con are."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice Tengo hambre?","options":["I have hungry.","I am hungry.","I has hungry."],"answer":1,"why":"Los estados se dicen con to be: I am hungry."},{"type":"choice","q":"It ___ a beautiful day.","options":["is","are","am"],"answer":0,"why":"It va con is."},{"type":"fill","q":"They ___ happy. (to be)","answer":["are"],"why":"They va con are."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ a student. (to be)","answer":["am"],"why":"I va con am."},{"type":"fill","q":"He ___ my brother. (to be)","answer":["is"],"why":"He va con is."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ 20 years old. (Yo / forma corta)","answer":["i'm","im"],"why":"I am se contrae como I'm."},{"type":"fill","q":"You ___ my friend. (to be)","answer":["are"],"why":"You siempre va con are."},{"type":"order","words":["I","am","from","Colombia"],"answer":"I am from Colombia","es":"Soy de Colombia."},{"type":"order","words":["She's","a","teacher"],"answer":"She's a teacher","es":"Ella es profesora."},{"type":"order","words":["tired","are","We","today"],"answer":"We are tired today","es":"Estamos cansados hoy."},{"type":"order","words":["old","I'm","years","20"],"answer":"I'm 20 years old","es":"Tengo 20 años."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella es mi hermana.","answer":["She is my sister.","She's my sister."],"why":"Ella se traduce como She, y ser como is."},{"type":"translate","es":"Tengo 20 años.","answer":["I am 20 years old.","I'm 20 years old.","I am 20.","I'm 20."],"why":"La edad se dice con to be: I am 20."},{"type":"translate","es":"Nosotros estamos cansados.","answer":["We are tired.","We're tired."],"why":"We va con are, y tired significa cansado."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ellos son de México.","answer":["They are from Mexico.","They're from Mexico."],"why":"They va con are."}],"speak":["I'm Santiago.","I'm 20 years old.","I'm a university student.","She's my sister.","We're in Orlando.","They're happy today.","I'm hungry and tired.","He's my best friend."],"tip":"Error común: traducir *tener* literal. En español *tengo 20 años, tengo hambre, tengo frío*. En inglés todo eso es **to be**: **I'm 20, I'm hungry, I'm cold**. Y no olvides el pronombre: nunca digas *Am a student*, siempre **I am a student**."},{"n":3,"block":"Primeros pasos","title":"To be: negativo, preguntas y respuestas cortas","emoji":"❓","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir que algo no es así, hacer preguntas con to be y responder con respuestas cortas.","sections":[{"h":"El negativo: agrega not","body":"En la clase pasada aprendiste **am / is / are**. Para decir que algo *no* es así, solo agregas **not** después del verbo.\n\n**I am not** tired. (*No estoy cansado.*)\n**She is not** a teacher. (*Ella no es profesora.*)\n**They are not** from Spain. (*Ellos no son de España.*)\n\nPara hablar rápido usamos contracciones, que verás en la tabla."},{"h":"Negativo: forma larga y corta","table":{"head":["Sujeto","Forma larga","Formas cortas","Significa"],"rows":[["I","I am not","I'm not","yo no soy / no estoy"],["you","you are not","you aren't / you're not","tú no eres / no estás"],["he","he is not","he isn't / he's not","él no es / no está"],["she","she is not","she isn't / she's not","ella no es / no está"],["it","it is not","it isn't / it's not","no es / no está"],["we","we are not","we aren't / we're not","no somos / no estamos"],["they","they are not","they aren't / they're not","no son / no están"]]},"note":"Ojo: con **I** solo existe **I'm not**. Nunca se dice *I amn't*."},{"h":"Preguntas: cambia el orden","body":"En español hacemos una pregunta cambiando la entonación. En inglés cambias el **orden**: el verbo **to be** pasa al inicio.\n\nAfirmación: **You are** a student.\nPregunta: **Are you** a student?\n\nAfirmación: **She is** at work.\nPregunta: **Is she** at work?\n\nNo se puede decir *You are a student?* como pregunta formal. El verbo va primero."},{"h":"Respuestas cortas","table":{"head":["Pregunta","Sí","No"],"rows":[["Are you a student?","Yes, I am.","No, I'm not."],["Is he your brother?","Yes, he is.","No, he isn't."],["Is she tired?","Yes, she is.","No, she isn't."],["Is it a big park?","Yes, it is.","No, it isn't."],["Are they from Brazil?","Yes, they are.","No, they aren't."],["Are we late?","Yes, we are.","No, we aren't."]]},"note":"En el **Yes** nunca se contrae: **Yes, I am** (no *Yes, I'm*). En el **No** sí: **No, he isn't**."},{"h":"Palabras para preguntar con to be","table":{"head":["Palabra","Significa","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["What","¿qué? / ¿cuál?","What's your name?"],["Where","¿dónde?","Where are you from?"],["Who","¿quién?","Who is he?"],["How","¿cómo?","How are you?"],["How old","¿cuántos años?","How old are you?"],["When","¿cuándo?","When is the class?"]]},"note":"La palabra de pregunta va primero, luego **am / is / are** y después el sujeto: **Where is** the hotel? **What are** your names?"},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["Decir *Are you from Colombia?* y responder solo *Yes, I'm.* Lo correcto es **Yes, I am.**","Olvidar el verbo: *Where you from?* Debe ser **Where are you from?**","Decir *How old do you have?* Lo correcto es **How old are you?**","Mezclar: *He no is tired.* Lo correcto es **He isn't tired.**"]}],"vocab":[{"en":"not","es":"no (negación)","ex":"I'm not tired."},{"en":"isn't","es":"no es / no está","ex":"She isn't here."},{"en":"aren't","es":"no son / no estás","ex":"We aren't late."},{"en":"yes","es":"sí","ex":"Yes, I am."},{"en":"no","es":"no","ex":"No, he isn't."},{"en":"what","es":"qué / cuál","ex":"What's your name?"},{"en":"where","es":"dónde","ex":"Where are you?"},{"en":"who","es":"quién","ex":"Who is she?"},{"en":"how","es":"cómo","ex":"How are you?"},{"en":"how old","es":"cuántos años","ex":"How old are you?"},{"en":"when","es":"cuándo","ex":"When is the party?"},{"en":"here","es":"aquí","ex":"I'm here at the hotel."},{"en":"there","es":"allá","ex":"The park is there."},{"en":"late","es":"tarde (retrasado)","ex":"We aren't late."},{"en":"married","es":"casado/a","ex":"He isn't married."},{"en":"single","es":"soltero/a","ex":"I'm single."},{"en":"from","es":"de (origen)","ex":"Where are you from?"},{"en":"at home","es":"en casa","ex":"I'm at home today."}],"examples":[{"en":"I'm not tired.","es":"No estoy cansado."},{"en":"She isn't my teacher.","es":"Ella no es mi profesora."},{"en":"They aren't at home.","es":"Ellos no están en casa."},{"en":"Are you a student?","es":"¿Eres estudiante?"},{"en":"Yes, I am.","es":"Sí, lo soy."},{"en":"Is he your brother?","es":"¿Es tu hermano?"},{"en":"No, he isn't.","es":"No, no lo es."},{"en":"What's your name?","es":"¿Cuál es tu nombre?"},{"en":"Where are you from?","es":"¿De dónde eres?"},{"en":"How old are you?","es":"¿Cuántos años tienes?"},{"en":"Where is the hotel?","es":"¿Dónde está el hotel?"},{"en":"Who is she?","es":"¿Quién es ella?"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"He ___ tired.","options":["aren't","isn't","am not"],"answer":1,"why":"He va con is, y el negativo es isn't."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ you from Colombia?","options":["Is","Am","Are"],"answer":2,"why":"You va con are, y en la pregunta va primero."},{"type":"choice","q":"Are they students? Respuesta correcta:","options":["Yes, they're.","Yes, they are.","Yes, they is."],"answer":1,"why":"En el Yes corto no se contrae: Yes, they are."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se pregunta la edad de alguien?","options":["How old are you?","How old do you have?","What old are you?"],"answer":0,"why":"La edad se pregunta con How old + to be."},{"type":"choice","q":"Is she your sister? No, ___.","options":["she isn't","she aren't","she amn't"],"answer":0,"why":"She va con is, y en negativo es isn't."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ not tired today. (to be)","answer":["am"],"why":"Con I siempre se usa am, incluso en negativo: I am not."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ at home. (negativo, forma corta)","answer":["isn't","is not"],"why":"She is not se contrae como isn't."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ are you from?","answer":["where"],"why":"Para preguntar el origen se usa Where."},{"type":"fill","q":"Are you late? No, I ___.","answer":["am not","'m not","i'm not","im not"],"why":"Con I solo existe I'm not, no existe amn't."},{"type":"fill","q":"Is he a doctor? Yes, he ___.","answer":["is"],"why":"En el Yes corto no se contrae: Yes, he is."},{"type":"order","words":["you","Are","a","student"],"answer":"Are you a student","es":"¿Eres estudiante?"},{"type":"order","words":["isn't","He","my","brother"],"answer":"He isn't my brother","es":"Él no es mi hermano."},{"type":"order","words":["are","Where","you","from"],"answer":"Where are you from","es":"¿De dónde eres?"},{"type":"order","words":["name","your","What's"],"answer":"What's your name","es":"¿Cuál es tu nombre?"},{"type":"translate","es":"No estoy cansado.","answer":["I am not tired.","I'm not tired."],"why":"El negativo con I es I'm not."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Ella es tu amiga?","answer":["Is she your friend?"],"why":"La pregunta lleva is al inicio."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Cuántos años tienes?","answer":["How old are you?"],"why":"La edad se pregunta con How old are you?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Ellos no están en casa.","answer":["They aren't at home.","They are not at home.","They're not at home."],"why":"They va con are, y el negativo es aren't."}],"speak":["I'm not tired.","She isn't my teacher.","Are you a student?","Yes, I am.","No, he isn't.","What's your name?","Where are you from?","How old are you?"],"tip":"Error común: responder *Yes, I'm.* o *No, I amn't.* En las respuestas cortas con **Yes** no se contrae (**Yes, I am**), y con **I** el negativo es **I'm not** (no existe *amn't*). Y recuerda: la pregunta lleva el verbo primero, no es solo cambiar la entonación."},{"n":4,"block":"Primeros pasos","title":"Pronombres, artículos y plurales","emoji":"🔤","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás usar pronombres de sujeto y objeto, los artículos a/an/the, formar plurales y señalar cosas con this y that.","sections":[{"h":"Pronombres de sujeto y de objeto","body":"Ya conoces los pronombres de sujeto (**I, you, he...**), que hacen la acción. Ahora aprendemos los de **objeto**, que reciben la acción y van *después* del verbo.\n\n**I like him.** (*Me gusta él / lo aprecio.*)\n**She helps me.** (*Ella me ayuda.*)\n\nEn español usamos *me, te, lo, la*. En inglés se ponen detrás del verbo."},{"h":"Tabla de pronombres","table":{"head":["Sujeto","Objeto","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["I","me","She calls me."],["you","you","I see you."],["he","him","We know him."],["she","her","I help her."],["it","it","I like it."],["we","us","He helps us."],["they","them","I call them."]]},"note":"**You** e **it** no cambian. También se usan los pronombres de objeto después de preposiciones: **with me**, **for you**, **to them**."},{"h":"Los artículos a, an y the","body":"**A** y **an** significan *un / una*. Se usan con cosas singulares, cuando hablas de algo por primera vez.\n\nUsa **a** antes de un sonido de consonante: **a** book, **a** teacher, **a** university.\nUsa **an** antes de un sonido de vocal: **an** apple, **an** hour, **an** engineer.\n\nOjo: importa el *sonido*, no la letra. *University* empieza con sonido *iu* (consonante), por eso es **a university**. *Hour* empieza con sonido vocal porque la *h* no se pronuncia, por eso es **an hour**.\n\n**The** significa *el / la / los / las*. Se usa cuando es algo específico que ya se conoce: **the hotel**, **the park**."},{"h":"Plurales regulares","table":{"head":["Regla","Singular","Plural"],"rows":[["Casi todos: agrega -s","book","books"],["Terminan en s, x, ch, sh: agrega -es","bus","buses"],["Terminan en s, x, ch, sh: agrega -es","box","boxes"],["Consonante + y: cambia a -ies","city","cities"],["Consonante + y: cambia a -ies","party","parties"],["Vocal + y: solo -s","day","days"]]},"note":"Los artículos **a / an** no se usan en plural: **a book** pero **books**. Y los verbos cambian: **The books are here.**"},{"h":"Plurales irregulares","table":{"head":["Singular","Plural","Significa"],"rows":[["man","men","hombre / hombres"],["woman","women","mujer / mujeres"],["child","children","niño / niños"],["person","people","persona / personas"],["foot","feet","pie / pies"],["tooth","teeth","diente / dientes"]]},"note":"**People** ya es plural: **The people are friendly**, no *the people is*. Estos plurales hay que memorizarlos."},{"h":"This, that, these, those","table":{"head":["Palabra","Cuándo","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["this","una cosa, cerca de ti","This is my phone."],["that","una cosa, lejos de ti","That is the castle."],["these","varias cosas, cerca","These are my friends."],["those","varias cosas, lejos","Those are big hotels."]]},"note":"Error típico: confundir **this** (cerca) con **that** (lejos). Piensa: *this* = *esto de aquí*, *that* = *eso de allá*."}],"vocab":[{"en":"me","es":"me / a mí","ex":"Call me later."},{"en":"him","es":"lo / a él","ex":"I know him."},{"en":"her","es":"la / a ella","ex":"I help her."},{"en":"us","es":"nos / a nosotros","ex":"He helps us."},{"en":"them","es":"los / a ellos","ex":"I call them."},{"en":"a","es":"un / una","ex":"I have a phone."},{"en":"an","es":"un / una (ante vocal)","ex":"She has an apple."},{"en":"the","es":"el / la / los / las","ex":"The park is big."},{"en":"book","es":"libro","ex":"This is a book."},{"en":"box","es":"caja","ex":"Those are boxes."},{"en":"city","es":"ciudad","ex":"Orlando is a big city."},{"en":"man / men","es":"hombre / hombres","ex":"Those men are engineers."},{"en":"woman / women","es":"mujer / mujeres","ex":"The women are teachers."},{"en":"child / children","es":"niño / niños","ex":"The children are happy."},{"en":"person / people","es":"persona / personas","ex":"Many people are here."},{"en":"this","es":"esto / este","ex":"This is my phone."},{"en":"that","es":"eso / aquel","ex":"That is my friend."},{"en":"engineer","es":"ingeniero/a","ex":"I'm an engineer student."}],"examples":[{"en":"I like her.","es":"Ella me cae bien."},{"en":"She calls me every day.","es":"Ella me llama todos los días."},{"en":"We know them.","es":"Los conocemos."},{"en":"This is a book.","es":"Esto es un libro."},{"en":"That is an apple.","es":"Eso es una manzana."},{"en":"I'm a student at a university.","es":"Soy estudiante en una universidad."},{"en":"The park is big.","es":"El parque es grande."},{"en":"Those are my friends.","es":"Esos son mis amigos."},{"en":"There are two buses.","es":"Hay dos buses."},{"en":"Two cities, three boxes.","es":"Dos ciudades, tres cajas."},{"en":"The children are happy.","es":"Los niños están felices."},{"en":"These men are engineers.","es":"Estos hombres son ingenieros."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I help ___. (a mi hermana)","options":["she","her","hers"],"answer":1,"why":"Después del verbo va el pronombre de objeto: her."},{"type":"choice","q":"She is ___ engineer.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":1,"why":"Engineer empieza con sonido de vocal, por eso an."},{"type":"choice","q":"He is ___ university student.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":0,"why":"University empieza con sonido iu, que es consonante: a."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el plural de child?","options":["childs","children","childes"],"answer":1,"why":"Child es irregular: children."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ is my phone. (está en tu mano)","options":["This","That","Those"],"answer":0,"why":"This se usa para una cosa que está cerca."},{"type":"fill","q":"Please help ___. (a mí)","answer":["me"],"why":"El objeto de I es me."},{"type":"fill","q":"We know ___. (a ellos)","answer":["them"],"why":"El objeto de they es them."},{"type":"fill","q":"one box, two ___","answer":["boxes"],"why":"Las palabras que terminan en x llevan -es."},{"type":"fill","q":"one city, two ___","answer":["cities"],"why":"Consonante + y cambia a -ies."},{"type":"fill","q":"one man, two ___","answer":["men"],"why":"Man es irregular: men."},{"type":"fill","q":"I have ___ apple. (a o an)","answer":["an"],"why":"Apple empieza con vocal: an."},{"type":"order","words":["help","I","her"],"answer":"I help her","es":"Yo la ayudo."},{"type":"order","words":["is","This","my","phone"],"answer":"This is my phone","es":"Este es mi teléfono."},{"type":"order","words":["children","The","are","happy"],"answer":"The children are happy","es":"Los niños están felices."},{"type":"order","words":["an","She","is","engineer"],"answer":"She is an engineer","es":"Ella es ingeniera."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella me ayuda.","answer":["She helps me."],"why":"Me es el pronombre de objeto de I y va después del verbo."},{"type":"translate","es":"Eso es un hotel.","answer":["That is a hotel.","That's a hotel."],"why":"That se usa para lo que está lejos, y hotel pide a."},{"type":"translate","es":"Las mujeres son profesoras.","answer":["The women are teachers."],"why":"Woman hace women en plural, y se usa are."}],"speak":["She helps me.","I know him.","This is my phone.","That is a big castle.","I'm a student at a university.","She is an engineer.","The children are happy.","Those are my friends."],"tip":"Error común: decir *a university* como *an university* porque empieza con la vocal u, o *the people is*. Recuerda: importa el **sonido** (**a university**, **an hour**) y **people** es plural (**the people are**). También: *I like he* es incorrecto; después del verbo va el objeto: **I like him**."},{"n":5,"block":"Primeros pasos","title":"Los números","emoji":"🔢","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás contar hasta miles, decir teléfonos, precios, edades, años y los ordinales básicos.","sections":[{"h":"Del 0 al 20","table":{"head":["Número","Inglés","Número","Inglés"],"rows":[["0","zero","11","eleven"],["1","one","12","twelve"],["2","two","13","thirteen"],["3","three","14","fourteen"],["4","four","15","fifteen"],["5","five","16","sixteen"],["6","six","17","seventeen"],["7","seven","18","eighteen"],["8","eight","19","nineteen"],["9","nine","20","twenty"],["10","ten","",""]]},"note":"Del 13 al 19 todos terminan en **-teen**. Cuidado con **15** (fifteen, no *fiveteen*) y **18** (eighteen, solo una t)."},{"h":"De 20 a 100: las decenas","table":{"head":["Decena","Inglés","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["20","twenty","twenty-one (21)"],["30","thirty","thirty-five (35)"],["40","forty","forty-two (42)"],["50","fifty","fifty-six (56)"],["60","sixty","sixty-seven (67)"],["70","seventy","seventy-eight (78)"],["80","eighty","eighty-nine (89)"],["90","ninety","ninety-nine (99)"],["100","one hundred","one hundred (100)"]]},"note":"Para números compuestos se une con guion: **twenty-one**, **forty-five**. Ojo con **forty**: se escribe sin la u, no *fourty*."},{"h":"Cientos y miles","body":"Para los cientos, di el número y luego **hundred**: **two hundred** (200), **five hundred** (500).\n\nPara los miles, igual con **thousand**: **three thousand** (3,000), **ten thousand** (10,000).\n\nEn inglés americano normalmente no se dice **and** en medio: 125 es **one hundred twenty-five**. Y atención: *hundred* y *thousand* **no llevan -s** cuando hay un número antes: *two hundred*, no *two hundreds*.\n\nEn inglés los miles se separan con **coma** (1,000) y los decimales con **punto** (4.99). Es lo contrario de Colombia."},{"h":"Teléfonos y datos personales","body":"Los números de teléfono se dicen **dígito por dígito**. El cero se puede decir **zero** u **oh**.\n\n(407) 555-0142 → **four oh seven, five five five, oh one four two.**\n\nEl signo $ se lee al final: $4.99 es **four ninety-nine** (informal) o **four dollars and ninety-nine cents** (formal). $20 es **twenty dollars**.\n\nPara la edad ya sabes: **I'm twenty years old.** Si preguntan **How old are you?** respondes solo con el número: **Twenty.**"},{"h":"Cómo se dicen los años","table":{"head":["Año","Se lee","Nota"],"rows":[["1999","nineteen ninety-nine","Se parte en dos pares"],["1984","nineteen eighty-four","Dos pares"],["2005","two thousand five","También: twenty oh five"],["2020","twenty twenty","Dos pares"],["2026","twenty twenty-six","Dos pares"],["2000","two thousand","Caso especial"]]},"note":"Los años no se leen como cantidades. *1999* no es *one thousand nine hundred...*, sino **nineteen ninety-nine**."},{"h":"Ordinales básicos","table":{"head":["Número","Ordinal","Significa"],"rows":[["1","first (1st)","primero"],["2","second (2nd)","segundo"],["3","third (3rd)","tercero"],["4","fourth (4th)","cuarto"],["5","fifth (5th)","quinto"],["10","tenth (10th)","décimo"]]},"note":"Después del 3 casi todos terminan en **-th**. Cuidado con **fifth** (la f cambia) y **twelfth**. Ejemplo: **the first day**, **the third floor**."}],"vocab":[{"en":"zero","es":"cero","ex":"My phone number has a zero."},{"en":"one","es":"uno","ex":"I have one brother."},{"en":"ten","es":"diez","ex":"I have ten dollars."},{"en":"thirteen","es":"trece","ex":"He's thirteen years old."},{"en":"fifteen","es":"quince","ex":"It's fifteen dollars."},{"en":"twenty","es":"veinte","ex":"I'm twenty years old."},{"en":"thirty","es":"treinta","ex":"There are thirty students."},{"en":"forty","es":"cuarenta","ex":"It's forty dollars."},{"en":"fifty","es":"cincuenta","ex":"She's fifty."},{"en":"hundred","es":"cien","ex":"One hundred people are here."},{"en":"thousand","es":"mil","ex":"Two thousand dollars."},{"en":"phone number","es":"número de teléfono","ex":"What's your phone number?"},{"en":"price","es":"precio","ex":"What's the price?"},{"en":"dollar","es":"dólar","ex":"It's five dollars."},{"en":"cent","es":"centavo","ex":"Ninety-nine cents."},{"en":"year","es":"año","ex":"The year is 2026."},{"en":"first","es":"primero","ex":"Today is my first day."},{"en":"second","es":"segundo","ex":"The second floor."},{"en":"third","es":"tercero","ex":"The third question."},{"en":"how much","es":"cuánto cuesta","ex":"How much is this?"}],"examples":[{"en":"I'm twenty years old.","es":"Tengo veinte años."},{"en":"There are thirty students.","es":"Hay treinta estudiantes."},{"en":"It's twenty-one dollars.","es":"Cuesta veintiún dólares."},{"en":"This is four ninety-nine.","es":"Esto cuesta 4.99."},{"en":"How much is this?","es":"¿Cuánto cuesta esto?"},{"en":"What's your phone number?","es":"¿Cuál es tu número de teléfono?"},{"en":"It's four oh seven, five five five, one two three four.","es":"Es 407-555-1234."},{"en":"I was born in nineteen ninety-nine.","es":"Nací en 1999."},{"en":"It's twenty twenty-six.","es":"Estamos en 2026."},{"en":"I live on the third floor.","es":"Vivo en el tercer piso."},{"en":"It's two hundred dollars.","es":"Cuesta doscientos dólares."},{"en":"Today is my first day.","es":"Hoy es mi primer día."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice 15?","options":["fiveteen","fifteen","fiftin"],"answer":1,"why":"15 se escribe fifteen, no fiveteen."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice 40?","options":["fourty","forty","fortie"],"answer":1,"why":"Forty se escribe sin la u."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es la forma correcta de decir 200?","options":["two hundreds","two hundred","twenty hundred"],"answer":1,"why":"Hundred no lleva -s cuando hay un número antes."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se lee 1999 como año?","options":["nineteen ninety-nine","one thousand nine hundred ninety-nine","ten ninety-nine"],"answer":0,"why":"Los años se leen en dos pares: nineteen ninety-nine."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se lee 2026 como año?","options":["twenty twenty-six","two thousand twenty-six","twenty twenty six hundred"],"answer":0,"why":"En inglés americano se dice twenty twenty-six."},{"type":"choice","q":"The ___ floor es el piso 3.","options":["three","third","threeth"],"answer":1,"why":"El ordinal de 3 es third."},{"type":"fill","q":"Escribe 13 en inglés: ___","answer":["thirteen"],"why":"13 es thirteen."},{"type":"fill","q":"Escribe 21 en inglés: ___","answer":["twenty-one","twenty one"],"why":"Las decenas se unen con guion: twenty-one."},{"type":"fill","q":"Escribe 80 en inglés: ___","answer":["eighty"],"why":"80 es eighty."},{"type":"fill","q":"Escribe 1,000 en inglés: one ___","answer":["thousand"],"why":"1,000 es one thousand."},{"type":"fill","q":"El ordinal de 5 es ___","answer":["fifth"],"why":"Fifth cambia la f por th."},{"type":"order","words":["I'm","years","twenty","old"],"answer":"I'm twenty years old","es":"Tengo veinte años."},{"type":"order","words":["is","How","this","much"],"answer":"How much is this","es":"¿Cuánto cuesta esto?"},{"type":"order","words":["phone","your","What's","number"],"answer":"What's your phone number","es":"¿Cuál es tu número de teléfono?"},{"type":"order","words":["dollars","It's","ten"],"answer":"It's ten dollars","es":"Cuesta diez dólares."},{"type":"translate","es":"Tengo veinte años.","answer":["I am twenty years old.","I'm twenty years old.","I am twenty.","I'm twenty."],"why":"La edad se dice con to be más el número."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Cuánto cuesta esto?","answer":["How much is this?","How much does this cost?","How much is it?"],"why":"How much is this? se usa para preguntar el precio."},{"type":"translate","es":"Cuesta cincuenta dólares.","answer":["It's fifty dollars.","It is fifty dollars.","It costs fifty dollars."],"why":"Fifty es 50, y dollars es el plural de dollar."}],"speak":["I'm twenty years old.","How much is this?","It's four ninety-nine.","What's your phone number?","I was born in nineteen ninety-nine.","It's twenty twenty-six.","I live on the third floor.","There are one hundred people here."],"tip":"Error común: decir los años como cantidades, por ejemplo *one thousand nine hundred ninety-nine* para 1999. En inglés se dicen en dos pares: **nineteen ninety-nine**. Y no escribas *fourty* ni *two hundreds*: es **forty** y **two hundred**. Además, el punto y la coma se usan al revés que en Colombia: **1,000** y **4.99**."},{"n":6,"block":"Primeros pasos","title":"Días, meses y fechas","emoji":"📅","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir los días, los meses y las estaciones, y dar una fecha en inglés americano.","sections":[{"h":"Los días de la semana","table":{"head":["Inglés","Español","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["Monday","lunes","I have class on Monday."],["Tuesday","martes","Tuesday is a busy day."],["Wednesday","miércoles","See you on Wednesday."],["Thursday","jueves","Thursday is my day off."],["Friday","viernes","Friday is a good day!"],["Saturday","sábado","We play soccer on Saturday."],["Sunday","domingo","Sunday is family day."]]},"note":"Los días y los meses **siempre se escriben con mayúscula** en inglés: *Monday*, *October*. En español no. Y la semana en Estados Unidos suele empezar el **domingo**."},{"h":"Los meses y las estaciones","table":{"head":["Mes","Español","Mes","Español"],"rows":[["January","enero","July","julio"],["February","febrero","August","agosto"],["March","marzo","September","septiembre"],["April","abril","October","octubre"],["May","mayo","November","noviembre"],["June","junio","December","diciembre"]]},"note":"Las estaciones: **spring** (primavera), **summer** (verano), **fall** o **autumn** (otoño), **winter** (invierno). En Estados Unidos se dice más **fall**."},{"h":"Los ordinales para las fechas","body":"Para decir el día del mes se usan **ordinales**: *primero, segundo, tercero*, etc. En inglés se escriben con número y letras: **1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th**.\n\nLa regla es sencilla: **1st, 2nd, 3rd** son especiales. Del **4th** al **20th** terminan en **-th**. Del **21st** al **31st** vuelves a empezar: 21st, 22nd, 23rd, 24th... 30th, 31st."},{"h":"Ordinales del 1 al 31","table":{"head":["Número","Inglés","Número","Inglés"],"rows":[["1st","first","12th","twelfth"],["2nd","second","13th","thirteenth"],["3rd","third","15th","fifteenth"],["4th","fourth","18th","eighteenth"],["5th","fifth","20th","twentieth"],["8th","eighth","21st","twenty-first"],["9th","ninth","22nd","twenty-second"],["10th","tenth","30th","thirtieth"],["11th","eleventh","31st","thirty-first"]]},"note":"Cuidado con **fifth** (5th), **eighth** (8th), **ninth** (9th, sin e) y **twelfth** (12th, la f)."},{"h":"Cómo se dice una fecha en inglés americano","body":"En Estados Unidos el orden es **mes + día + año**, distinto al nuestro.\n\n**October 18th, 2026** se lee **October eighteenth, twenty twenty-six**.\n\nEn números, **10/18/2026** significa 18 de octubre. Pero **03/04/2026** es **March 4th** (no 3 de abril). Esto confunde mucho a los latinos.\n\nSe pregunta con **What's the date today?** o **What day is it today?** (esa última se contesta con el día de la semana: **It's Sunday.**)\n\nPara contestar: **It's October eighteenth.** (Se dice el ordinal aunque escribas solo *18*.)"},{"h":"Preposiciones in, on, at (resumen)","table":{"head":["Preposición","Se usa con","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["on","días y fechas","on Monday, on October 18th"],["in","meses, años, estaciones","in October, in 2026, in summer"],["in","partes del día","in the morning, in the afternoon"],["at","horas y night","at 5:00, at night"]]},"note":"Error típico: *in Monday* o *on October*. Lo correcto es **on Monday** e **in October**. Si el día está junto al mes, vuelve **on**: **on October 18th**."}],"vocab":[{"en":"Monday","es":"lunes","ex":"I have class on Monday."},{"en":"Tuesday","es":"martes","ex":"Tuesday is busy."},{"en":"Wednesday","es":"miércoles","ex":"See you on Wednesday."},{"en":"Thursday","es":"jueves","ex":"Thursday is my day off."},{"en":"Friday","es":"viernes","ex":"Friday is a good day."},{"en":"Saturday","es":"sábado","ex":"We play soccer on Saturday."},{"en":"Sunday","es":"domingo","ex":"Sunday is family day."},{"en":"month","es":"mes","ex":"October is my favorite month."},{"en":"week","es":"semana","ex":"I study every week."},{"en":"weekend","es":"fin de semana","ex":"Have a nice weekend!"},{"en":"date","es":"fecha","ex":"What's the date today?"},{"en":"today","es":"hoy","ex":"Today is Sunday."},{"en":"tomorrow","es":"mañana","ex":"Tomorrow is Monday."},{"en":"yesterday","es":"ayer","ex":"Yesterday was Saturday."},{"en":"birthday","es":"cumpleaños","ex":"My birthday is in May."},{"en":"spring","es":"primavera","ex":"Spring is beautiful."},{"en":"summer","es":"verano","ex":"Summer is hot in Orlando."},{"en":"fall","es":"otoño","ex":"Fall is my favorite season."},{"en":"winter","es":"invierno","ex":"Winter is cold in New York."}],"examples":[{"en":"Today is Sunday.","es":"Hoy es domingo."},{"en":"Tomorrow is Monday.","es":"Mañana es lunes."},{"en":"What's the date today?","es":"¿Cuál es la fecha de hoy?"},{"en":"It's October eighteenth.","es":"Es 18 de octubre."},{"en":"My birthday is on May fifth.","es":"Mi cumpleaños es el 5 de mayo."},{"en":"I have class on Monday.","es":"Tengo clase el lunes."},{"en":"We go to Orlando in December.","es":"Vamos a Orlando en diciembre."},{"en":"The trip is in 2027.","es":"El viaje es en 2027."},{"en":"Summer is hot in Florida.","es":"El verano es caluroso en Florida."},{"en":"I work on Saturday and Sunday.","es":"Trabajo el sábado y el domingo."},{"en":"The party is on December twenty-fifth.","es":"La fiesta es el 25 de diciembre."},{"en":"I study in the morning.","es":"Estudio en la mañana."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I have class ___ Monday.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":1,"why":"Con días de la semana se usa on."},{"type":"choice","q":"My birthday is ___ May.","options":["on","at","in"],"answer":2,"why":"Con meses se usa in."},{"type":"choice","q":"The party is ___ December 25th.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":1,"why":"Con una fecha completa se usa on."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el ordinal correcto de 3?","options":["3th","3rd","3nd"],"answer":1,"why":"El 3 es third (3rd)."},{"type":"choice","q":"En EE. UU., ¿qué significa normalmente 04/10/2026?","options":["10 de abril","4 de octubre","10 de abril de 2010"],"answer":0,"why":"En EE. UU. el orden es mes/día/año, así que 04/10 es April 10th."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se escribe correctamente en inglés?","options":["monday","Monday","MONday"],"answer":1,"why":"Los días de la semana siempre llevan mayúscula."},{"type":"fill","q":"I work ___ Saturday. (in, on o at)","answer":["on"],"why":"Los días llevan on."},{"type":"fill","q":"We travel ___ summer. (in, on o at)","answer":["in"],"why":"Las estaciones llevan in."},{"type":"fill","q":"El ordinal de 5 es ___","answer":["fifth"],"why":"Fifth cambia la f por th."},{"type":"fill","q":"Después de Sunday viene ___","answer":["monday"],"why":"El día siguiente a domingo es lunes: Monday."},{"type":"fill","q":"El mes antes de November es ___","answer":["october"],"why":"Antes de noviembre está octubre: October."},{"type":"order","words":["is","Today","Sunday"],"answer":"Today is Sunday","es":"Hoy es domingo."},{"type":"order","words":["the","What's","date","today"],"answer":"What's the date today","es":"¿Cuál es la fecha de hoy?"},{"type":"order","words":["birthday","My","is","May","in"],"answer":"My birthday is in May","es":"Mi cumpleaños es en mayo."},{"type":"order","words":["on","I","Monday","work"],"answer":"I work on Monday","es":"Trabajo el lunes."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mañana es lunes.","answer":["Tomorrow is Monday."],"why":"Tomorrow es mañana, y Monday va con mayúscula."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mi cumpleaños es en octubre.","answer":["My birthday is in October."],"why":"Con meses se usa in."},{"type":"translate","es":"Hoy es 18 de octubre.","answer":["Today is October 18th.","Today is October eighteenth.","Today is October 18.","It's October 18th.","It's October eighteenth.","It is October 18th.","It is October eighteenth."],"why":"En inglés americano primero va el mes y luego el día."}],"speak":["Today is Sunday.","Tomorrow is Monday.","What's the date today?","It's October eighteenth.","My birthday is in May.","I have class on Monday.","We go to Orlando in December.","Summer is hot in Florida."],"tip":"Error común: escribir *monday* o *october* en minúscula, y usar mal las preposiciones: *in Monday* u *on October*. Recuerda: **on Monday**, **in October**, **on October 18th**. Y en una fecha como 04/10, en Estados Unidos va primero el mes: es **April 10th**, no el 4 de octubre."},{"n":7,"block":"Primeros pasos","title":"La hora","emoji":"⏰","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás preguntar y decir la hora, usar a.m. y p.m., y hablar de horarios diarios.","sections":[{"h":"Preguntar la hora","body":"Para preguntar la hora hay dos frases muy comunes:\n\n**What time is it?** (*¿Qué hora es?*)\n**Do you have the time?** (*¿Tiene la hora?*, más educado)\n\nPara responder empiezas con **It's** y luego la hora: **It's three o'clock.** Fíjate que se usa **it**, no *they*. En español decimos *son las tres* (plural), en inglés siempre es **It's** (singular)."},{"h":"Las horas exactas y la media hora","table":{"head":["Reloj","Se dice","Significado"],"rows":[["3:00","It's three o'clock.","Son las tres en punto."],["7:00","It's seven o'clock.","Son las siete en punto."],["3:30","It's half past three.","Son las tres y media."],["3:30","It's three thirty.","Son las tres y media (informal)."],["9:30","It's half past nine.","Son las nueve y media."]]},"note":"Hay dos formas de decir la hora: la formal (**half past three**) y la rápida, solo con números (**three thirty**). Las dos son correctas."},{"h":"Cuarto y minutos: past y to","table":{"head":["Reloj","Se dice","Cómo funciona"],"rows":[["3:05","It's five past three.","Pasan 5 minutos de las 3"],["3:10","It's ten past three.","Pasan 10 minutos de las 3"],["3:15","It's a quarter past three.","Quarter = un cuarto de hora"],["3:20","It's twenty past three.","Pasan 20 minutos"],["3:40","It's twenty to four.","Faltan 20 para las 4"],["4:45","It's a quarter to five.","Falta un cuarto para las 5"],["4:50","It's ten to five.","Faltan 10 para las 5"],["4:55","It's five to five.","Faltan 5 para las 5"]]},"note":"Regla fácil: del minuto 1 al 30 usas **past** (después de la hora). Del 31 al 59 usas **to** (faltan para la siguiente hora) y nombras la hora *siguiente*."},{"h":"a.m., p.m., noon y midnight","body":"En Estados Unidos casi no se usa el reloj de 24 horas. Se usa el de 12 horas con **a.m.** o **p.m.**\n\n**a.m.** es de medianoche hasta el mediodía (la mañana). **p.m.** es del mediodía hasta la medianoche (tarde y noche).\n\n**7:00 a.m.** es *las 7 de la mañana*. **7:00 p.m.** es *las 7 de la noche* (19:00).\n\n**Noon** es las 12 del día. **Midnight** es las 12 de la noche. Ejemplo: **The park opens at 9:00 a.m. and closes at midnight.**"},{"h":"What time does it start?","body":"Para preguntar a qué hora empieza algo usamos **What time does ... start?**\n\n**What time does the class start?** (*¿A qué hora empieza la clase?*)\n**What time does the show start?** (*¿A qué hora empieza el show?*)\n\nSe responde con **at** más la hora: **It starts at 8:00 p.m.** (*Empieza a las 8 p. m.*).\n\nPara el final: **What time does it finish?** o **What time does it end?**\n\nOjo: aquí hay un verbo nuevo, **does**. Lo verás con calma más adelante. Por ahora, aprende la frase completa."},{"h":"Mi horario diario","table":{"head":["Hora","Frase","Significa"],"rows":[["6:30 a.m.","I get up at half past six.","Me levanto a las 6:30."],["8:00 a.m.","I have class at eight.","Tengo clase a las 8."],["12:00 p.m.","I have lunch at noon.","Almuerzo al mediodía."],["6:15 p.m.","I finish work at a quarter past six.","Termino a las 6:15."],["11:00 p.m.","I go to bed at eleven.","Me acuesto a las 11."]]},"note":"Error típico: *The class is at the 8*. En inglés no usamos *the* antes de la hora: **at 8**."}],"vocab":[{"en":"time","es":"hora / tiempo","ex":"What time is it?"},{"en":"o'clock","es":"en punto","ex":"It's two o'clock."},{"en":"half past","es":"y media","ex":"It's half past five."},{"en":"quarter past","es":"y cuarto","ex":"It's a quarter past nine."},{"en":"quarter to","es":"menos cuarto","ex":"It's a quarter to ten."},{"en":"past","es":"después de (hora)","ex":"It's ten past one."},{"en":"to","es":"para (falta para)","ex":"It's twenty to six."},{"en":"a.m.","es":"de la mañana","ex":"I wake up at 7 a.m."},{"en":"p.m.","es":"de la tarde/noche","ex":"The show is at 8 p.m."},{"en":"noon","es":"mediodía","ex":"Lunch is at noon."},{"en":"midnight","es":"medianoche","ex":"The park closes at midnight."},{"en":"start","es":"empezar","ex":"What time does the class start?"},{"en":"finish","es":"terminar","ex":"I finish work at six."},{"en":"open","es":"abrir","ex":"The park opens at nine."},{"en":"close","es":"cerrar","ex":"The store closes at ten."},{"en":"get up","es":"levantarse","ex":"I get up at 6:30."},{"en":"have lunch","es":"almorzar","ex":"I have lunch at noon."},{"en":"go to bed","es":"acostarse","ex":"I go to bed at eleven."},{"en":"late","es":"tarde (retrasado)","ex":"I'm late for class."},{"en":"early","es":"temprano","ex":"I'm early today."}],"examples":[{"en":"What time is it?","es":"¿Qué hora es?"},{"en":"It's three o'clock.","es":"Son las tres en punto."},{"en":"It's half past three.","es":"Son las tres y media."},{"en":"It's three fifteen.","es":"Son las tres y quince."},{"en":"It's a quarter to five.","es":"Son las cinco menos cuarto."},{"en":"It's twenty to four.","es":"Son las cuatro menos veinte."},{"en":"What time does the show start?","es":"¿A qué hora empieza el show?"},{"en":"It starts at eight p.m.","es":"Empieza a las ocho de la noche."},{"en":"The park opens at nine a.m.","es":"El parque abre a las nueve de la mañana."},{"en":"I have lunch at noon.","es":"Almuerzo al mediodía."},{"en":"The class finishes at six.","es":"La clase termina a las seis."},{"en":"I go to bed at eleven.","es":"Me acuesto a las once."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice 3:15?","options":["It's a quarter past three.","It's a quarter to three.","It's half past three."],"answer":0,"why":"Past significa después de la hora, y quarter es un cuarto."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice 4:45?","options":["It's a quarter past four.","It's a quarter to five.","It's half past four."],"answer":1,"why":"Faltan 15 minutos para las 5: a quarter to five."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice 3:30?","options":["It's half past three.","It's half to three.","It's three o'clock."],"answer":0,"why":"Y media se dice half past."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se pregunta a qué hora empieza la clase?","options":["What time does the class start?","What hour is the class?","How time is the class?"],"answer":0,"why":"La frase estándar es What time does ... start?"},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se escribe 7:00 de la noche?","options":["7:00 a.m.","7:00 p.m.","7:00 noon"],"answer":1,"why":"Después del mediodía se usa p.m."},{"type":"choice","q":"The park closes at ___. (12 de la noche)","options":["noon","midnight","morning"],"answer":1,"why":"Midnight es la medianoche."},{"type":"fill","q":"It's five ___ two. (2:05)","answer":["past"],"why":"Hasta el minuto 30 se usa past."},{"type":"fill","q":"It's twenty ___ four. (3:40)","answer":["to"],"why":"Del minuto 31 al 59 se usa to."},{"type":"fill","q":"It's seven ___. (7:00 en punto)","answer":["o'clock","oclock"],"why":"En punto se dice o'clock."},{"type":"fill","q":"What ___ is it?","answer":["time"],"why":"La pregunta es What time is it?"},{"type":"fill","q":"The show starts ___ eight p.m.","answer":["at"],"why":"Antes de una hora exacta se usa at."},{"type":"order","words":["time","What","it","is"],"answer":"What time is it","es":"¿Qué hora es?"},{"type":"order","words":["half","past","It's","three"],"answer":"It's half past three","es":"Son las tres y media."},{"type":"order","words":["does","What","show","the","start","time"],"answer":"What time does the show start","es":"¿A qué hora empieza el show?"},{"type":"order","words":["lunch","at","I","noon","have"],"answer":"I have lunch at noon","es":"Almuerzo al mediodía."},{"type":"translate","es":"Son las cuatro en punto.","answer":["It's four o'clock.","It is four o'clock."],"why":"La hora exacta se dice con o'clock."},{"type":"translate","es":"Son las seis y cuarto.","answer":["It's a quarter past six.","It is a quarter past six.","It's quarter past six.","It's six fifteen.","It is six fifteen."],"why":"Y cuarto es a quarter past."},{"type":"translate","es":"Son las ocho menos cuarto.","answer":["It's a quarter to eight.","It is a quarter to eight.","It's quarter to eight.","It's seven forty-five.","It is seven forty-five."],"why":"Menos cuarto es a quarter to, y se nombra la hora siguiente."}],"speak":["What time is it?","It's three o'clock.","It's half past three.","It's a quarter to five.","What time does the show start?","It starts at eight p.m.","I get up at half past six.","The park closes at midnight."],"tip":"Error común: decir *Are the three o'clock* o *They are three o'clock* porque en español la hora es plural (*son las tres*). En inglés siempre es singular: **It's three o'clock**. Tampoco uses *the* antes de la hora: **at 8**, no *at the 8*."},{"n":8,"block":"Primeros pasos","title":"Países y nacionalidades","emoji":"🌎","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir de dónde eres, tu nacionalidad, tu idioma y hablar de países, ciudades y continentes.","sections":[{"h":"País, nacionalidad e idioma","body":"En inglés hay tres palabras que se parecen y que no debes mezclar: el **país** (Colombia), la **nacionalidad** (Colombian) y el **idioma** (Spanish).\n\nPara decir de dónde eres usa **I'm from + país**: **I'm from Colombia.**\nPara decir tu nacionalidad usa **I'm + nacionalidad**: **I'm Colombian.**\nPara el idioma: **I speak Spanish.**\n\nLas nacionalidades y los idiomas **siempre llevan mayúscula** en inglés, aunque en español no: *Colombian*, *Spanish*, *American*."},{"h":"Países y nacionalidades (América)","table":{"head":["País","Nacionalidad","Idioma"],"rows":[["Colombia","Colombian","Spanish"],["the United States","American","English"],["Mexico","Mexican","Spanish"],["Canada","Canadian","English / French"],["Brazil","Brazilian","Portuguese"],["Argentina","Argentine","Spanish"],["Peru","Peruvian","Spanish"],["Venezuela","Venezuelan","Spanish"],["Chile","Chilean","Spanish"],["Ecuador","Ecuadorian","Spanish"],["Cuba","Cuban","Spanish"]]},"note":"Las nacionalidades terminan muchas veces en **-an** o **-ian**. Cuidado con **American** (no *United Statesian*) y **Argentine**."},{"h":"Países y nacionalidades (Europa, Asia y más)","table":{"head":["País","Nacionalidad","Idioma"],"rows":[["Spain","Spanish","Spanish"],["France","French","French"],["Germany","German","German"],["Italy","Italian","Italian"],["Portugal","Portuguese","Portuguese"],["the United Kingdom (the UK)","British","English"],["Ireland","Irish","English / Irish"],["the Netherlands","Dutch","Dutch"],["Russia","Russian","Russian"],["China","Chinese","Chinese"],["Japan","Japanese","Japanese"],["South Korea","Korean","Korean"],["India","Indian","Hindi / English"],["Australia","Australian","English"],["the Philippines","Filipino","Filipino / English"],["Egypt","Egyptian","Arabic"]]},"note":"Las nacionalidades que terminan en **-ese** (Chinese, Japanese) y **-ch / -sh** (French, Spanish) no cambian en plural: **two Japanese**, **three Spanish**."},{"h":"¿Cuándo se usa the con los países?","body":"La mayoría de países **no llevan the**: **Colombia, Mexico, France, Japan**. Lo correcto es **I'm from Colombia**, no *I'm from the Colombia*.\n\nPero algunos sí llevan **the**:\n- Países con **United**, **Republic** o **Kingdom** en el nombre: **the United States** (the USA), **the United Kingdom** (the UK), **the Dominican Republic**.\n- Países en plural: **the Netherlands**, **the Philippines**.\n\nPor eso: **I'm from the USA.** pero **I'm from Canada.**"},{"h":"Preguntar y responder","table":{"head":["Pregunta","Respuesta","Significa"],"rows":[["Where are you from?","I'm from Colombia.","¿De dónde eres? Soy de Colombia."],["Where is he from?","He's from Medellín.","¿De dónde es él? Es de Medellín."],["What's your nationality?","I'm Colombian.","¿Cuál es tu nacionalidad? Soy colombiano."],["What languages do you speak?","I speak Spanish and English.","¿Qué idiomas hablas? Hablo español e inglés."],["Are you American?","No, I'm Colombian.","¿Eres estadounidense? No, soy colombiano."]]},"note":"Usa **from** con el país o la ciudad, pero **no** con la nacionalidad. Es **I'm from Colombia** o **I'm Colombian**, nunca *I'm from Colombian*."},{"h":"Ciudades y continentes","table":{"head":["Ciudad / continente","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["Bogotá, Medellín, Cali","I'm from Medellín, Colombia.","Soy de Medellín, Colombia."],["Orlando, Miami, New York","Orlando is in Florida.","Orlando está en Florida."],["South America","Colombia is in South America.","Colombia está en Sudamérica."],["North America","Canada is in North America.","Canadá está en Norteamérica."],["Europe","Spain is in Europe.","España está en Europa."],["Asia, Africa, Oceania","Japan is in Asia.","Japón está en Asia."]]},"note":"Para ubicar algo usa **in**: **Orlando is in Florida. Florida is in the United States.**"}],"vocab":[{"en":"country","es":"país","ex":"Colombia is my country."},{"en":"nationality","es":"nacionalidad","ex":"What's your nationality?"},{"en":"language","es":"idioma","ex":"Spanish is my language."},{"en":"city","es":"ciudad","ex":"Orlando is a big city."},{"en":"continent","es":"continente","ex":"South America is a continent."},{"en":"Colombian","es":"colombiano/a","ex":"I'm Colombian."},{"en":"American","es":"estadounidense","ex":"She's American."},{"en":"Mexican","es":"mexicano/a","ex":"He's Mexican."},{"en":"Brazilian","es":"brasileño/a","ex":"They're Brazilian."},{"en":"British","es":"británico/a","ex":"My teacher is British."},{"en":"French","es":"francés/a","ex":"She's French."},{"en":"German","es":"alemán/a","ex":"He's German."},{"en":"Japanese","es":"japonés/a","ex":"Our guest is Japanese."},{"en":"Chinese","es":"chino/a","ex":"My friend is Chinese."},{"en":"Spanish","es":"español/a (idioma)","ex":"I speak Spanish."},{"en":"English","es":"inglés (idioma)","ex":"I'm learning English."},{"en":"speak","es":"hablar","ex":"I speak two languages."},{"en":"from","es":"de (origen)","ex":"I'm from Medellín."},{"en":"Europe","es":"Europa","ex":"France is in Europe."},{"en":"Asia","es":"Asia","ex":"Japan is in Asia."}],"examples":[{"en":"Where are you from?","es":"¿De dónde eres?"},{"en":"I'm from Colombia.","es":"Soy de Colombia."},{"en":"I'm Colombian.","es":"Soy colombiano."},{"en":"I'm from Medellín, Colombia.","es":"Soy de Medellín, Colombia."},{"en":"She's from the United States.","es":"Ella es de Estados Unidos."},{"en":"He's American.","es":"Él es estadounidense."},{"en":"My friends are Mexican.","es":"Mis amigos son mexicanos."},{"en":"I speak Spanish and English.","es":"Hablo español e inglés."},{"en":"Orlando is in Florida.","es":"Orlando está en Florida."},{"en":"Colombia is in South America.","es":"Colombia está en Sudamérica."},{"en":"We are from the UK.","es":"Somos del Reino Unido."},{"en":"Are you Brazilian? No, I'm not.","es":"¿Eres brasileño? No, no lo soy."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I'm ___ Colombia.","options":["from","in","of"],"answer":0,"why":"Para el origen se usa from."},{"type":"choice","q":"I'm from ___ United States.","options":["the","a","an"],"answer":0,"why":"United States lleva the."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es la nacionalidad de una persona de Japón?","options":["Japanese","Japaner","Japanian"],"answer":0,"why":"La nacionalidad de Japan es Japanese."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es correcta?","options":["I'm from the Colombia.","I'm from Colombia.","I'm from Colombian."],"answer":1,"why":"Colombia no lleva the, y from va con el país."},{"type":"choice","q":"Paris is in ___.","options":["Europe","Asia","South America"],"answer":0,"why":"París está en Francia, en Europa."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["I speak colombian.","I speak Spanish.","I speak spanish."],"answer":1,"why":"Spanish es el idioma y siempre lleva mayúscula."},{"type":"fill","q":"Where ___ you from?","answer":["are"],"why":"Con you se usa are."},{"type":"fill","q":"I'm from Colombia. I'm ___. (nacionalidad)","answer":["colombian"],"why":"La nacionalidad de Colombia es Colombian."},{"type":"fill","q":"She is from the USA. She is ___. (nacionalidad)","answer":["american"],"why":"La nacionalidad de USA es American."},{"type":"fill","q":"I'm from Mexico. I'm ___. (nacionalidad)","answer":["mexican"],"why":"La nacionalidad de Mexico es Mexican."},{"type":"fill","q":"Orlando is ___ Florida. (in, on o at)","answer":["in"],"why":"Para ubicar una ciudad se usa in."},{"type":"fill","q":"They are from Germany. They are ___. (nacionalidad)","answer":["german"],"why":"La nacionalidad de Germany es German."},{"type":"order","words":["from","I'm","Colombia"],"answer":"I'm from Colombia","es":"Soy de Colombia."},{"type":"order","words":["Where","from","are","you"],"answer":"Where are you from","es":"¿De dónde eres?"},{"type":"order","words":["speak","I","and","Spanish","English"],"answer":"I speak Spanish and English","es":"Hablo español e inglés."},{"type":"order","words":["is","in","Orlando","Florida"],"answer":"Orlando is in Florida","es":"Orlando está en Florida."},{"type":"translate","es":"Soy colombiano.","answer":["I am Colombian.","I'm Colombian."],"why":"La nacionalidad se dice con to be y va con mayúscula."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella es de Estados Unidos.","answer":["She is from the United States.","She's from the United States.","She is from the USA.","She's from the USA.","She is from the US.","She's from the US."],"why":"Estados Unidos lleva the en inglés."},{"type":"translate","es":"Hablo español e inglés.","answer":["I speak Spanish and English."],"why":"Los idiomas llevan mayúscula y el verbo es speak."}],"speak":["Where are you from?","I'm from Colombia.","I'm Colombian.","I'm from Medellín, Colombia.","I speak Spanish and English.","She's from the United States.","Orlando is in Florida.","Colombia is in South America."],"tip":"Error común: decir *I'm from Colombian* o *I'm from the Colombia*, o escribir *colombian* y *spanish* en minúscula. En inglés: **I'm from Colombia** (país, sin the) o **I'm Colombian** (nacionalidad), y las nacionalidades e idiomas siempre llevan **mayúscula**. Solo algunos países llevan **the**: **the United States**, **the UK**, **the Netherlands**."},{"n":9,"block":"Mi mundo","title":"La casa: there is / there are","emoji":"🏠","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás describir tu casa, sus cuartos y lo que hay dentro usando there is y there are.","sections":[{"h":"Los cuartos de la casa","body":"Empecemos por lo básico: ¿dónde vives y cómo es tu casa?\n\nPara decir dónde vives usa **I live in a house** (una casa) o **I live in an apartment** (un apartamento). Si es tu ciudad, usa **in**: **I live in Medellín**.\n\nLos cuartos principales son: **living room** (sala), **bedroom** (habitación), **kitchen** (cocina), **bathroom** (baño), **dining room** (comedor), **garage** (garaje) y **garden** (jardín).","note":"En inglés americano también se dice **restroom** para el baño público y **bathroom** para el de la casa. En Orlando vas a escuchar ambas."},{"h":"Muebles y objetos","table":{"head":["Inglés","Español","Dónde suele estar"],"rows":[["sofa","sofá","living room"],["bed","cama","bedroom"],["fridge","nevera / refrigerador","kitchen"],["table","mesa","dining room"],["lamp","lámpara","bedroom / living room"],["window","ventana","en casi todos los cuartos"],["door","puerta","en todos los cuartos"],["shower","ducha","bathroom"]]},"note":"Fíjate: en inglés los objetos casi siempre llevan **a** o **an** delante: a bed, a lamp, an armchair."},{"h":"There is / There are: lo que hay","body":"En español usamos **hay** para una cosa o para muchas. En inglés tienes dos opciones:\n\n**There is** para una sola cosa (singular).\n**There are** para dos o más cosas (plural).\n\nLa forma corta de there is es **there's**. There are no tiene forma corta común.","table":{"head":["Forma","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["There is + a/an + singular","There is a sofa in the living room.","Hay un sofá en la sala."],["There are + plural","There are two beds in the bedroom.","Hay dos camas en la habitación."],["There are + some + plural","There are some books on the table.","Hay unos libros en la mesa."]]}},{"h":"Negativo y preguntas","table":{"head":["Tipo","Singular","Plural"],"rows":[["Afirmativo","There is a lamp.","There are two lamps."],["Negativo","There isn't a lamp.","There aren't any lamps."],["Pregunta","Is there a lamp?","Are there any lamps?"],["Respuesta corta","Yes, there is. / No, there isn't.","Yes, there are. / No, there aren't."]]},"note":"En negativo y preguntas con plural usamos **any** en lugar de some: There aren't **any** chairs. Are there **any** chairs?"},{"h":"Errores típicos de hispanohablantes","list":["No digas *Has a sofa*. Para 'hay' se usa **There is a sofa**, no el verbo have.","No mezcles singular y plural: *There is two beds* está mal. Correcto: **There are two beds**.","No olvides el there: *Is a fridge in the kitchen?* está mal. Correcto: **Is there a fridge in the kitchen?**","Con 'a house' dices **in a house**, no *on a house*."]}],"vocab":[{"en":"house","es":"casa","ex":"I live in a big house."},{"en":"apartment","es":"apartamento","ex":"My apartment is small."},{"en":"living room","es":"sala","ex":"The TV is in the living room."},{"en":"bedroom","es":"habitación","ex":"My bedroom is quiet."},{"en":"kitchen","es":"cocina","ex":"There is a fridge in the kitchen."},{"en":"bathroom","es":"baño","ex":"The bathroom is next to my room."},{"en":"dining room","es":"comedor","ex":"We eat in the dining room."},{"en":"garden","es":"jardín","ex":"There is a tree in the garden."},{"en":"sofa","es":"sofá","ex":"The sofa is very comfortable."},{"en":"bed","es":"cama","ex":"I have a small bed."},{"en":"fridge","es":"nevera","ex":"There is milk in the fridge."},{"en":"lamp","es":"lámpara","ex":"The lamp is on the desk."},{"en":"window","es":"ventana","ex":"Open the window, please."},{"en":"door","es":"puerta","ex":"Close the door, please."},{"en":"table","es":"mesa","ex":"There are four chairs at the table."},{"en":"chair","es":"silla","ex":"This chair is new."},{"en":"desk","es":"escritorio","ex":"My computer is on the desk."},{"en":"shower","es":"ducha","ex":"There is a shower in the bathroom."}],"examples":[{"en":"I live in an apartment in Bogotá.","es":"Vivo en un apartamento en Bogotá."},{"en":"There is a sofa in the living room.","es":"Hay un sofá en la sala."},{"en":"There are two windows in my bedroom.","es":"Hay dos ventanas en mi habitación."},{"en":"There's a big fridge in the kitchen.","es":"Hay una nevera grande en la cocina."},{"en":"There isn't a garden.","es":"No hay jardín."},{"en":"There aren't any chairs here.","es":"No hay sillas aquí."},{"en":"Is there a bathroom on this floor?","es":"¿Hay un baño en este piso?"},{"en":"Are there any lamps in your room?","es":"¿Hay lámparas en tu cuarto?"},{"en":"Yes, there is.","es":"Sí, hay."},{"en":"No, there aren't.","es":"No, no hay."},{"en":"My house has three bedrooms.","es":"Mi casa tiene tres habitaciones."},{"en":"There is a computer on my desk.","es":"Hay un computador en mi escritorio."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"There ___ a lamp in my bedroom.","options":["is","are","have"],"answer":0,"why":"Una sola lámpara es singular: there is."},{"type":"choice","q":"There ___ three chairs in the kitchen.","options":["is","are","has"],"answer":1,"why":"Tres sillas es plural: there are."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice 'sala' en inglés?","options":["bedroom","living room","bathroom"],"answer":1,"why":"Living room es la sala; bedroom es habitación y bathroom es baño."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ there a garden?","options":["Is","Are","Does"],"answer":0,"why":"Garden es singular, así que la pregunta empieza con Is there."},{"type":"choice","q":"There aren't ___ chairs.","options":["a","any","an"],"answer":1,"why":"En negativo con plural se usa any."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which room has a bed?","options":["kitchen","bedroom","garage"],"answer":1,"why":"La cama (bed) está en la habitación (bedroom)."},{"type":"fill","q":"There ___ a fridge in the kitchen.","answer":["is"],"why":"Fridge es singular: there is."},{"type":"fill","q":"There ___ two windows in the living room.","answer":["are"],"why":"Two windows es plural: there are."},{"type":"fill","q":"I live ___ an apartment.","answer":["in"],"why":"Para vivir en un lugar usamos in."},{"type":"fill","q":"There ___ any lamps here. (negativo, forma corta)","answer":["aren't","are not"],"why":"Negativo plural: there aren't (o there are not)."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ there a bathroom? Yes, there is.","answer":["is"],"why":"Pregunta con singular: Is there...?"},{"type":"order","words":["in","There","sofa","a","is","the","living","room"],"answer":"There is a sofa in the living room","es":"Hay un sofá en la sala."},{"type":"order","words":["there","Are","any","chairs","here"],"answer":"Are there any chairs here","es":"¿Hay sillas aquí?"},{"type":"order","words":["live","I","in","a","house"],"answer":"I live in a house","es":"Vivo en una casa."},{"type":"translate","es":"Hay una cama en mi habitación.","answer":["There is a bed in my bedroom.","There's a bed in my bedroom.","There is a bed in my room.","There's a bed in my room."],"why":"Hay + singular = there is."},{"type":"translate","es":"No hay ventanas en el baño.","answer":["There aren't any windows in the bathroom.","There are not any windows in the bathroom."],"why":"Negativo plural: there aren't any."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Hay una nevera en la cocina?","answer":["Is there a fridge in the kitchen?"],"why":"Pregunta singular: Is there a...?"}],"speak":["I live in an apartment.","There is a bed in my bedroom.","There are two chairs at my desk.","There's a big window in the living room.","There isn't a garden.","Is there a bathroom here?"],"tip":"Los hispanohablantes dicen *Has a sofa* porque piensan en 'hay'. Recuerda: 'hay' siempre es **there is** (una cosa) o **there are** (varias), nunca el verbo have."},{"n":10,"block":"Mi mundo","title":"Preposiciones de lugar y this / that","emoji":"📍","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir dónde están las cosas y señalar objetos cercanos y lejanos con this, that, these y those.","sections":[{"h":"¿Dónde está? Where is / Where are","body":"Para preguntar por un lugar usa **Where is...?** con una cosa y **Where are...?** con varias.\n\n**Where is the key?** ¿Dónde está la llave?\n**Where are my shoes?** ¿Dónde están mis zapatos?\n\nPara responder usas una preposición de lugar: **It's on the table.** / **They're under the bed.**"},{"h":"Las preposiciones de lugar","table":{"head":["Preposición","Significa","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["in","dentro de / en","The phone is in the bag."],["on","sobre / encima (tocando)","The book is on the desk."],["under","debajo de","The cat is under the chair."],["next to","al lado de","The lamp is next to the bed."],["between","entre (dos cosas)","The bank is between the bakery and the cafe."],["in front of","enfrente de / delante de","The car is in front of the house."],["behind","detrás de","The garden is behind the house."],["near","cerca de","My school is near my house."],["at","en (un punto o lugar)","I am at work. / She is at home."]]},"note":"Ojo: en español 'en' sirve para todo. En inglés eliges: **in** (dentro), **on** (encima), **at** (un punto o lugar de actividad)."},{"h":"This, that, these, those","body":"Sirven para señalar. Dependen de dos cosas: si es una o varias, y si está cerca o lejos de ti.","table":{"head":["","Cerca de ti","Lejos de ti"],"rows":[["Singular (una cosa)","this = este / esta","that = ese / aquel"],["Plural (varias)","these = estos / estas","those = esos / aquellos"]]},"note":"Ejemplos: **This** is my phone (lo tengo en la mano). **That** is the castle (está lejos). **These** are my keys. **Those** are your friends."},{"h":"Describir un cuarto","body":"Ahora combinamos todo. Mira este pequeño texto:\n\n**This is my room. There is a bed next to the window. There is a desk in front of the bed. My laptop is on the desk and my bag is under the desk. Those are my books on the shelf.**\n\nPrimero dices qué es el lugar, luego usas **there is / there are** y las preposiciones para ubicar cada cosa."},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["No digas *in the table* para algo encima de la mesa. Es **on the table**.","No uses *this* para varias cosas: *this are my keys* está mal. Correcto: **these are my keys**.","*Next of* no existe. Siempre es **next to**.","Con *where* y un plural usa are: **Where are my keys?**, no *Where is my keys?*"]}],"vocab":[{"en":"in","es":"en / dentro de","ex":"The milk is in the fridge."},{"en":"on","es":"sobre / encima de","ex":"My laptop is on the desk."},{"en":"under","es":"debajo de","ex":"The shoes are under the bed."},{"en":"next to","es":"al lado de","ex":"The bank is next to the hotel."},{"en":"between","es":"entre","ex":"I sit between Ana and Luis."},{"en":"in front of","es":"enfrente de","ex":"The bus stop is in front of the park."},{"en":"behind","es":"detrás de","ex":"The ball is behind the door."},{"en":"near","es":"cerca de","ex":"I live near the university."},{"en":"at","es":"en (lugar)","ex":"I am at the airport."},{"en":"far from","es":"lejos de","ex":"Orlando is far from Bogotá."},{"en":"where","es":"dónde","ex":"Where is the bathroom?"},{"en":"this","es":"este / esta","ex":"This is my bag."},{"en":"that","es":"ese / aquel","ex":"That is my teacher."},{"en":"these","es":"estos / estas","ex":"These are my keys."},{"en":"those","es":"esos / aquellos","ex":"Those are big windows."},{"en":"shelf","es":"estante","ex":"The books are on the shelf."},{"en":"keys","es":"llaves","ex":"Where are my keys?"},{"en":"bag","es":"bolso / mochila","ex":"My phone is in my bag."}],"examples":[{"en":"Where is my phone?","es":"¿Dónde está mi teléfono?"},{"en":"It's on the table.","es":"Está sobre la mesa."},{"en":"Where are my keys?","es":"¿Dónde están mis llaves?"},{"en":"They're under the sofa.","es":"Están debajo del sofá."},{"en":"The lamp is next to the bed.","es":"La lámpara está al lado de la cama."},{"en":"The bank is between the cafe and the school.","es":"El banco está entre la cafetería y la escuela."},{"en":"My car is in front of the house.","es":"Mi carro está enfrente de la casa."},{"en":"The garden is behind the house.","es":"El jardín está detrás de la casa."},{"en":"I'm at work.","es":"Estoy en el trabajo."},{"en":"This is my laptop.","es":"Este es mi portátil."},{"en":"That is Cinderella Castle.","es":"Ese es el Castillo de Cenicienta."},{"en":"Those are my friends over there.","es":"Esos son mis amigos allá."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"The book is ___ the table. (encima)","options":["in","on","under"],"answer":1,"why":"Encima de una superficie se dice on."},{"type":"choice","q":"The cat is ___ the chair. (debajo)","options":["under","behind","between"],"answer":0,"why":"Debajo de se dice under."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ are my shoes? They're under the bed.","options":["Where","What","Who"],"answer":0,"why":"Para preguntar el lugar usamos Where."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ is my book. (lo tengo en la mano)","options":["That","This","Those"],"answer":1,"why":"Singular y cerca de ti: this."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ are my friends over there. (lejos, varios)","options":["These","This","Those"],"answer":2,"why":"Plural y lejos: those."},{"type":"choice","q":"The bank is ___ the cafe and the hotel. (entre los dos)","options":["between","behind","at"],"answer":0,"why":"Entre dos cosas se dice between."},{"type":"choice","q":"I live ___ the university. (cerca)","options":["far","near","under"],"answer":1,"why":"Cerca de se dice near."},{"type":"fill","q":"The phone is ___ my bag. (dentro)","answer":["in"],"why":"Dentro de un bolso: in."},{"type":"fill","q":"Where ___ my keys?","answer":["are"],"why":"Keys es plural: where are."},{"type":"fill","q":"The lamp is ___ to the bed. (al lado)","answer":["next"],"why":"Al lado de se dice next to."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ are my keys. (cerca, varios)","answer":["these"],"why":"Plural y cerca: these."},{"type":"fill","q":"I am ___ home now.","answer":["at"],"why":"Con home se usa at: at home."},{"type":"order","words":["is","Where","the","bathroom"],"answer":"Where is the bathroom","es":"¿Dónde está el baño?"},{"type":"order","words":["under","bag","is","My","the","desk"],"answer":"My bag is under the desk","es":"Mi mochila está debajo del escritorio."},{"type":"order","words":["my","is","This","room"],"answer":"This is my room","es":"Esta es mi habitación."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mi teléfono está sobre la mesa.","answer":["My phone is on the table.","My phone's on the table."],"why":"Encima de la mesa: on the table."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Dónde están mis llaves?","answer":["Where are my keys?"],"why":"Llaves es plural: where are."},{"type":"translate","es":"Esos son mis amigos.","answer":["Those are my friends.","Those are my friends"],"why":"Plural y lejos: those are."}],"speak":["Where is my phone?","My bag is under the desk.","The lamp is next to the bed.","This is my room.","Those are my friends.","I live near the university."],"tip":"En español decimos 'en' para todo. En inglés: **in** si algo está dentro, **on** si está encima y **at** si es un lugar o punto. Un error muy común es decir *The book is in the table*; lo correcto es **on the table**."},{"n":11,"block":"Mi mundo","title":"La familia y las personas","emoji":"👨‍👩‍👧","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás hablar de tu familia, decir cuántos años tienen y describir a las personas con my, your, his, her y 's.","sections":[{"h":"Los miembros de la familia","body":"La familia es uno de los temas más comunes en una conversación. Mira las palabras clave:","table":{"head":["Hombre","Mujer","Significa"],"rows":[["father (dad)","mother (mom)","padre / madre"],["brother","sister","hermano / hermana"],["son","daughter","hijo / hija"],["grandfather (grandpa)","grandmother (grandma)","abuelo / abuela"],["uncle","aunt","tío / tía"],["cousin","cousin","primo / prima"],["husband","wife","esposo / esposa"]]},"note":"**Parents** son los padres (papá y mamá), no los 'parientes'. Parientes en general se dice **relatives**."},{"h":"Adjetivos posesivos","body":"Dicen de quién es algo. Siempre van **antes del sustantivo** y no cambian con singular o plural.","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Posesivo","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["I","my","my mother"],["you","your","your brother"],["he","his","his sister"],["she","her","her father"],["we","our","our house"],["they","their","their parents"]]},"note":"En inglés el posesivo depende de **quién posee**, no de lo que se posee. **His mother** = la madre de él. **Her brothers** = los hermanos de ella."},{"h":"El posesivo 's","body":"Para decir 'el hermano de Ana' no existe 'de'. Se pone un **'s** al final del nombre del dueño:\n\n**Ana's brother** = el hermano de Ana.\n**My father's car** = el carro de mi padre.\n\nOjo: **Ana's** puede ser posesivo o la forma corta de **Ana is**. El contexto te dice cuál es."},{"h":"Have / has: tener familia","body":"Para decir cuántos hermanos, hijos o primos tienes, usa **have** (I, you, we, they) y **has** (he, she, it).\n\n**I have two brothers.** Tengo dos hermanos.\n**She has one sister.** Ella tiene una hermana.\n**I don't have any sisters.** No tengo hermanas.\n**Does he have a brother?** ¿Tiene él un hermano?"},{"h":"Edad y descripción","body":"La edad se dice con **to be**: **I am 20 years old.** (no *I have 20 years*).\n\nPregunta: **How old are you?** Respuesta corta: **I'm 20.**\n\nPara describir a una persona usa **to be** + adjetivo: **My mom is kind.** **My brother is tall.** O **has** + parte del cuerpo: **She has long hair.**"}],"vocab":[{"en":"family","es":"familia","ex":"I love my family."},{"en":"parents","es":"padres","ex":"My parents live in Cali."},{"en":"mother","es":"madre","ex":"My mother is a nurse."},{"en":"father","es":"padre","ex":"My father works in a bank."},{"en":"brother","es":"hermano","ex":"I have one brother."},{"en":"sister","es":"hermana","ex":"Her sister is 15."},{"en":"son","es":"hijo","ex":"They have a son."},{"en":"daughter","es":"hija","ex":"Their daughter is five."},{"en":"grandmother","es":"abuela","ex":"My grandmother makes great food."},{"en":"grandfather","es":"abuelo","ex":"My grandfather is 70 years old."},{"en":"uncle","es":"tío","ex":"My uncle lives in Orlando."},{"en":"aunt","es":"tía","ex":"My aunt is very funny."},{"en":"cousin","es":"primo / prima","ex":"My cousin is my best friend."},{"en":"husband","es":"esposo","ex":"Her husband is a teacher."},{"en":"wife","es":"esposa","ex":"His wife is from Peru."},{"en":"years old","es":"años de edad","ex":"I'm 20 years old."},{"en":"kind","es":"amable","ex":"My mom is very kind."},{"en":"funny","es":"divertido","ex":"My uncle is funny."}],"examples":[{"en":"This is my family.","es":"Esta es mi familia."},{"en":"I have two brothers and one sister.","es":"Tengo dos hermanos y una hermana."},{"en":"She has a big family.","es":"Ella tiene una familia grande."},{"en":"His mother is a doctor.","es":"Su madre (de él) es doctora."},{"en":"Her father is a driver.","es":"Su padre (de ella) es conductor."},{"en":"Our house is small.","es":"Nuestra casa es pequeña."},{"en":"Their parents are from Mexico.","es":"Sus padres son de México."},{"en":"Ana's brother is 18.","es":"El hermano de Ana tiene 18 años."},{"en":"How old is your sister?","es":"¿Cuántos años tiene tu hermana?"},{"en":"She is 12 years old.","es":"Ella tiene 12 años."},{"en":"I don't have any cousins here.","es":"No tengo primos aquí."},{"en":"My grandfather is tall and kind.","es":"Mi abuelo es alto y amable."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ two brothers.","options":["has","have","am"],"answer":1,"why":"Con I se usa have."},{"type":"choice","q":"She ___ one sister.","options":["have","has","is"],"answer":1,"why":"Con she se usa has."},{"type":"choice","q":"This is Ana. ___ brother is Pablo.","options":["Her","His","Their"],"answer":0,"why":"Ana es mujer: her brother."},{"type":"choice","q":"Pablo has a car. ___ car is red.","options":["Her","His","Our"],"answer":1,"why":"Pablo es hombre: his car."},{"type":"choice","q":"How old ___ you?","options":["is","have","are"],"answer":2,"why":"La edad se pregunta con to be: How old are you?"},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cómo se dice 'tía'?","options":["uncle","aunt","cousin"],"answer":1,"why":"Aunt es tía; uncle es tío."},{"type":"choice","q":"They love ___ children.","options":["her","their","our"],"answer":1,"why":"Para they el posesivo es their."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ 20 years old. (to be)","answer":["am","'m","i'm"],"why":"La edad usa to be: I am 20."},{"type":"fill","q":"He ___ two sisters. (have)","answer":["has"],"why":"Con he se usa has."},{"type":"fill","q":"This is Ana___ brother.","answer":["'s","’s"],"why":"El posesivo se forma con 's: Ana's brother."},{"type":"fill","q":"We love ___ grandmother. (nosotros)","answer":["our"],"why":"El posesivo de we es our."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ have any sisters.","answer":["don't","do not"],"why":"Negativo con I: don't have."},{"type":"order","words":["have","I","brothers","two"],"answer":"I have two brothers","es":"Tengo dos hermanos."},{"type":"order","words":["is","mother","My","a","nurse"],"answer":"My mother is a nurse","es":"Mi madre es enfermera."},{"type":"order","words":["old","How","is","your","father"],"answer":"How old is your father","es":"¿Cuántos años tiene tu padre?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Tengo 20 años.","answer":["I am 20 years old.","I'm 20 years old.","I am 20.","I'm 20."],"why":"La edad se dice con to be, no con have."},{"type":"translate","es":"El hermano de Ana tiene 18 años.","answer":["Ana's brother is 18.","Ana's brother is 18 years old."],"why":"El dueño con 's y la edad con is."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella tiene una hermana.","answer":["She has one sister.","She has a sister."],"why":"Con she se usa has."}],"speak":["This is my family.","I have two brothers and one sister.","My mother is a nurse.","My father's name is Carlos.","My sister is 15 years old.","I'm 20 years old."],"tip":"Un error clásico: *I have 20 years*. En inglés la edad se dice con to be: **I am 20**. Otro: *the brother of Ana*. Lo natural es **Ana's brother**."},{"n":12,"block":"Mi mundo","title":"Adjetivos, colores y descripciones","emoji":"🎨","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás describir personas, cosas y lugares usando colores, adjetivos opuestos y palabras como very y really.","sections":[{"h":"Los colores","table":{"head":["Color","Español","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["red","rojo","a red bus"],["blue","azul","a blue shirt"],["green","verde","a green tree"],["yellow","amarillo","a yellow taxi"],["black","negro","a black phone"],["white","blanco","a white house"],["orange","naranja","an orange ball"],["pink","rosado","a pink bag"],["brown","café / marrón","a brown dog"],["gray","gris","a gray car"]]},"note":"Para preguntar: **What color is it?** Respuesta: **It's red.**"},{"h":"Opuestos comunes","body":"Aprender los adjetivos en pares es mucho más fácil:","table":{"head":["Adjetivo","Opuesto","Significa"],"rows":[["big","small","grande / pequeño"],["new","old","nuevo / viejo"],["cheap","expensive","barato / caro"],["tall","short","alto / bajo"],["hot","cold","caliente / frío"],["good","bad","bueno / malo"],["fast","slow","rápido / lento"],["easy","difficult","fácil / difícil"]]}},{"h":"Dónde va el adjetivo","body":"En español el adjetivo va después: *un carro rojo*. En inglés va **antes del sustantivo**: **a red car**.\n\nAdemás, el adjetivo **nunca cambia a plural**. No existe el -s ni el género:\n\n**a red car** → **two red cars** (no *reds cars*)\n**a tall man** → **tall women** (no *talls*)\n\nSi usas a/an, mira la primera letra del adjetivo: **an old house**, **a new house**."},{"h":"To be + adjetivo","body":"También puedes poner el adjetivo después de **to be**, sin sustantivo:\n\n**The car is red.** El carro es rojo.\n**My phone is new.** Mi teléfono es nuevo.\n**They are tall.** Ellos son altos.\n\nPara describir a una persona: **My brother is tall and funny.** Y para el pelo o los ojos usa have: **She has long black hair.** **He has brown eyes.**"},{"h":"Very, really, a bit","body":"Estas palabras cambian la fuerza del adjetivo y van **antes** de él:","table":{"head":["Palabra","Fuerza","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["a bit","poco","The room is a bit small."],["very","mucho","The park is very big."],["really","muchísimo","The ride is really fast!"]]},"note":"No digas *very much big*. En inglés es simplemente **very big**."}],"vocab":[{"en":"red","es":"rojo","ex":"The red bus is here."},{"en":"blue","es":"azul","ex":"My shirt is blue."},{"en":"green","es":"verde","ex":"The grass is green."},{"en":"yellow","es":"amarillo","ex":"A yellow taxi is outside."},{"en":"black","es":"negro","ex":"I have a black backpack."},{"en":"white","es":"blanco","ex":"The castle is white."},{"en":"big","es":"grande","ex":"Orlando is a big city."},{"en":"small","es":"pequeño","ex":"My room is small."},{"en":"new","es":"nuevo","ex":"I have a new laptop."},{"en":"old","es":"viejo","ex":"That is an old car."},{"en":"cheap","es":"barato","ex":"This shirt is cheap."},{"en":"expensive","es":"caro","ex":"The tickets are expensive."},{"en":"tall","es":"alto","ex":"My brother is tall."},{"en":"short","es":"bajo / corto","ex":"She has short hair."},{"en":"fast","es":"rápido","ex":"That roller coaster is fast."},{"en":"slow","es":"lento","ex":"The bus is slow today."},{"en":"beautiful","es":"hermoso","ex":"The park is beautiful."},{"en":"very","es":"muy","ex":"It is very hot."},{"en":"really","es":"realmente / muy","ex":"I am really happy."},{"en":"a bit","es":"un poco","ex":"The coffee is a bit cold."}],"examples":[{"en":"I have a red backpack.","es":"Tengo una mochila roja."},{"en":"She has a new phone.","es":"Ella tiene un teléfono nuevo."},{"en":"It's an old house.","es":"Es una casa vieja."},{"en":"These are cheap shoes.","es":"Estos son zapatos baratos."},{"en":"The tickets are expensive.","es":"Los boletos son caros."},{"en":"My brother is tall and funny.","es":"Mi hermano es alto y gracioso."},{"en":"He has short black hair.","es":"Él tiene el pelo corto y negro."},{"en":"The room is a bit small.","es":"El cuarto es un poco pequeño."},{"en":"The park is very big.","es":"El parque es muy grande."},{"en":"The ride is really fast!","es":"¡La atracción es rapidísima!"},{"en":"What color is your bag?","es":"¿De qué color es tu bolso?"},{"en":"It's a beautiful day.","es":"Es un día hermoso."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I have a ___ car.","options":["car red","red","reds"],"answer":1,"why":"El adjetivo va antes del sustantivo y no lleva -s."},{"type":"choice","q":"What is the opposite of 'big'?","options":["small","old","cheap"],"answer":0,"why":"El opuesto de big es small."},{"type":"choice","q":"They are two ___ dogs.","options":["blacks","black","blacken"],"answer":1,"why":"Los adjetivos no cambian en plural: two black dogs."},{"type":"choice","q":"It is ___ old house.","options":["a","an","the one"],"answer":1,"why":"Old empieza con vocal, por eso an."},{"type":"choice","q":"The pool is ___ big. (muchísimo)","options":["really","a bit","much"],"answer":0,"why":"Really es la forma fuerte, antes del adjetivo."},{"type":"choice","q":"What color is the sky on a sunny day?","options":["blue","black","brown"],"answer":0,"why":"Un cielo soleado es azul: blue."},{"type":"fill","q":"The tickets are very ___. (caro)","answer":["expensive"],"why":"Caro en inglés es expensive."},{"type":"fill","q":"My phone is ___. (nuevo)","answer":["new"],"why":"Nuevo se dice new."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ long black hair. (have)","answer":["has"],"why":"Para el pelo usamos have; con she, has."},{"type":"fill","q":"The coffee is a ___ cold. (un poco)","answer":["bit"],"why":"Un poco se dice a bit."},{"type":"fill","q":"My brother ___ tall. (to be)","answer":["is","'s"],"why":"He/brother es singular: is."},{"type":"fill","q":"It is a ___ day. (hermoso)","answer":["beautiful"],"why":"Hermoso se dice beautiful."},{"type":"order","words":["a","I","red","have","bag"],"answer":"I have a red bag","es":"Tengo un bolso rojo."},{"type":"order","words":["is","very","The","park","big"],"answer":"The park is very big","es":"El parque es muy grande."},{"type":"order","words":["color","What","is","your","bag"],"answer":"What color is your bag","es":"¿De qué color es tu bolso?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Tengo una camisa azul.","answer":["I have a blue shirt.","I've got a blue shirt."],"why":"El color va antes del sustantivo: a blue shirt."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mi hermano es muy alto.","answer":["My brother is very tall.","My brother's very tall."],"why":"to be + very + adjetivo."},{"type":"translate","es":"La casa es vieja.","answer":["The house is old.","The house's old."],"why":"to be + adjetivo: is old."}],"speak":["I have a red backpack.","My phone is new.","The tickets are expensive.","My brother is tall and funny.","The park is very big.","The ride is really fast!"],"tip":"En español el adjetivo va después (*carro rojo*) y tiene plural (*rojos*). En inglés va antes y no cambia: **red cars**. Nunca digas *reds cars* ni *car red*."},{"n":13,"block":"Mi mundo","title":"Comida y bebida: pedir en un restaurante","emoji":"🍔","minutes":32,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás hablar de comida y bebida, usar some y any, y pedir en un restaurante con I'd like.","sections":[{"h":"Comida y bebida","body":"En Orlando vas a comer (y servir) mucha comida rápida. Estas son palabras que verás en cualquier menú:","table":{"head":["Inglés","Español","Tipo"],"rows":[["burger","hamburguesa","comida"],["fries","papas fritas","comida"],["chicken","pollo","comida"],["salad","ensalada","comida"],["pizza","pizza","comida"],["water","agua","bebida"],["soda","gaseosa","bebida"],["coffee","café","bebida"],["juice","jugo","bebida"]]},"note":"En Estados Unidos las papas fritas son **fries** (o **French fries**). **Chips** son las papitas de bolsa."},{"h":"Contables y no contables","body":"Las cosas **contables** se pueden contar de una en una: **a burger, two burgers**.\n\nLas **no contables** no se cuentan directamente: **water, rice, milk, coffee, bread**. No existe *two waters* en una frase normal sobre cantidad; se dice **a glass of water** o **a cup of coffee**.\n\nLas no contables nunca llevan **a / an** ni plural."},{"h":"A, an, some y any","table":{"head":["Tipo","Afirmativo","Negativo / pregunta"],"rows":[["Contable singular","I'd like a burger.","I don't want a burger. / Do you have a burger?"],["Contable plural","I have some fries.","I don't have any fries. / Do you have any fries?"],["No contable","There is some water.","There isn't any water. / Is there any water?"]]},"note":"Usa **a** antes de consonante (a burger) y **an** antes de vocal (an apple). **Some** va en frases afirmativas y **any** en negativas y preguntas."},{"h":"Pedir en un restaurante","body":"Para pedir con educación usa **I'd like...** (me gustaría). Es más amable que *I want*.\n\nMira este diálogo:\n\n**Waiter:** Hi! Are you ready to order?\n**Customer:** Yes. I'd like a burger and some fries, please.\n**Waiter:** Anything to drink?\n**Customer:** Yes, a soda, please.\n**Waiter:** Sure. Is that all?\n**Customer:** Yes, thank you. How much is it?\n**Waiter:** It's twelve dollars.\n\nPara preguntar el precio: **How much is it?** (uno) o **How much are they?** (varios)."},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["No digas *I want a burger* a un mesero: suena brusco. Mejor **I'd like a burger, please**.","No digas *I'd like a water*. Agua es no contable: **I'd like some water** o **a glass of water**.","No digas *How much cost?*. Es **How much is it?**","Con precios, el dinero se dice así: $12 = **twelve dollars**."]}],"vocab":[{"en":"burger","es":"hamburguesa","ex":"I'd like a burger, please."},{"en":"fries","es":"papas fritas","ex":"Can I have some fries?"},{"en":"chicken","es":"pollo","ex":"The chicken is very good."},{"en":"salad","es":"ensalada","ex":"I'd like a small salad."},{"en":"pizza","es":"pizza","ex":"We want a big pizza."},{"en":"sandwich","es":"sándwich","ex":"I eat a sandwich for lunch."},{"en":"rice","es":"arroz","ex":"We have rice and beans."},{"en":"bread","es":"pan","ex":"There is some bread on the table."},{"en":"water","es":"agua","ex":"A glass of water, please."},{"en":"soda","es":"gaseosa","ex":"I'd like a soda."},{"en":"coffee","es":"café","ex":"She drinks coffee every morning."},{"en":"juice","es":"jugo","ex":"Orange juice, please."},{"en":"menu","es":"menú / carta","ex":"Can I see the menu?"},{"en":"waiter","es":"mesero","ex":"The waiter is friendly."},{"en":"bill","es":"cuenta","ex":"The bill, please."},{"en":"I'd like","es":"me gustaría","ex":"I'd like some water."},{"en":"How much is it?","es":"¿Cuánto cuesta?","ex":"How much is the burger?"},{"en":"dollar","es":"dólar","ex":"It is ten dollars."},{"en":"to drink","es":"beber / tomar","ex":"I drink water at work."},{"en":"to eat","es":"comer","ex":"We eat dinner at seven."}],"examples":[{"en":"I'd like a burger, please.","es":"Quisiera una hamburguesa, por favor."},{"en":"I'd like some fries and a soda.","es":"Quisiera unas papas fritas y una gaseosa."},{"en":"Do you have any juice?","es":"¿Tiene jugo?"},{"en":"There isn't any milk.","es":"No hay leche."},{"en":"We have some rice and chicken.","es":"Tenemos arroz y pollo."},{"en":"Can I see the menu, please?","es":"¿Puedo ver el menú, por favor?"},{"en":"Are you ready to order?","es":"¿Están listos para ordenar?"},{"en":"Anything to drink?","es":"¿Algo de beber?"},{"en":"How much is it?","es":"¿Cuánto cuesta?"},{"en":"It's twelve dollars.","es":"Cuesta doce dólares."},{"en":"How much are the fries?","es":"¿Cuánto cuestan las papas?"},{"en":"The bill, please.","es":"La cuenta, por favor."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I'd like ___ burger, please.","options":["a","an","some"],"answer":0,"why":"Burger es contable singular y empieza con consonante: a burger."},{"type":"choice","q":"I'd like ___ apple.","options":["a","an","any"],"answer":1,"why":"Apple empieza con vocal: an apple."},{"type":"choice","q":"I'd like ___ water, please.","options":["a","an","some"],"answer":2,"why":"Water es no contable, por eso some."},{"type":"choice","q":"Do you have ___ juice?","options":["some","any","an"],"answer":1,"why":"En preguntas se usa any."},{"type":"choice","q":"There isn't ___ bread.","options":["any","some","a"],"answer":0,"why":"En negativo se usa any."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which one is uncountable?","options":["burger","rice","sandwich"],"answer":1,"why":"Rice (arroz) es no contable; burger y sandwich se cuentan."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you ask the price of a burger?","options":["How much is it?","How many is it?","What cost it?"],"answer":0,"why":"El precio se pregunta con How much is it?"},{"type":"fill","q":"I'd ___ a soda, please.","answer":["like"],"why":"I'd like = me gustaría."},{"type":"fill","q":"We have ___ fries. (afirmativo)","answer":["some"],"why":"En frases afirmativas con plural se usa some."},{"type":"fill","q":"Is there ___ coffee? (pregunta)","answer":["any"],"why":"En preguntas se usa any."},{"type":"fill","q":"How ___ is the pizza?","answer":["much"],"why":"El precio se pregunta con how much."},{"type":"fill","q":"Can I see the ___, please? (la carta del restaurante)","answer":["menu"],"why":"El menú del restaurante es menu."},{"type":"order","words":["like","I'd","a","burger","please"],"answer":"I'd like a burger please","es":"Quisiera una hamburguesa, por favor."},{"type":"order","words":["is","much","How","it"],"answer":"How much is it","es":"¿Cuánto cuesta?"},{"type":"order","words":["any","Do","you","have","juice"],"answer":"Do you have any juice","es":"¿Tiene jugo?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Quisiera un poco de agua, por favor.","answer":["I'd like some water, please.","I would like some water, please."],"why":"Agua es no contable: some water."},{"type":"translate","es":"No hay pan.","answer":["There isn't any bread.","There is not any bread.","There's no bread."],"why":"Negativo con no contable: there isn't any."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Cuánto cuestan las papas fritas?","answer":["How much are the fries?","How much are fries?"],"why":"Fries es plural: how much are."}],"speak":["I'd like a burger and some fries, please.","Can I see the menu, please?","Do you have any juice?","A glass of water, please.","How much is it?","The bill, please."],"tip":"Mucha gente dice *I want a coffee* o *I'd like a water*. En un restaurante usa **I'd like...** (más amable) y recuerda que water, rice y coffee son no contables: **some water**, **a cup of coffee**."},{"n":14,"block":"Mi mundo","title":"Ropa, cuerpo y clima","emoji":"🌦️","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás hablar de la ropa que llevas, las partes del cuerpo y el clima, incluyendo la temperatura en grados Fahrenheit.","sections":[{"h":"La ropa","body":"Para decir qué ropa llevas puesta usa **I'm wearing...** (estoy usando / llevo puesto).\n\n**I'm wearing a blue shirt and black pants.**\n\nCuidado con la palabra *pants*: en inglés americano siempre es plural. **My pants are new.**","table":{"head":["Inglés","Español","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["shirt","camisa","a white shirt"],["T-shirt","camiseta","a red T-shirt"],["pants","pantalón","black pants"],["shorts","pantalones cortos","blue shorts"],["dress","vestido","a green dress"],["shoes","zapatos","new shoes"],["jacket","chaqueta","a warm jacket"],["hat","sombrero / gorra","a funny hat"]]},"note":"Pants, shorts, shoes y jeans son plurales: no se dice *a pants*. Se dice **a pair of pants** o simplemente **pants**."},{"h":"Partes del cuerpo","body":"Te servirán en el trabajo, en una consulta médica y para describir personas:","table":{"head":["Inglés","Español"],"rows":[["head","cabeza"],["eyes","ojos"],["nose","nariz"],["mouth","boca"],["hand / hands","mano / manos"],["arm","brazo"],["leg","pierna"],["foot / feet","pie / pies"]]},"note":"Ojo con los plurales irregulares: **foot → feet**. Y recuerda: *my hand hurts* = me duele la mano (**My hand hurts**)."},{"h":"El clima y las estaciones","body":"Para preguntar por el clima: **What's the weather like?** (¿Cómo está el clima?)\n\nPara responder con **It's** + adjetivo: **It's sunny. It's hot. It's cold.** O con **It's** + verbo -ing: **It's raining. It's snowing.**","table":{"head":["Palabra","Significa","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["sunny","soleado","It's sunny today."],["cloudy","nublado","It's cloudy."],["rainy / raining","lluvioso / lloviendo","It's raining now."],["windy","ventoso","It's windy."],["hot / cold","caliente / frío","It's very hot."],["summer / winter","verano / invierno","Summer is hot in Orlando."],["spring / fall","primavera / otoño","Fall is nice."]]},"note":"En Estados Unidos el otoño se dice **fall**; en inglés británico, **autumn**."},{"h":"Fahrenheit y Celsius","body":"En Colombia usamos grados **Celsius** (°C). En Estados Unidos usan **Fahrenheit** (°F). Esto es muy importante para tu viaje a Orlando.\n\n**32 °F = 0 °C** (el agua se congela)\n**68 °F = 20 °C** (clima agradable)\n**86 °F = 30 °C** (hace calor)\n**95 °F = 35 °C** (¡mucho calor!)\n\nEn verano, Orlando suele tener entre **90 y 95 degrees**. Se dice: **It's ninety-five degrees today.** (sin decir 'Fahrenheit').\n\nTruco rápido: resta 30 a los grados Fahrenheit y divide entre 2. Es solo aproximado, pero te da una idea."},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["No digas *I wear a blue shirt* para 'llevo puesta ahora'. Lo natural es **I'm wearing a blue shirt**.","No digas *Is hot* ni *Hace calor* literal. Se dice **It's hot**.","No digas *I have cold* para 'tengo frío'. Se dice **I'm cold**.","No digas *a pants*. **Pants** es plural: *my pants are black*."]}],"vocab":[{"en":"shirt","es":"camisa","ex":"I'm wearing a white shirt."},{"en":"T-shirt","es":"camiseta","ex":"He has a red T-shirt."},{"en":"pants","es":"pantalón","ex":"My pants are black."},{"en":"shorts","es":"pantalones cortos","ex":"I wear shorts in summer."},{"en":"dress","es":"vestido","ex":"She's wearing a blue dress."},{"en":"shoes","es":"zapatos","ex":"My shoes are new."},{"en":"jacket","es":"chaqueta","ex":"It's cold. Take a jacket."},{"en":"hat","es":"sombrero / gorra","ex":"I wear a hat in the sun."},{"en":"head","es":"cabeza","ex":"My head hurts."},{"en":"eyes","es":"ojos","ex":"She has green eyes."},{"en":"hand","es":"mano","ex":"Wash your hands."},{"en":"foot","es":"pie","ex":"My foot hurts."},{"en":"weather","es":"clima","ex":"The weather is nice today."},{"en":"sunny","es":"soleado","ex":"It's sunny in Orlando."},{"en":"cloudy","es":"nublado","ex":"It's cloudy this morning."},{"en":"raining","es":"lloviendo","ex":"It's raining now."},{"en":"hot","es":"caliente / hace calor","ex":"It's very hot today."},{"en":"cold","es":"frío / hace frío","ex":"I'm cold."},{"en":"summer","es":"verano","ex":"Summer is hot in Florida."},{"en":"degrees","es":"grados","ex":"It's ninety degrees."}],"examples":[{"en":"I'm wearing a blue shirt and black pants.","es":"Llevo una camisa azul y pantalón negro."},{"en":"She's wearing a green dress.","es":"Ella lleva un vestido verde."},{"en":"My shoes are new.","es":"Mis zapatos son nuevos."},{"en":"My head hurts.","es":"Me duele la cabeza."},{"en":"She has brown eyes.","es":"Ella tiene ojos cafés."},{"en":"What's the weather like today?","es":"¿Cómo está el clima hoy?"},{"en":"It's sunny and hot.","es":"Está soleado y hace calor."},{"en":"It's raining now.","es":"Está lloviendo ahora."},{"en":"It's ninety-five degrees in Orlando.","es":"Hay 95 grados en Orlando."},{"en":"I'm cold. I need a jacket.","es":"Tengo frío. Necesito una chaqueta."},{"en":"Summer is very hot in Florida.","es":"El verano es muy caluroso en Florida."},{"en":"I wear shorts in the summer.","es":"Uso pantalones cortos en el verano."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What's the weather like? It's ___ and I need an umbrella.","options":["sunny","raining","hot"],"answer":1,"why":"Un paraguas se necesita cuando llueve: raining."},{"type":"choice","q":"I'm ___ a blue shirt.","options":["wearing","wear","having"],"answer":0,"why":"Para ropa que llevas ahora: I'm wearing."},{"type":"choice","q":"My ___ are black.","options":["pants","pant","a pants"],"answer":0,"why":"Pants es plural: my pants are."},{"type":"choice","q":"In Orlando in summer it is ___ degrees.","options":["35","95","5"],"answer":1,"why":"Con Fahrenheit, 95 es unos 35 °C: mucho calor."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say 'Tengo frío'?","options":["I'm cold.","I have cold.","It's cold me."],"answer":0,"why":"Para sensación personal usamos I'm cold."},{"type":"choice","q":"What is the plural of 'foot'?","options":["foots","feet","feets"],"answer":1,"why":"Foot tiene plural irregular: feet."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which word means 'otoño' in the USA?","options":["fall","spring","summer"],"answer":0,"why":"En inglés americano otoño es fall."},{"type":"fill","q":"It's ___ today. I need my hat. (soleado)","answer":["sunny"],"why":"Soleado se dice sunny."},{"type":"fill","q":"What's the ___ like today?","answer":["weather"],"why":"El clima es weather."},{"type":"fill","q":"It's ___ now. (llover, -ing)","answer":["raining"],"why":"Para algo que pasa ahora: raining."},{"type":"fill","q":"She has green ___. (ojos)","answer":["eyes"],"why":"Ojos en plural: eyes."},{"type":"fill","q":"I'm ___ shorts today. (llevar puesto)","answer":["wearing"],"why":"Ropa puesta: I'm wearing."},{"type":"order","words":["like","What's","the","weather","today"],"answer":"What's the weather like today","es":"¿Cómo está el clima hoy?"},{"type":"order","words":["wearing","I'm","a","jacket"],"answer":"I'm wearing a jacket","es":"Llevo una chaqueta."},{"type":"order","words":["hot","very","It's","today"],"answer":"It's very hot today","es":"Hoy hace mucho calor."},{"type":"translate","es":"Está lloviendo.","answer":["It's raining.","It is raining."],"why":"Clima ahora: It's raining."},{"type":"translate","es":"Me duele la cabeza.","answer":["My head hurts.","I have a headache."],"why":"My head hurts es la forma más común."},{"type":"translate","es":"Llevo una camiseta roja.","answer":["I'm wearing a red T-shirt.","I am wearing a red T-shirt.","I'm wearing a red shirt.","I am wearing a red shirt."],"why":"Ropa puesta ahora: I'm wearing."}],"speak":["What's the weather like today?","It's sunny and very hot.","It's ninety-five degrees in Orlando.","I'm wearing a blue shirt and black pants.","I'm cold. I need a jacket.","My head hurts."],"tip":"Tendemos a decir *I have cold* o *I have hot* por 'tengo frío/calor'. En inglés se usa to be: **I'm cold**, **I'm hot**. Y recuerda: en EE. UU. los grados son Fahrenheit, no Celsius."},{"n":15,"block":"Mi mundo","title":"La ciudad y las direcciones","emoji":"🗺️","minutes":32,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás preguntar y dar direcciones en la ciudad, y hablar de medios de transporte.","sections":[{"h":"Lugares de la ciudad","body":"Cuando llegues a Orlando necesitarás encontrar muchos lugares. Estas son las palabras más útiles:","table":{"head":["Inglés","Español","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["bank","banco","The bank is open."],["bus stop","parada de bus","The bus stop is near."],["supermarket","supermercado","I go to the supermarket."],["airport","aeropuerto","The airport is far."],["hotel","hotel","My hotel is nice."],["restaurant","restaurante","The restaurant is busy."],["pharmacy","farmacia","The pharmacy is closed."],["hospital","hospital","The hospital is big."],["park","parque","We walk in the park."]]}},{"h":"Preguntar dónde está algo","body":"Para llamar la atención de alguien con amabilidad empieza con **Excuse me**.\n\n**Excuse me, where is the bank?** Disculpe, ¿dónde está el banco?\n**Excuse me, how do I get to the airport?** ¿Cómo llego al aeropuerto?\n**Is there a pharmacy near here?** ¿Hay una farmacia cerca de aquí?\n\nCuando alguien te ayuda, di **Thank you!** o **Thanks a lot!**"},{"h":"Dar direcciones","table":{"head":["Frase","Significa"],"rows":[["Go straight.","Siga derecho."],["Turn left.","Gire a la izquierda."],["Turn right.","Gire a la derecha."],["It's next to the bank.","Está al lado del banco."],["It's across from the park.","Está al frente (al otro lado) del parque."],["It's on the corner.","Está en la esquina."],["It's on the left / right.","Está a la izquierda / derecha."],["It's two blocks away.","Está a dos cuadras."]]},"note":"Las órdenes (**go, turn, walk**) no llevan sujeto. Ejemplo completo: **Go straight for two blocks, then turn left. The hotel is on the corner.**"},{"h":"El transporte","body":"Para decir cómo viajas usamos **by** + medio de transporte: **by bus, by taxi, by train, by plane, by car**.\n\nExcepción: caminando se dice **on foot** o **I walk**.\n\n**I go to work by bus.** Voy al trabajo en bus.\n**We travel to Orlando by plane.** Viajamos a Orlando en avión.\n\nAlgunas preguntas útiles: **How do you get to work?** **How long is the trip?**"},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["No digas *Go direct*. Es **Go straight**.","No digas *I go in the bus*. Con medio de transporte generalizado se usa **by bus**.","No uses *in front of* para 'al frente, al otro lado de la calle'. Mejor **across from**.","Para llamar la atención no grites *Hey!*: di **Excuse me**."]}],"vocab":[{"en":"bank","es":"banco","ex":"The bank is on Main Street."},{"en":"bus stop","es":"parada de bus","ex":"The bus stop is near my hotel."},{"en":"supermarket","es":"supermercado","ex":"The supermarket is open."},{"en":"airport","es":"aeropuerto","ex":"I'm at the airport."},{"en":"hotel","es":"hotel","ex":"My hotel is across from the park."},{"en":"pharmacy","es":"farmacia","ex":"Is there a pharmacy near here?"},{"en":"restaurant","es":"restaurante","ex":"The restaurant is on the corner."},{"en":"street","es":"calle","ex":"Turn left on this street."},{"en":"corner","es":"esquina","ex":"It's on the corner."},{"en":"block","es":"cuadra","ex":"It's two blocks away."},{"en":"turn left","es":"gire a la izquierda","ex":"Turn left at the bank."},{"en":"turn right","es":"gire a la derecha","ex":"Turn right at the hotel."},{"en":"go straight","es":"siga derecho","ex":"Go straight for one block."},{"en":"across from","es":"al frente de","ex":"The bank is across from the park."},{"en":"bus","es":"bus","ex":"I go to work by bus."},{"en":"taxi","es":"taxi","ex":"We take a taxi to the hotel."},{"en":"train","es":"tren","ex":"The train is fast."},{"en":"plane","es":"avión","ex":"I travel by plane."},{"en":"far","es":"lejos","ex":"The airport is far from here."},{"en":"excuse me","es":"disculpe","ex":"Excuse me, where is the bank?"}],"examples":[{"en":"Excuse me, where is the bank?","es":"Disculpe, ¿dónde está el banco?"},{"en":"Is there a pharmacy near here?","es":"¿Hay una farmacia cerca de aquí?"},{"en":"How do I get to the airport?","es":"¿Cómo llego al aeropuerto?"},{"en":"Go straight for two blocks.","es":"Siga derecho dos cuadras."},{"en":"Turn left at the corner.","es":"Gire a la izquierda en la esquina."},{"en":"Turn right, then go straight.","es":"Gire a la derecha y siga derecho."},{"en":"The bank is next to the supermarket.","es":"El banco está al lado del supermercado."},{"en":"The hotel is across from the park.","es":"El hotel está frente al parque."},{"en":"It's on the left.","es":"Está a la izquierda."},{"en":"I go to work by bus.","es":"Voy al trabajo en bus."},{"en":"We travel to Orlando by plane.","es":"Viajamos a Orlando en avión."},{"en":"Thank you very much!","es":"¡Muchas gracias!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"___ me, where is the bank?","options":["Excuse","Sorry","Please"],"answer":0,"why":"Excuse me es la forma educada para llamar la atención."},{"type":"choice","q":"Go ___ for two blocks. (siga derecho)","options":["direct","straight","right"],"answer":1,"why":"Siga derecho se dice go straight."},{"type":"choice","q":"I go to work ___ bus.","options":["in","by","on the"],"answer":1,"why":"Con medios de transporte usamos by: by bus."},{"type":"choice","q":"The hotel is ___ the park. (al otro lado, frente a)","options":["across from","behind","under"],"answer":0,"why":"Al frente (al otro lado) se dice across from."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which place sells medicine?","options":["pharmacy","airport","bus stop"],"answer":0,"why":"Pharmacy es la farmacia."},{"type":"choice","q":"Turn ___ at the corner. (a la izquierda)","options":["left","right","straight"],"answer":0,"why":"Izquierda es left."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say 'a dos cuadras'?","options":["two blocks away","two streets near","two corners"],"answer":0,"why":"A dos cuadras se dice two blocks away."},{"type":"fill","q":"Excuse me, where ___ the airport?","answer":["is"],"why":"Airport es singular: where is."},{"type":"fill","q":"Turn ___ at the bank. (a la derecha)","answer":["right"],"why":"Derecha es right."},{"type":"fill","q":"I travel to Orlando ___ plane.","answer":["by"],"why":"Transporte con by: by plane."},{"type":"fill","q":"The supermarket is ___ to the bank. (al lado)","answer":["next"],"why":"Al lado de se dice next to."},{"type":"fill","q":"It's on the ___. (la esquina)","answer":["corner"],"why":"Esquina es corner."},{"type":"order","words":["is","Excuse","me","where","the","bank"],"answer":"Excuse me where is the bank","es":"Disculpe, ¿dónde está el banco?"},{"type":"order","words":["Turn","left","the","at","corner"],"answer":"Turn left at the corner","es":"Gire a la izquierda en la esquina."},{"type":"order","words":["go","I","bus","to","by","work"],"answer":"I go to work by bus","es":"Voy al trabajo en bus."},{"type":"translate","es":"Siga derecho dos cuadras.","answer":["Go straight for two blocks.","Go straight two blocks."],"why":"Go straight es siga derecho; blocks son cuadras."},{"type":"translate","es":"El hotel está al lado del banco.","answer":["The hotel is next to the bank."],"why":"Al lado de se dice next to."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Hay una farmacia cerca de aquí?","answer":["Is there a pharmacy near here?","Is there a pharmacy near?"],"why":"Pregunta con there is en singular: Is there a...?"}],"speak":["Excuse me, where is the bank?","How do I get to the airport?","Go straight for two blocks.","Turn left at the corner.","The hotel is across from the park.","Thank you very much!"],"tip":"Un error muy común es traducir 'siga derecho' como *go direct* o *go right straight*. Recuerda: **go straight**. Y para el transporte, no digas *in the bus*: usa **by bus**."},{"n":16,"block":"Mi mundo","title":"Trabajos y estudios","emoji":"💼","minutes":32,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir qué haces (trabajo o estudios), preguntar a otros y usar vocabulario básico de un parque temático.","sections":[{"h":"Trabajos comunes","body":"En inglés casi siempre usamos **a / an** antes del trabajo: **I am a student**, **She is an engineer**. En español lo omitimos, pero en inglés es obligatorio.","table":{"head":["Inglés","Español","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["engineer","ingeniero/a","He is an engineer."],["student","estudiante","I am a student."],["teacher","profesor/a","She is a teacher."],["waiter","mesero/a","He is a waiter."],["cashier","cajero/a","She is a cashier."],["driver","conductor/a","He is a driver."],["doctor","médico/a","My mom is a doctor."],["nurse","enfermero/a","She is a nurse."]]},"note":"**An** va antes de vocal: an engineer, an actor. **A** va antes de consonante: a teacher, a waiter."},{"h":"What do you do?","body":"Esta es la pregunta clásica para conocer a alguien.\n\n**What do you do?** significa ¿A qué te dedicas? o ¿En qué trabajas?\n\nRespuestas:\n**I'm a student.**\n**I work at a bank.**\n**I study systems engineering.**\n\nLa pregunta también se puede dirigir a otras personas: **What does she do?** (con she/he, **does**). Respuesta: **She is a nurse.**"},{"h":"Work at, work in, study","table":{"head":["Frase","Cuándo se usa","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["I work at...","una empresa o lugar específico","I work at a restaurant."],["I work in...","un área o ciudad","I work in marketing. / I work in Orlando."],["I work as...","tu cargo","I work as a cashier."],["I study...","tu carrera o materia","I study engineering."],["I study at...","tu universidad","I study at a university."]]},"note":"Con he/she/it el verbo termina en **-s**: He **works** at a bank. She **studies** at a university."},{"h":"Vocabulario del parque temático","body":"Si trabajas en Disney, estas palabras las escucharás todos los días:","table":{"head":["Inglés","Español","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["ride","atracción","This ride is fun."],["ticket","boleto","Show your ticket, please."],["guest","visitante / huésped","Welcome, guests!"],["shift","turno de trabajo","My shift starts at nine."],["uniform","uniforme","I wear a uniform."],["manager","gerente","My manager is very kind."],["cast member","empleado de Disney","I'm a cast member."]]},"note":"En Disney a los clientes se les llama **guests**, no customers. Y a los empleados, **cast members**."},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["No digas *I am student*. Con trabajos usa **a / an**: **I am a student**.","No digas *I am working in a bank* para tu trabajo general. Mejor **I work at a bank**.","No digas *She work*. Con she/he/it hay una -s: **She works**.","No digas *I am engineer*. Es **I am an engineer** (an antes de vocal)."]}],"vocab":[{"en":"job","es":"trabajo (empleo)","ex":"I want a new job."},{"en":"engineer","es":"ingeniero","ex":"He is an engineer."},{"en":"student","es":"estudiante","ex":"I am a university student."},{"en":"teacher","es":"profesor","ex":"My teacher is friendly."},{"en":"waiter","es":"mesero","ex":"The waiter is busy."},{"en":"cashier","es":"cajero","ex":"She is a cashier at a store."},{"en":"driver","es":"conductor","ex":"He is a bus driver."},{"en":"doctor","es":"médico","ex":"My aunt is a doctor."},{"en":"ride","es":"atracción","ex":"That ride is really fast."},{"en":"ticket","es":"boleto","ex":"Do you have your ticket?"},{"en":"guest","es":"visitante","ex":"Welcome, guests!"},{"en":"shift","es":"turno","ex":"My shift is from nine to five."},{"en":"uniform","es":"uniforme","ex":"I wear a blue uniform."},{"en":"manager","es":"gerente","ex":"Ask the manager, please."},{"en":"cast member","es":"empleado de Disney","ex":"I want to be a cast member."},{"en":"to work","es":"trabajar","ex":"I work in Orlando."},{"en":"to study","es":"estudiar","ex":"I study at night."},{"en":"university","es":"universidad","ex":"I study at a university."},{"en":"company","es":"empresa","ex":"She works at a big company."},{"en":"What do you do?","es":"¿A qué te dedicas?","ex":"Hi, what do you do?"}],"examples":[{"en":"What do you do?","es":"¿A qué te dedicas?"},{"en":"I'm a student.","es":"Soy estudiante."},{"en":"I study systems engineering.","es":"Estudio ingeniería de sistemas."},{"en":"She is an engineer.","es":"Ella es ingeniera."},{"en":"He works at a restaurant.","es":"Él trabaja en un restaurante."},{"en":"What does your brother do?","es":"¿A qué se dedica tu hermano?"},{"en":"My shift starts at nine.","es":"Mi turno empieza a las nueve."},{"en":"I wear a uniform at work.","es":"Uso uniforme en el trabajo."},{"en":"Welcome, guests!","es":"¡Bienvenidos, visitantes!"},{"en":"This ride is open.","es":"Esta atracción está abierta."},{"en":"Please show your ticket.","es":"Por favor muestre su boleto."},{"en":"I want to be a cast member.","es":"Quiero ser empleado de Disney."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I am ___ student.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":0,"why":"Student empieza con consonante: a student."},{"type":"choice","q":"She is ___ engineer.","options":["a","an","–"],"answer":1,"why":"Engineer empieza con vocal: an engineer."},{"type":"choice","q":"He ___ at a bank.","options":["work","works","working"],"answer":1,"why":"Con he se agrega -s: works."},{"type":"choice","q":"What ___ she do?","options":["do","does","is"],"answer":1,"why":"Con she se usa does en la pregunta."},{"type":"choice","q":"At a theme park, what are the visitors called?","options":["guests","drivers","managers"],"answer":0,"why":"En Disney a los visitantes se les llama guests."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which word means 'turno de trabajo'?","options":["shift","ticket","ride"],"answer":0,"why":"Shift es el turno."},{"type":"choice","q":"I study ___ a university.","options":["in","at","by"],"answer":1,"why":"Con instituciones se usa at: at a university."},{"type":"fill","q":"What do you ___?","answer":["do"],"why":"La pregunta correcta es What do you do?"},{"type":"fill","q":"I am ___ engineer.","answer":["an"],"why":"Engineer empieza con vocal: an."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ at a restaurant. (work)","answer":["works"],"why":"Con she se agrega -s: works."},{"type":"fill","q":"My ___ starts at eight. (turno)","answer":["shift"],"why":"Turno de trabajo es shift."},{"type":"fill","q":"Please show your ___. (boleto)","answer":["ticket"],"why":"Boleto se dice ticket."},{"type":"order","words":["do","What","you","do"],"answer":"What do you do","es":"¿A qué te dedicas?"},{"type":"order","words":["a","am","I","student"],"answer":"I am a student","es":"Soy estudiante."},{"type":"order","words":["works","He","at","a","restaurant"],"answer":"He works at a restaurant","es":"Él trabaja en un restaurante."},{"type":"translate","es":"Soy ingeniero.","answer":["I am an engineer.","I'm an engineer."],"why":"Con trabajos usamos a/an: an engineer."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella trabaja en un banco.","answer":["She works at a bank.","She works in a bank."],"why":"Con she el verbo lleva -s: works."},{"type":"translate","es":"Estudio ingeniería de sistemas.","answer":["I study systems engineering."],"why":"Estudiar una carrera: I study + carrera."}],"speak":["What do you do?","I'm a student.","I study systems engineering.","I want to be a cast member.","My shift starts at nine.","Welcome, guests!"],"tip":"En español decimos *soy estudiante* sin artículo. En inglés es obligatorio: **I am a student**, **I am an engineer**. Y no olvides la -s con he/she: **She works**."},{"n":17,"block":"Verbos y tiempos","title":"Presente simple I: tu rutina diaria","emoji":"⏰","minutes":35,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás contar tu rutina y la de otras personas usando el presente simple afirmativo.","sections":[{"h":"¿Para qué sirve el presente simple?","body":"El **presente simple** (*simple present*) sirve para hablar de **rutinas, hábitos y hechos que siempre son verdad**.\n\nEn español usamos el presente: *me levanto a las 7*, *trabajo en Orlando*, *el sol sale por el este*. En inglés también, pero con una regla especial para **he / she / it**.\n\nLos tres momentos con el verbo **work**:\n\n- Pasado: **I worked** yesterday. (Trabajé ayer.)\n- Presente: **I work** every day. (Trabajo todos los días.)\n- Futuro: **I will work** tomorrow. (Trabajaré mañana.)\n\nHoy nos concentramos en el **presente**."},{"h":"Cómo se forma: I / you / we / they + verbo base","body":"Con **I, you, we, they** usas el **verbo base**, sin cambiar nada. El verbo base es el verbo tal como aparece en el diccionario, sin *to*.\n\n**I study** at the university. (Estudio en la universidad.)\n\n**They live** in Bogotá. (Ellos viven en Bogotá.)\n\nNo se agrega nada. No hay un verbo auxiliar en la afirmación: solo pronombre + verbo."},{"h":"Conjugación completa del verbo work","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Presente: work","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["I","work","I work in the morning.","Trabajo en la mañana."],["you","work","You work every day.","Tú trabajas todos los días."],["he / she / it","works","She works at a hotel.","Ella trabaja en un hotel."],["we","work","We work together.","Trabajamos juntos."],["they","work","They work in Orlando.","Ellos trabajan en Orlando."]]},"note":"Mira la diferencia: solo he / she / it cambia (work → works). Esa es la famosa **-s de la tercera persona**."},{"h":"He / she / it: la regla de la -s","body":"Con **he, she, it** el verbo lleva **-s** o **-es** al final. Hay cuatro reglas de escritura:","table":{"head":["Regla","Verbo base","He / she / it","Significa"],"rows":[["Casi todos: + s","eat","eats","come"],["Casi todos: + s","work","works","trabaja"],["Termina en -s, -sh, -ch, -x, -o: + es","watch","watches","mira"],["Termina en -s, -sh, -ch, -x, -o: + es","go","goes","va"],["Consonante + y: quita y, pone -ies","study","studies","estudia"],["Vocal + y: solo + s","play","plays","juega"],["Irregular","have","has","tiene"]]},"note":"**Have** es el único realmente irregular: he **has**, nunca *he haves*. **Do** también cambia de sonido: he **does**."},{"h":"25 verbos de todos los días","list":["**wake up** (despertarse), **get up** (levantarse), **take a shower** (bañarse), **brush** (cepillar), **eat** (comer)","**drink** (beber), **go** (ir), **study** (estudiar), **work** (trabajar), **have** (tener / comer)","**read** (leer), **write** (escribir), **watch** (mirar), **play** (jugar), **listen** (escuchar)","**walk** (caminar), **cook** (cocinar), **clean** (limpiar), **start** (empezar), **finish** (terminar)","**live** (vivir), **speak** (hablar), **drive** (manejar), **sleep** (dormir), **come** (venir)"],"note":"Con **he / she / it**: wakes up, gets up, takes, brushes, eats, drinks, goes, studies, works, has, reads, writes, watches, plays, listens, walks, cooks, cleans, starts, finishes, lives, speaks, drives, sleeps, comes."},{"h":"Expresiones de tiempo para la rutina","table":{"head":["Expresión","Significa","Ejemplo","Traducción"],"rows":[["every day","todos los días","I study every day.","Estudio todos los días."],["every morning","todas las mañanas","He drinks coffee every morning.","Él toma café todas las mañanas."],["in the morning","en la mañana","We work in the morning.","Trabajamos en la mañana."],["in the afternoon","en la tarde","They play soccer in the afternoon.","Ellos juegan fútbol en la tarde."],["at night","en la noche","She reads at night.","Ella lee en la noche."],["at 7 o'clock","a las 7","I get up at 7.","Me levanto a las 7."],["on Mondays","los lunes","I go to class on Mondays.","Voy a clase los lunes."]]},"note":"Usa **at** con horas (at 7), **in** con partes del día (in the morning), **on** con días (on Monday). Excepción: **at night**."},{"h":"Error típico: olvidar la -s","body":"En español el verbo cambia con todas las personas, así que en inglés es fácil olvidar que **he / she / it** necesita su -s.\n\n- Mal: *She work at Disney.*\n- Bien: **She works at Disney.**\n\nY al revés: no pongas -s con I / you / we / they. *I works* está mal; **I work** está bien."}],"vocab":[{"en":"wake up","es":"despertarse","ex":"I wake up at 6."},{"en":"get up","es":"levantarse","ex":"She gets up at 7."},{"en":"take a shower","es":"bañarse / ducharse","ex":"He takes a shower in the morning."},{"en":"eat","es":"comer","ex":"We eat lunch at noon."},{"en":"drink","es":"beber / tomar","ex":"I drink coffee every day."},{"en":"go","es":"ir","ex":"They go to the university."},{"en":"study","es":"estudiar","ex":"He studies English at night."},{"en":"work","es":"trabajar","ex":"She works in Orlando."},{"en":"have","es":"tener / comer (una comida)","ex":"I have breakfast at 7."},{"en":"read","es":"leer","ex":"He reads emails every morning."},{"en":"watch","es":"mirar / ver","ex":"She watches TV at night."},{"en":"play","es":"jugar / tocar","ex":"We play soccer on Sundays."},{"en":"walk","es":"caminar","ex":"I walk to class."},{"en":"cook","es":"cocinar","ex":"My mother cooks dinner."},{"en":"clean","es":"limpiar","ex":"They clean the house on Saturdays."},{"en":"start","es":"empezar","ex":"Class starts at 8."},{"en":"finish","es":"terminar","ex":"He finishes work at 5."},{"en":"live","es":"vivir","ex":"I live in Medellín."},{"en":"every day","es":"todos los días","ex":"I practice English every day."},{"en":"in the morning","es":"en la mañana","ex":"She works in the morning."},{"en":"at night","es":"en la noche","ex":"We study at night."},{"en":"at 7 o'clock","es":"a las 7 en punto","ex":"He gets up at 7 o'clock."}],"examples":[{"en":"I wake up at 6 in the morning.","es":"Me despierto a las 6 de la mañana."},{"en":"I take a shower and brush my teeth.","es":"Me baño y me cepillo los dientes."},{"en":"You study systems engineering.","es":"Tú estudias ingeniería de sistemas."},{"en":"She works at a hotel in Orlando.","es":"Ella trabaja en un hotel en Orlando."},{"en":"He eats breakfast at 7.","es":"Él desayuna a las 7."},{"en":"My brother plays video games every night.","es":"Mi hermano juega videojuegos todas las noches."},{"en":"We go to the university every day.","es":"Vamos a la universidad todos los días."},{"en":"They live near the park.","es":"Ellos viven cerca del parque."},{"en":"The bus comes at 7:30.","es":"El bus llega a las 7:30."},{"en":"My mother cooks lunch for the family.","es":"Mi mamá cocina el almuerzo para la familia."},{"en":"He studies English and watches movies at night.","es":"Él estudia inglés y ve películas en la noche."},{"en":"Class starts at 8 and finishes at 10.","es":"La clase empieza a las 8 y termina a las 10."},{"en":"Yesterday I worked a lot. Today I work less. Tomorrow I will rest.","es":"Ayer trabajé mucho. Hoy trabajo menos. Mañana descansaré."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"She ___ at a hotel.","options":["work","works","working"],"answer":1,"why":"She es tercera persona singular, así que el verbo lleva -s: works."},{"type":"choice","q":"They ___ to the university every day.","options":["go","goes","going"],"answer":0,"why":"They usa el verbo base: go."},{"type":"choice","q":"He ___ English at night.","options":["study","studys","studies"],"answer":2,"why":"Study termina en consonante + y, entonces la y cambia a -ies."},{"type":"choice","q":"My sister ___ a car.","options":["have","haves","has"],"answer":2,"why":"Have es irregular con he / she / it: has."},{"type":"choice","q":"I get up ___ 7 o'clock.","options":["in","at","on"],"answer":1,"why":"Con horas exactas se usa at."},{"type":"choice","q":"We work ___ the morning.","options":["in","at","on"],"answer":0,"why":"Con partes del día (the morning) se usa in."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el presente correcto de watch con she?","options":["watchs","watches","watchies"],"answer":1,"why":"Los verbos que terminan en -ch llevan -es."},{"type":"fill","q":"He ___ coffee every morning. (drink)","answer":["drinks"],"why":"He necesita -s: drinks."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ at 6 every day. (wake up)","answer":["wake up"],"why":"Con I se usa el verbo base: wake up."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ TV at night. (watch)","answer":["watches"],"why":"Watch termina en -ch, entonces agrega -es."},{"type":"fill","q":"My father ___ to work by bus. (go)","answer":["goes"],"why":"Go termina en -o, entonces agrega -es."},{"type":"fill","q":"The class ___ at 8. (start)","answer":["starts"],"why":"The class equivale a it, así que lleva -s."},{"type":"fill","q":"Santiago ___ English every day. (study)","answer":["studies"],"why":"Study cambia la y por -ies con he / she / it."},{"type":"order","words":["at","I","7","get","up"],"answer":"I get up at 7","es":"Me levanto a las 7."},{"type":"order","words":["lives","in","She","Orlando"],"answer":"She lives in Orlando","es":"Ella vive en Orlando."},{"type":"order","words":["every","play","They","soccer","Sunday"],"answer":"They play soccer every Sunday","es":"Ellos juegan fútbol todos los domingos."},{"type":"translate","es":"Yo trabajo todos los días.","answer":["I work every day."],"why":"Con I se usa el verbo base: work."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella estudia en la noche.","answer":["She studies at night.","She studies in the evening."],"why":"She lleva -ies en study, y at night es la expresión usual."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mi hermano come a las 12.","answer":["My brother eats at 12.","My brother eats at noon.","My brother eats at 12 o'clock."],"why":"My brother equivale a he, así que eat pasa a eats."}],"speak":["I wake up at six every day.","I take a shower in the morning.","I study systems engineering.","My mother cooks dinner at night.","My brother works in the afternoon.","She goes to the university on Mondays.","We eat lunch at noon.","He watches TV and studies English at night."],"tip":"Error típico: olvidar la -s con he / she / it (*She work*) o ponerla con I / you / we / they (*I works*). Antes de hablar, pregúntate: ¿es he, she o it? Entonces agrega -s / -es / -ies."},{"n":18,"block":"Verbos y tiempos","title":"Presente simple II: negativo, preguntas y frecuencia","emoji":"❓","minutes":40,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás negar, preguntar y decir con qué frecuencia haces las cosas usando do / does.","sections":[{"h":"La idea: do y does son ayudantes","body":"En el presente simple, para **negar** y **preguntar** necesitas un verbo ayudante (*auxiliar*): **do** o **does**.\n\n- **do** va con I, you, we, they.\n- **does** va con he, she, it.\n\nLo más importante: cuando aparece **does**, la -s ya está en does. El verbo principal vuelve a su forma base: *She does not work*, no *She does not works*.\n\nLos tres momentos con **work**:\n\n- Pasado: **I didn't work** yesterday. (No trabajé ayer.)\n- Presente: **I don't work** on Sundays. (No trabajo los domingos.)\n- Futuro: **I won't work** tomorrow. (No trabajaré mañana.)"},{"h":"Negativo: don't / doesn't + verbo base","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Negativo","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["I","don't work","I don't work on Sundays.","No trabajo los domingos."],["you","don't work","You don't study at night.","Tú no estudias en la noche."],["he / she / it","doesn't work","She doesn't work here.","Ella no trabaja aquí."],["we","don't work","We don't work today.","No trabajamos hoy."],["they","don't work","They don't work in Orlando.","Ellos no trabajan en Orlando."]]},"note":"**don't** = do not y **doesn't** = does not. En conversación casi siempre se usa la forma corta."},{"h":"Preguntas de sí o no y respuestas cortas","body":"Para preguntar, pon **Do / Does** al inicio, luego el sujeto y el verbo base.\n\n**Do you like coffee?** (¿Te gusta el café?)\n\n**Does she work here?** (¿Ella trabaja aquí?)\n\nLa respuesta corta repite do / does: no repitas el verbo principal.","table":{"head":["Pregunta","Sí","No"],"rows":[["Do I work?","Yes, I do.","No, I don't."],["Do you work?","Yes, I do.","No, I don't."],["Does he / she / it work?","Yes, he does.","No, he doesn't."],["Do we work?","Yes, we do.","No, we don't."],["Do they work?","Yes, they do.","No, they don't."]]}},{"h":"Preguntas con Wh-: where, what, when, why, who","body":"Pon la palabra **Wh-** primero y después sigue la estructura normal: **Wh- + do / does + sujeto + verbo base**.","table":{"head":["Pregunta","Significa","Respuesta posible"],"rows":[["Where do you live?","¿Dónde vives?","I live in Medellín."],["What do you study?","¿Qué estudias?","I study engineering."],["When does class start?","¿Cuándo empieza la clase?","It starts at 8."],["Why does he study English?","¿Por qué él estudia inglés?","Because he wants to work at Disney."],["What time does she get up?","¿A qué hora se levanta ella?","She gets up at 6."],["How does he go to work?","¿Cómo va él al trabajo?","He goes by bus."]]},"note":"Ojo: **Who works here?** (¿Quién trabaja aquí?) no usa does, porque *who* es el sujeto. Aquí el verbo sí lleva -s."},{"h":"Adverbios de frecuencia y su posición","table":{"head":["Adverbio","Significa","Porcentaje aprox.","Ejemplo"],"rows":[["always","siempre","100%","I always drink coffee."],["usually","normalmente","80%","She usually walks to class."],["often","a menudo","60%","We often eat out."],["sometimes","a veces","40%","He sometimes works at night."],["never","nunca","0%","They never watch TV."]]},"body":"Posición: el adverbio va **antes del verbo principal** y **después de to be**.\n\n- I **always** study at night. (antes de study)\n- She **is** **never** late. (después de is)\n\nCon la negación: *I don't usually eat breakfast* (el adverbio va después de don't).\n\nNunca uses dos negaciones: *I never don't...* está mal. **never** ya es negativo.","note":"**Sometimes** también puede ir al inicio o al final de la oración: *Sometimes I work at night.*"},{"h":"How often...? ¿Con qué frecuencia?","body":"Para preguntar la frecuencia usa **How often + do / does + sujeto + verbo base?**\n\n**How often do you study English?** (¿Con qué frecuencia estudias inglés?)\n\nPuedes responder con un adverbio o con una expresión: **every day**, **once a week** (una vez por semana), **twice a week** (dos veces por semana), **three times a month**.\n\n**How often does she go to the gym?** She goes **twice a week**."},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["Mal: *She doesn't works.* Bien: **She doesn't work.** (does ya lleva la -s).","Mal: *Do she work here?* Bien: **Does she work here?**","Mal: *Where you live?* Bien: **Where do you live?** (en inglés la pregunta necesita do / does).","Mal: *Yes, I work.* como respuesta corta. Bien: **Yes, I do.**","Mal: *I no like coffee.* Bien: **I don't like coffee.**"]}],"vocab":[{"en":"don't (do not)","es":"no (con I, you, we, they)","ex":"I don't eat meat."},{"en":"doesn't (does not)","es":"no (con he, she, it)","ex":"He doesn't drink coffee."},{"en":"always","es":"siempre","ex":"I always get up at 6."},{"en":"usually","es":"normalmente","ex":"She usually walks to work."},{"en":"often","es":"a menudo","ex":"We often eat pizza."},{"en":"sometimes","es":"a veces","ex":"He sometimes studies at night."},{"en":"never","es":"nunca","ex":"They never arrive late."},{"en":"How often...?","es":"¿Con qué frecuencia...?","ex":"How often do you exercise?"},{"en":"once a week","es":"una vez por semana","ex":"I call my mother once a week."},{"en":"twice a week","es":"dos veces por semana","ex":"She goes to the gym twice a week."},{"en":"three times a month","es":"tres veces al mes","ex":"We visit my aunt three times a month."},{"en":"like","es":"gustar / querer","ex":"Do you like theme parks?"},{"en":"want","es":"querer","ex":"He wants to work at Disney."},{"en":"need","es":"necesitar","ex":"I need a visa."},{"en":"know","es":"saber / conocer","ex":"Do you know Orlando?"},{"en":"Where do you live?","es":"¿Dónde vives?","ex":"Where do you live? I live in Bogotá."},{"en":"What time...?","es":"¿A qué hora...?","ex":"What time does the park open?"},{"en":"Why...?","es":"¿Por qué...?","ex":"Why do you study English?"},{"en":"because","es":"porque","ex":"I study English because I want to travel."}],"examples":[{"en":"I don't work on Sundays.","es":"No trabajo los domingos."},{"en":"She doesn't live in Orlando.","es":"Ella no vive en Orlando."},{"en":"Do you study at night?","es":"¿Estudias en la noche?"},{"en":"Yes, I do. I study every night.","es":"Sí. Estudio todas las noches."},{"en":"Does he like theme parks?","es":"¿A él le gustan los parques temáticos?"},{"en":"No, he doesn't. He prefers museums.","es":"No. Él prefiere los museos."},{"en":"Where do they work?","es":"¿Dónde trabajan ellos?"},{"en":"What time does the park open?","es":"¿A qué hora abre el parque?"},{"en":"I always drink coffee in the morning.","es":"Siempre tomo café en la mañana."},{"en":"She is never late for class.","es":"Ella nunca llega tarde a clase."},{"en":"We usually don't eat breakfast at home.","es":"Normalmente no desayunamos en casa."},{"en":"How often do you practice English? Every day.","es":"¿Con qué frecuencia practicas inglés? Todos los días."},{"en":"He sometimes works on Saturdays.","es":"A veces él trabaja los sábados."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"She ___ work on Sundays.","options":["don't","doesn't","isn't"],"answer":1,"why":"She es tercera persona, entonces se usa doesn't."},{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ like cold coffee.","options":["don't","doesn't","no"],"answer":0,"why":"Con I se usa don't + verbo base."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ they live in Orlando?","options":["Does","Do","Is"],"answer":1,"why":"They va con Do."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ your brother play soccer?","options":["Do","Does","Is"],"answer":1,"why":"Your brother equivale a he, entonces se usa Does."},{"type":"choice","q":"He ___ eats breakfast. (nunca)","options":["never","don't","no"],"answer":0,"why":"Never es el adverbio de frecuencia que significa nunca y va antes del verbo."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál oración es correcta?","options":["She doesn't works here.","She doesn't work here.","She don't work here."],"answer":1,"why":"Después de doesn't el verbo vuelve a la forma base: work."},{"type":"choice","q":"Do you work here? Respuesta corta afirmativa:","options":["Yes, I do.","Yes, I work.","Yes, I does."],"answer":0,"why":"La respuesta corta repite do: Yes, I do."},{"type":"choice","q":"She is ___ late. (siempre)","options":["always","usually do","does"],"answer":0,"why":"Always va después del verbo to be (is)."},{"type":"fill","q":"He ___ drink coffee at night.","answer":["doesn't","does not"],"why":"He pide doesn't + verbo base."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ you study English every day?","answer":["do"],"why":"You va con Do."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ she live in Medellín?","answer":["does"],"why":"She va con Does."},{"type":"fill","q":"Does he like pizza? No, he ___.","answer":["doesn't","does not"],"why":"La respuesta corta negativa con he es doesn't."},{"type":"fill","q":"Where ___ you live?","answer":["do"],"why":"En preguntas Wh- con you se usa do."},{"type":"fill","q":"How ___ does she go to the gym? Twice a week.","answer":["often"],"why":"How often pregunta por la frecuencia."},{"type":"order","words":["don't","I","on","work","Sundays"],"answer":"I don't work on Sundays","es":"No trabajo los domingos."},{"type":"order","words":["Does","work","she","here"],"answer":"Does she work here","es":"¿Ella trabaja aquí?"},{"type":"order","words":["What","time","does","class","start"],"answer":"What time does class start","es":"¿A qué hora empieza la clase?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Él no vive en Orlando.","answer":["He doesn't live in Orlando.","He does not live in Orlando."],"why":"Con he se usa doesn't + verbo base."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Tú estudias inglés todos los días?","answer":["Do you study English every day?"],"why":"You pide Do al inicio de la pregunta."},{"type":"translate","es":"Yo siempre tomo café en la mañana.","answer":["I always drink coffee in the morning.","I always have coffee in the morning."],"why":"Always va antes del verbo principal."}],"speak":["I don't work on Sundays.","Do you like theme parks?","Yes, I do.","She doesn't live in Orlando.","Where do you live?","What time does the park open?","I always drink coffee in the morning.","How often do you study English?"],"tip":"Error típico: poner la -s dos veces (*She doesn't works*) o preguntar sin do / does (*Where you live?*). Recuerda: con do / does el verbo principal siempre va en forma base."},{"n":19,"block":"Verbos y tiempos","title":"Los verbos y sus cuatro formas","emoji":"🧩","minutes":40,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás leer una tabla de verbos y formar el pasado, el participio y el -ing de los verbos regulares.","sections":[{"h":"Cada verbo tiene cuatro formas","body":"En español un verbo tiene muchas terminaciones: trabajo, trabajé, trabajaré, trabajando. En inglés es más sencillo: cada verbo tiene solo **cuatro formas** y con ellas formas casi todos los tiempos.\n\n1. **Base form** (forma base): *work*. Se usa en presente con I / you / we / they y después de *will*, *don't*, *did*.\n2. **Past** (pasado): *worked*. Se usa para contar lo que pasó.\n3. **Past participle** (participio): *worked*. Se usa con *have* (tiempos perfectos) y en la voz pasiva.\n4. **-ing form** (gerundio): *working*. Se usa para acciones en progreso.\n\nLos tres momentos con **work**:\n\n- Pasado: **I worked** yesterday. (Trabajé ayer.)\n- Presente: **I work** every day. (Trabajo todos los días.)\n- Futuro: **I will work** tomorrow. (Trabajaré mañana.)"},{"h":"Cómo leer una tabla de verbos","body":"Las tablas de verbos tienen siempre este orden: **base → past → past participle → -ing**.\n\nSi el verbo es **regular**, el pasado y el participio son **iguales** y terminan en **-ed**. Si es **irregular**, cambian de otra forma (lo veremos en la próxima clase).","table":{"head":["Base","Past","Past participle","-ing","Significa"],"rows":[["work","worked","worked","working","trabajar"],["play","played","played","playing","jugar"],["go (irregular)","went","gone","going","ir"]]},"note":"La tabla muestra una columna para cada forma. Si el verbo es regular, la 2.ª y la 3.ª columna se ven iguales."},{"h":"Reglas para escribir -ed","table":{"head":["Regla","Base","Past (-ed)","Significa"],"rows":[["Casi todos: + ed","walk","walked","caminó"],["Termina en e: + d","live","lived","vivió"],["Consonante + y: y → ied","study","studied","estudió"],["Vocal + y: + ed","play","played","jugó"],["Una sílaba, consonante-vocal-consonante: dobla la última","stop","stopped","paró"],["Una sílaba, consonante-vocal-consonante: dobla la última","plan","planned","planeó"]]},"note":"No dobles la consonante si termina en **w, x, y** (*play → played*, *fix → fixed*) ni si el verbo tiene más de una sílaba con acento al inicio (*visit → visited*, *listen → listened*)."},{"h":"Reglas para escribir -ing","table":{"head":["Regla","Base","-ing","Significa"],"rows":[["Casi todos: + ing","work","working","trabajando"],["Termina en e: quita la e","live","living","viviendo"],["Termina en e: quita la e","use","using","usando"],["Consonante-vocal-consonante (una sílaba): dobla","stop","stopping","parando"],["Consonante-vocal-consonante (una sílaba): dobla","plan","planning","planeando"],["Termina en y: solo + ing","study","studying","estudiando"],["Termina en ie: ie → ying","lie","lying","mintiendo"]]}},{"h":"Tres sonidos para -ed","body":"Aunque se escribe igual (-ed), suena de tres formas. Es fácil de recordar:\n\n- **/t/**: después de sonidos sordos (p, k, f, s, sh, ch). *worked* (workt), *helped*, *watched*, *asked*, *finished*.\n- **/d/**: después de sonidos con vibración y vocales. *played* (pleid), *lived*, *called*, *cleaned*, *opened*, *used*.\n- **/ɪd/**: después de **t** o **d**. Aquí sí se agrega una sílaba. *wanted* (wan-tid), *needed*, *started*, *visited*, *waited*.","table":{"head":["Sonido","Cuándo","Ejemplos"],"rows":[["/t/","después de p, k, f, s, sh, ch","worked, walked, helped, watched, asked, finished"],["/d/","después de vocal o sonido con vibración","played, lived, called, cleaned, opened, used"],["/ɪd/","después de t o d (sílaba extra)","wanted, needed, started, visited, waited"]]},"note":"Truco: si el verbo ya termina en **t** o **d**, el -ed suena como una sílaba nueva. En los demás casos no se agrega sílaba."},{"h":"30 verbos regulares en tabla","table":{"head":["Base","Past","Past participle","-ing","Significa"],"rows":[["work","worked","worked","working","trabajar"],["play","played","played","playing","jugar"],["study","studied","studied","studying","estudiar"],["stop","stopped","stopped","stopping","parar"],["live","lived","lived","living","vivir"],["walk","walked","walked","walking","caminar"],["watch","watched","watched","watching","mirar"],["listen","listened","listened","listening","escuchar"],["cook","cooked","cooked","cooking","cocinar"],["clean","cleaned","cleaned","cleaning","limpiar"],["start","started","started","starting","empezar"],["finish","finished","finished","finishing","terminar"],["open","opened","opened","opening","abrir"],["close","closed","closed","closing","cerrar"],["call","called","called","calling","llamar"]]}},{"h":"30 verbos regulares: segunda parte","table":{"head":["Base","Past","Past participle","-ing","Significa"],"rows":[["help","helped","helped","helping","ayudar"],["want","wanted","wanted","wanting","querer"],["need","needed","needed","needing","necesitar"],["like","liked","liked","liking","gustar"],["love","loved","loved","loving","amar"],["use","used","used","using","usar"],["visit","visited","visited","visiting","visitar"],["arrive","arrived","arrived","arriving","llegar"],["plan","planned","planned","planning","planear"],["try","tried","tried","trying","intentar"],["ask","asked","asked","asking","preguntar"],["learn","learned","learned","learning","aprender"],["wait","waited","waited","waiting","esperar"],["stay","stayed","stayed","staying","quedarse"],["practice","practiced","practiced","practicing","practicar"]]},"note":"Error típico: confundir las formas. *I am work* está mal; **I am working**. *I work yesterday* está mal; **I worked yesterday**."}],"vocab":[{"en":"base form","es":"forma base","ex":"The base form of worked is work."},{"en":"past","es":"pasado","ex":"The past of play is played."},{"en":"past participle","es":"participio pasado","ex":"The past participle of walk is walked."},{"en":"-ing form","es":"forma en -ing (gerundio)","ex":"The -ing form of study is studying."},{"en":"regular verb","es":"verbo regular","ex":"Walk is a regular verb."},{"en":"irregular verb","es":"verbo irregular","ex":"Go is an irregular verb."},{"en":"work","es":"trabajar","ex":"I worked yesterday."},{"en":"play","es":"jugar / tocar","ex":"They played soccer."},{"en":"study","es":"estudiar","ex":"She studied last night."},{"en":"stop","es":"parar / detenerse","ex":"The bus stopped here."},{"en":"live","es":"vivir","ex":"I lived in Cali."},{"en":"walk","es":"caminar","ex":"We walked to the park."},{"en":"watch","es":"mirar / ver","ex":"He watched a movie."},{"en":"listen","es":"escuchar","ex":"I listened to music."},{"en":"cook","es":"cocinar","ex":"She cooked dinner."},{"en":"clean","es":"limpiar","ex":"We cleaned the room."},{"en":"start","es":"empezar","ex":"Class started at 8."},{"en":"finish","es":"terminar","ex":"I finished my homework."},{"en":"visit","es":"visitar","ex":"They visited Orlando."},{"en":"arrive","es":"llegar","ex":"The plane arrived at noon."},{"en":"plan","es":"planear","ex":"We planned the trip."},{"en":"try","es":"intentar","ex":"He tried again."}],"examples":[{"en":"I work in the morning.","es":"Trabajo en la mañana."},{"en":"I worked yesterday.","es":"Trabajé ayer."},{"en":"I am working now.","es":"Estoy trabajando ahora."},{"en":"She lived in Bogotá for two years.","es":"Ella vivió en Bogotá por dos años."},{"en":"He studied for the exam last night.","es":"Él estudió para el examen anoche."},{"en":"The bus stopped at the corner.","es":"El bus paró en la esquina."},{"en":"We are planning a trip to Orlando.","es":"Estamos planeando un viaje a Orlando."},{"en":"They walked to the university.","es":"Ellos caminaron a la universidad."},{"en":"I am studying English now.","es":"Estoy estudiando inglés ahora."},{"en":"The park opened at 9.","es":"El parque abrió a las 9."},{"en":"She is using her laptop.","es":"Ella está usando su computador."},{"en":"I arrived late, but I tried to be quiet.","es":"Llegué tarde, pero intenté hacer silencio."},{"en":"He wanted a job, so he visited the office.","es":"Él quería un trabajo, así que visitó la oficina."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el pasado de play?","options":["plaied","played","plad"],"answer":1,"why":"Vocal + y solo agrega -ed: played."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el pasado de study?","options":["studyed","studied","studdied"],"answer":1,"why":"Consonante + y: la y cambia a -ied."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el pasado de stop?","options":["stoped","stopped","stoppeed"],"answer":1,"why":"Verbo corto de consonante-vocal-consonante: se dobla la p."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el -ing de live?","options":["liveing","living","livving"],"answer":1,"why":"Si el verbo termina en e, se quita la e: living."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el -ing de plan?","options":["planing","planning","planeing"],"answer":1,"why":"Consonante-vocal-consonante: se dobla la n."},{"type":"choice","q":"En worked, el -ed suena como?","options":["/t/","/d/","/ɪd/"],"answer":0,"why":"Después de k (sonido sordo) el -ed suena /t/."},{"type":"choice","q":"En wanted, el -ed suena como?","options":["/t/","/d/","/ɪd/"],"answer":2,"why":"Después de t o d el -ed suena /ɪd/ y agrega una sílaba."},{"type":"choice","q":"En played, el -ed suena como?","options":["/t/","/d/","/ɪd/"],"answer":1,"why":"Después de una vocal el -ed suena /d/."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de walk: ___","answer":["walked"],"why":"Walk es regular: walk + ed."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de try: ___","answer":["tried"],"why":"Consonante + y cambia a -ied."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de arrive: ___","answer":["arrived"],"why":"Termina en e, solo agrega -d."},{"type":"fill","q":"-ing de use: ___","answer":["using"],"why":"Termina en e, quita la e y agrega -ing."},{"type":"fill","q":"-ing de study: ___","answer":["studying"],"why":"Con -ing la y se mantiene: studying."},{"type":"fill","q":"past participle de cook: ___","answer":["cooked"],"why":"En verbos regulares el participio es igual al pasado."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ in Cali for two years. (live, past)","answer":["lived"],"why":"Es un hecho pasado: live + d."},{"type":"order","words":["worked","I","yesterday"],"answer":"I worked yesterday","es":"Trabajé ayer."},{"type":"order","words":["am","I","now","studying"],"answer":"I am studying now","es":"Estoy estudiando ahora."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella caminó a la universidad.","answer":["She walked to the university.","She walked to university."],"why":"Walk es regular y el pasado es walked."},{"type":"translate","es":"Estoy trabajando ahora.","answer":["I am working now.","I'm working now."],"why":"Para acciones en progreso se usa am + verbo -ing."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ellos visitaron Orlando.","answer":["They visited Orlando."],"why":"Visit es regular y agrega -ed: visited."}],"speak":["I work every day.","I worked yesterday.","I am working now.","She lived in Bogotá.","He studied for the exam.","We walked to the park.","They visited Orlando.","I am planning a trip."],"tip":"Error típico: dar al pasado la forma del presente (*I walk yesterday*) o usar el infinitivo para una acción en progreso (*I am walk*). Revisa siempre la columna que necesitas: pasado, participio o -ing."},{"n":20,"block":"Verbos y tiempos","title":"Verbos irregulares: los 60 más comunes","emoji":"🔀","minutes":40,"goal":"Al final de esta clase conocerás 60 verbos irregulares con su pasado y participio, y tendrás trucos para memorizarlos por grupos.","sections":[{"h":"¿Qué es un verbo irregular?","body":"En la clase anterior viste que los verbos regulares forman el pasado con **-ed**. Los **irregulares** no siguen esa regla: cambian de forma y hay que aprenderlos.\n\nLa buena noticia: los irregulares son los más usados. Si aprendes estos 60, puedes contar casi cualquier cosa.\n\nLos tres momentos con **go**:\n\n- Pasado: **I went** to Orlando last year. (Fui a Orlando el año pasado.)\n- Presente: **I go** to class every day. (Voy a clase todos los días.)\n- Futuro: **I will go** to Disney next year. (Iré a Disney el próximo año.)\n\nLas tablas siguen el orden: **base → past → past participle → Spanish**."},{"h":"Tabla 1: los 15 más importantes","table":{"head":["Base","Past","Past participle","Significa"],"rows":[["be","was / were","been","ser / estar"],["have","had","had","tener"],["do","did","done","hacer"],["go","went","gone","ir"],["see","saw","seen","ver"],["eat","ate","eaten","comer"],["take","took","taken","tomar / llevar"],["make","made","made","hacer / fabricar"],["come","came","come","venir"],["get","got","got / gotten","conseguir / obtener"],["give","gave","given","dar"],["know","knew","known","saber / conocer"],["think","thought","thought","pensar"],["say","said","said","decir"],["tell","told","told","contar / decir a alguien"]]},"note":"**Be** es el más irregular: I **was**, you **were**, he / she / it **was**, we **were**, they **were**. En el participio: **been**."},{"h":"Tabla 2: verbos de la vida diaria","table":{"head":["Base","Past","Past participle","Significa"],"rows":[["buy","bought","bought","comprar"],["bring","brought","brought","traer"],["write","wrote","written","escribir"],["read","read","read","leer"],["speak","spoke","spoken","hablar"],["drink","drank","drunk","beber"],["drive","drove","driven","manejar"],["sleep","slept","slept","dormir"],["run","ran","run","correr"],["meet","met","met","conocer / encontrarse"],["leave","left","left","salir / dejar"],["pay","paid","paid","pagar"],["send","sent","sent","enviar"],["sit","sat","sat","sentarse"],["stand","stood","stood","estar de pie / pararse"]]},"note":"**Read** se escribe igual en las tres formas, pero el pasado suena **/red/** (como *red*, rojo). El presente suena /riid/."},{"h":"Tabla 3: más verbos útiles","table":{"head":["Base","Past","Past participle","Significa"],"rows":[["find","found","found","encontrar"],["keep","kept","kept","guardar / mantener"],["begin","began","begun","empezar"],["break","broke","broken","romper"],["build","built","built","construir"],["catch","caught","caught","atrapar / coger"],["choose","chose","chosen","elegir"],["cost","cost","cost","costar"],["cut","cut","cut","cortar"],["fall","fell","fallen","caer"],["feel","felt","felt","sentir"],["fly","flew","flown","volar"],["forget","forgot","forgotten","olvidar"],["hear","heard","heard","oír"],["hold","held","held","sostener"]]}},{"h":"Tabla 4: los últimos 15","table":{"head":["Base","Past","Past participle","Significa"],"rows":[["hurt","hurt","hurt","doler / lastimar"],["lose","lost","lost","perder"],["put","put","put","poner"],["sell","sold","sold","vender"],["sing","sang","sung","cantar"],["swim","swam","swum","nadar"],["teach","taught","taught","enseñar"],["wear","wore","worn","llevar puesto"],["win","won","won","ganar"],["understand","understood","understood","entender"],["wake","woke","woken","despertar"],["lend","lent","lent","prestar"],["let","let","let","dejar / permitir"],["draw","drew","drawn","dibujar"],["ride","rode","ridden","montar"]]}},{"h":"Trucos para memorizarlos por grupos","body":"No memorices 60 verbos sueltos. Agrúpalos por patrón:","table":{"head":["Patrón","Verbos","Idea"],"rows":[["Los tres iguales","put - put - put, cut - cut - cut, let - let - let, cost - cost - cost, hurt - hurt - hurt, read - read - read","No cambian nada"],["Pasado = participio (-ought / -aught)","buy - bought - bought, bring - brought - brought, think - thought - thought, catch - caught - caught, teach - taught - taught","Todos suenan parecido"],["Pasado = participio con -t","sleep - slept, keep - kept, feel - felt, leave - left, send - sent, lend - lent, build - built, spend - spent","Cambian a una -t final"],["i - a - u","sing - sang - sung, swim - swam - swum, drink - drank - drunk, begin - began - begun","Cambian las vocales: i, a, u"],["-ow / -ew / -own","know - knew - known, fly - flew - flown, draw - drew - drawn","El participio termina en -n"],["Participio con -en","take - took - taken, break - broke - broken, speak - spoke - spoken, choose - chose - chosen, wake - woke - woken, eat - ate - eaten, give - gave - given","El participio termina en -en"]]},"note":"Practica diciendo cada grupo en voz alta, como una canción: *buy, bought, bought; bring, brought, brought*."},{"h":"Error típico y cómo usarlos","body":"Un error común es aplicar -ed a un irregular: *I goed*, *I eated*, *I buyed*. Eso no existe. Son **went**, **ate**, **bought**.\n\nEl **pasado** (2.ª columna) se usa para contar lo que pasó: **I bought a ticket yesterday.**\n\nEl **participio** (3.ª columna) lo usarás más adelante con *have* (**I have seen** that movie). Por ahora, apréndelo junto al pasado."}],"vocab":[{"en":"go - went - gone","es":"ir","ex":"I went to Orlando last year."},{"en":"see - saw - seen","es":"ver","ex":"We saw a fireworks show."},{"en":"eat - ate - eaten","es":"comer","ex":"She ate pizza for lunch."},{"en":"take - took - taken","es":"tomar / llevar","ex":"I took a bus to the park."},{"en":"make - made - made","es":"hacer / fabricar","ex":"He made coffee."},{"en":"come - came - come","es":"venir","ex":"They came home late."},{"en":"get - got - got / gotten","es":"conseguir","ex":"She got a job at a hotel."},{"en":"give - gave - given","es":"dar","ex":"He gave me his phone number."},{"en":"know - knew - known","es":"saber / conocer","ex":"I knew the answer."},{"en":"think - thought - thought","es":"pensar","ex":"I thought it was easy."},{"en":"say - said - said","es":"decir","ex":"She said hello."},{"en":"tell - told - told","es":"contar / decir","ex":"He told me a story."},{"en":"buy - bought - bought","es":"comprar","ex":"I bought a ticket."},{"en":"bring - brought - brought","es":"traer","ex":"She brought her laptop."},{"en":"write - wrote - written","es":"escribir","ex":"I wrote an email."},{"en":"speak - spoke - spoken","es":"hablar","ex":"He spoke English with the guide."},{"en":"drink - drank - drunk","es":"beber","ex":"We drank coffee."},{"en":"sleep - slept - slept","es":"dormir","ex":"I slept eight hours."},{"en":"meet - met - met","es":"conocer / encontrarse","ex":"I met a friend at the airport."},{"en":"leave - left - left","es":"salir / dejar","ex":"The bus left at noon."},{"en":"pay - paid - paid","es":"pagar","ex":"He paid for dinner."},{"en":"send - sent - sent","es":"enviar","ex":"She sent me a message."}],"examples":[{"en":"I went to Orlando last year.","es":"Fui a Orlando el año pasado."},{"en":"I saw Mickey Mouse at the park.","es":"Vi a Mickey Mouse en el parque."},{"en":"We ate lunch at noon.","es":"Almorzamos al mediodía."},{"en":"She took the bus to work.","es":"Ella tomó el bus al trabajo."},{"en":"He bought two tickets.","es":"Él compró dos boletos."},{"en":"I wrote an email to the manager.","es":"Escribí un correo al gerente."},{"en":"They spoke English in the interview.","es":"Ellos hablaron inglés en la entrevista."},{"en":"I slept well last night.","es":"Dormí bien anoche."},{"en":"We met at the airport.","es":"Nos encontramos en el aeropuerto."},{"en":"The plane left at 9.","es":"El avión salió a las 9."},{"en":"She paid with her card.","es":"Ella pagó con su tarjeta."},{"en":"I was tired, but I was happy.","es":"Estaba cansado, pero estaba feliz."},{"en":"Yesterday I went out. Today I go to class. Tomorrow I will go home.","es":"Ayer salí. Hoy voy a clase. Mañana iré a casa."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"Pasado de go?","options":["goed","went","gone"],"answer":1,"why":"Go es irregular: go - went - gone. El pasado es went."},{"type":"choice","q":"Pasado de eat?","options":["eated","ate","eaten"],"answer":1,"why":"Eat - ate - eaten. El pasado es ate."},{"type":"choice","q":"Pasado de buy?","options":["buyed","boughted","bought"],"answer":2,"why":"Buy - bought - bought."},{"type":"choice","q":"Participio de write?","options":["wrote","written","writed"],"answer":1,"why":"Write - wrote - written. El participio es written."},{"type":"choice","q":"Pasado de see?","options":["saw","seen","seed"],"answer":0,"why":"See - saw - seen. El pasado es saw."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál de estos verbos NO cambia en pasado?","options":["put","take","sit"],"answer":0,"why":"Put - put - put no cambia en ninguna forma."},{"type":"choice","q":"Pasado de be con they?","options":["was","were","been"],"answer":1,"why":"They usa were en pasado."},{"type":"choice","q":"Pasado de think?","options":["thinked","thought","thinkt"],"answer":1,"why":"Think - thought - thought, igual que buy / bring."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de take: ___","answer":["took"],"why":"Take - took - taken."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de drink: ___","answer":["drank"],"why":"Drink - drank - drunk (patrón i - a - u)."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de sleep: ___","answer":["slept"],"why":"Sleep - slept - slept."},{"type":"fill","q":"past participle de speak: ___","answer":["spoken"],"why":"Speak - spoke - spoken."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de meet: ___","answer":["met"],"why":"Meet - met - met."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de leave: ___","answer":["left"],"why":"Leave - left - left."},{"type":"fill","q":"past de bring: ___","answer":["brought"],"why":"Bring - brought - brought."},{"type":"fill","q":"Yesterday I ___ a ticket. (buy, past)","answer":["bought"],"why":"Yesterday pide pasado: bought."},{"type":"order","words":["I","to","went","Orlando"],"answer":"I went to Orlando","es":"Fui a Orlando."},{"type":"order","words":["She","an","email","wrote"],"answer":"She wrote an email","es":"Ella escribió un correo."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ayer compré un boleto.","answer":["I bought a ticket yesterday.","Yesterday I bought a ticket."],"why":"Buy es irregular y el pasado es bought."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella vio a Mickey.","answer":["She saw Mickey."],"why":"El pasado de see es saw."}],"speak":["I went to Orlando.","I saw a big castle.","We ate lunch together.","She took a bus to work.","He bought a ticket.","They spoke English.","I slept eight hours.","I met a new friend."],"tip":"Error típico: poner -ed a todos los verbos (*I goed*, *I eated*, *I buyed*). Si el verbo es uno de los 60, usa la segunda columna de la tabla. Practica por grupos de patrones, no uno por uno."},{"n":21,"block":"Verbos y tiempos","title":"Pasado simple I: was / were y verbos regulares","emoji":"⏪","minutes":35,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir dónde estabas y contar qué hiciste usando was / were y los verbos regulares en pasado.","sections":[{"h":"Ideas clave: hablar del pasado","body":"El **pasado simple** (*simple past*) cuenta cosas que **empezaron y terminaron** en un momento del pasado: *ayer*, *la semana pasada*, *en 2020*.\n\nHay dos casos que veremos hoy:\n\n1. El verbo **to be**: en pasado es **was / were**.\n2. Los verbos **regulares**: base + **-ed**.\n\nLos tres momentos con **to be**:\n\n- Pasado: **I was** tired yesterday. (Estaba cansado ayer.)\n- Presente: **I am** tired now. (Estoy cansado ahora.)\n- Futuro: **I will be** tired tomorrow. (Estaré cansado mañana.)\n\nLos tres momentos con **work**:\n\n- Pasado: **I worked** on Monday. (Trabajé el lunes.)\n- Presente: **I work** every day. (Trabajo todos los días.)\n- Futuro: **I will work** next week. (Trabajaré la próxima semana.)"},{"h":"Was / were: conjugación completa","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Pasado de be","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["I","was","I was at home.","Estaba en casa."],["you","were","You were late.","Tú llegaste tarde / estabas tarde."],["he / she / it","was","She was at work.","Ella estaba en el trabajo."],["we","were","We were in Orlando.","Estuvimos en Orlando."],["they","were","They were happy.","Ellos estaban felices."]]},"note":"Dos formas, no más: **was** (I, he, she, it) y **were** (you, we, they)."},{"h":"Negativo y preguntas con was / were","body":"Para negar agrega **not**: **wasn't** (was not) y **weren't** (were not). Para preguntar, invierte el orden: **Was / Were + sujeto?**","table":{"head":["Tipo","Con was","Con were"],"rows":[["Afirmativo","She was at work.","They were at work."],["Negativo","She wasn't at work.","They weren't at work."],["Pregunta","Was she at work?","Were they at work?"],["Respuesta corta sí","Yes, she was.","Yes, they were."],["Respuesta corta no","No, she wasn't.","No, they weren't."],["Wh-","Where was she?","Where were they?"]]},"note":"Con was / were **no** se usa did: *Did you were late?* está mal. Es **Were you late?**"},{"h":"Verbos regulares: base + -ed","body":"Los verbos regulares usan **la misma forma para todas las personas**: no hay diferencia entre I, he o they.\n\n**I worked**, **you worked**, **she worked**, **we worked**, **they worked**.","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Pasado: work","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["I","worked","I worked yesterday.","Trabajé ayer."],["you","worked","You worked a lot.","Trabajaste mucho."],["he / she / it","worked","He worked at a hotel.","Él trabajó en un hotel."],["we","worked","We worked together.","Trabajamos juntos."],["they","worked","They worked last week.","Ellos trabajaron la semana pasada."]]},"note":"Recuerda las reglas: *live → lived*, *study → studied*, *stop → stopped*, *play → played*. Ya no existe la -s de la tercera persona en pasado."},{"h":"Expresiones de tiempo del pasado","table":{"head":["Expresión","Significa","Ejemplo","Traducción"],"rows":[["yesterday","ayer","I studied yesterday.","Estudié ayer."],["last night","anoche","We watched a movie last night.","Vimos una película anoche."],["last week","la semana pasada","She visited Orlando last week.","Ella visitó Orlando la semana pasada."],["last year","el año pasado","I started English last year.","Empecé inglés el año pasado."],["two days ago","hace dos días","They arrived two days ago.","Ellos llegaron hace dos días."],["in 2020","en 2020","He lived in Cali in 2020.","Él vivió en Cali en 2020."],["when I was a child","cuando era niño","I played soccer when I was a child.","Jugaba fútbol cuando era niño."]]},"note":"**Ago** va después del tiempo: *two days ago*. **Last** va antes: *last week*."},{"h":"Contar lo que hiciste","body":"Para contar un día completo combina los verbos en orden:\n\n*Yesterday I **got up** at 6. I **worked** in the morning. I **studied** English in the afternoon. I **watched** TV at night.*\n\nLos verbos irregulares como *get up* los veremos en la próxima clase.\n\nUsa conectores simples: **then** (luego), **after that** (después de eso), **and** (y), **but** (pero)."},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["Mal: *I was work yesterday.* Bien: **I worked yesterday.** (was no se mezcla con un verbo normal en pasado simple).","Mal: *She were at home.* Bien: **She was at home.**","Mal: *They was happy.* Bien: **They were happy.**","Mal: *I study yesterday.* Bien: **I studied yesterday.**","Mal: *Last year I am in Orlando.* Bien: **Last year I was in Orlando.**"]}],"vocab":[{"en":"was","es":"era / estaba / fue (I, he, she, it)","ex":"I was at home."},{"en":"were","es":"eras / estabas / fueron (you, we, they)","ex":"They were in Orlando."},{"en":"wasn't","es":"no era / no estaba","ex":"She wasn't tired."},{"en":"weren't","es":"no eran / no estaban","ex":"We weren't late."},{"en":"worked","es":"trabajó / trabajé","ex":"I worked in a store."},{"en":"studied","es":"estudió / estudié","ex":"He studied all night."},{"en":"visited","es":"visitó / visité","ex":"We visited a museum."},{"en":"watched","es":"miró / miré","ex":"I watched a movie."},{"en":"played","es":"jugó / jugué","ex":"They played cards."},{"en":"walked","es":"caminó / caminé","ex":"She walked home."},{"en":"cooked","es":"cocinó / cociné","ex":"I cooked pasta."},{"en":"cleaned","es":"limpió / limpié","ex":"He cleaned his room."},{"en":"arrived","es":"llegó / llegué","ex":"The bus arrived late."},{"en":"called","es":"llamó / llamé","ex":"My mother called me."},{"en":"yesterday","es":"ayer","ex":"I was busy yesterday."},{"en":"last night","es":"anoche","ex":"We studied last night."},{"en":"last week","es":"la semana pasada","ex":"I visited my aunt last week."},{"en":"two days ago","es":"hace dos días","ex":"She called two days ago."},{"en":"in 2020","es":"en 2020","ex":"I started school in 2020."},{"en":"then","es":"luego","ex":"I cooked, then I ate."}],"examples":[{"en":"I was at the university yesterday.","es":"Ayer estuve en la universidad."},{"en":"She was tired last night.","es":"Ella estaba cansada anoche."},{"en":"We were in Orlando last year.","es":"Estuvimos en Orlando el año pasado."},{"en":"They weren't at home.","es":"Ellos no estaban en casa."},{"en":"Were you at the party?","es":"¿Estuviste en la fiesta?"},{"en":"Where was he two days ago?","es":"¿Dónde estaba él hace dos días?"},{"en":"I worked in a store in 2020.","es":"Trabajé en una tienda en 2020."},{"en":"He studied English last night.","es":"Él estudió inglés anoche."},{"en":"We watched a movie and then we cooked dinner.","es":"Vimos una película y luego cocinamos la cena."},{"en":"My friend called me two days ago.","es":"Mi amigo me llamó hace dos días."},{"en":"They arrived at the airport at 9.","es":"Ellos llegaron al aeropuerto a las 9."},{"en":"I played soccer when I was a child.","es":"Jugaba fútbol cuando era niño."},{"en":"She visited her aunt last week.","es":"Ella visitó a su tía la semana pasada."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ at home yesterday.","options":["was","were","am"],"answer":0,"why":"I usa was en pasado."},{"type":"choice","q":"They ___ in Orlando last year.","options":["was","were","are"],"answer":1,"why":"They usa were en pasado."},{"type":"choice","q":"She ___ at work last night.","options":["wasn't","weren't","doesn't"],"answer":0,"why":"She va con was; en negativo es wasn't."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ you tired yesterday?","options":["Was","Were","Did"],"answer":1,"why":"You usa were, y con to be no se usa did."},{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ English two days ago.","options":["study","studied","studyed"],"answer":1,"why":"Study cambia la y por ied: studied."},{"type":"choice","q":"We ___ a movie last night.","options":["watch","watches","watched"],"answer":2,"why":"Last night pide pasado: watched."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál oración es correcta?","options":["She were happy.","She was happy.","She is happy yesterday."],"answer":1,"why":"She usa was."},{"type":"fill","q":"He ___ in Cali in 2020. (live, past)","answer":["lived"],"why":"Live termina en e, solo agrega -d."},{"type":"fill","q":"We ___ in Orlando last week. (be, past)","answer":["were"],"why":"We usa were."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ her mother yesterday. (call, past)","answer":["called"],"why":"Call es regular: called."},{"type":"fill","q":"They ___ at the party. (not be, past)","answer":["weren't","were not"],"why":"They usa were y en negativo weren't."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ soccer last Sunday. (play, past)","answer":["played"],"why":"Vocal + y solo agrega -ed: played."},{"type":"fill","q":"She arrived two days ___.","answer":["ago"],"why":"Hace dos días se dice two days ago."},{"type":"order","words":["was","I","yesterday","tired"],"answer":"I was tired yesterday","es":"Ayer estaba cansado."},{"type":"order","words":["Were","you","at","the","party"],"answer":"Were you at the party","es":"¿Estuviste en la fiesta?"},{"type":"order","words":["visited","She","Orlando","last","year"],"answer":"She visited Orlando last year","es":"Ella visitó Orlando el año pasado."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ellos estaban en casa.","answer":["They were at home.","They were home."],"why":"They usa were."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ayer estudié inglés.","answer":["I studied English yesterday.","Yesterday I studied English."],"why":"Study cambia a studied."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella no estaba cansada.","answer":["She wasn't tired.","She was not tired."],"why":"She usa was y en negativo wasn't."}],"speak":["I was at home yesterday.","We were in Orlando last year.","She wasn't tired.","Were you at the party?","I worked in a store in 2020.","He studied English last night.","They arrived two days ago.","I played soccer when I was a child."],"tip":"Error típico: usar presente con palabras de pasado (*I study yesterday*) o mezclar was con otro verbo (*I was study*). En pasado simple, un solo verbo en pasado: studied. Y con to be, was o were solos."},{"n":22,"block":"Verbos y tiempos","title":"Pasado simple II: irregulares, didn't y Did...?","emoji":"📖","minutes":40,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás negar, preguntar y contar una historia corta en pasado con verbos irregulares.","sections":[{"h":"Verbos irregulares en afirmativo","body":"En la clase 20 aprendiste las formas irregulares. Ahora las usas en frases. En afirmativo solo cambias el verbo a su forma de **pasado** (2.ª columna) y es **igual para todas las personas**.\n\nLos tres momentos con **go**:\n\n- Pasado: **I went** to Orlando. (Fui a Orlando.)\n- Presente: **I go** to Orlando. (Voy a Orlando.)\n- Futuro: **I will go** to Orlando. (Iré a Orlando.)","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Pasado: go","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["I","went","I went to the park.","Fui al parque."],["you","went","You went home early.","Tú fuiste a casa temprano."],["he / she / it","went","She went to work.","Ella fue al trabajo."],["we","went","We went to Disney.","Fuimos a Disney."],["they","went","They went by bus.","Ellos fueron en bus."]]},"note":"Ya no hay -s: en pasado he / she / it usa la misma forma que I."},{"h":"Negativo: didn't + verbo base","body":"Para negar en pasado (con cualquier verbo, regular o irregular) usa **didn't** (did not) + **verbo base**. Ojo: **el pasado se queda en didn't**, el verbo principal vuelve a la forma base.\n\n- Bien: **I didn't go** to class.\n- Mal: *I didn't went* to class.","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Negativo de eat","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["I","didn't eat","I didn't eat breakfast.","No desayuné."],["you","didn't eat","You didn't eat lunch.","No almorzaste."],["he / she / it","didn't eat","He didn't eat meat.","Él no comió carne."],["we","didn't eat","We didn't eat dinner.","No cenamos."],["they","didn't eat","They didn't eat pizza.","Ellos no comieron pizza."]]},"note":"Con **was / were** sigue siendo **wasn't / weren't**, sin did."},{"h":"Preguntas con Did... ? y respuestas cortas","body":"Para preguntar en pasado: **Did + sujeto + verbo base?** Igual que en la negación, el verbo vuelve a la base.\n\n**Did you go to Orlando?** (¿Fuiste a Orlando?)\n\n**Did she see the fireworks?** (¿Ella vio los fuegos artificiales?)","table":{"head":["Pregunta","Sí","No"],"rows":[["Did I go?","Yes, I did.","No, I didn't."],["Did you go?","Yes, I did.","No, I didn't."],["Did he / she / it go?","Yes, she did.","No, she didn't."],["Did we go?","Yes, we did.","No, we didn't."],["Did they go?","Yes, they did.","No, they didn't."]]},"note":"La respuesta corta usa **did**, no el verbo principal: *Yes, I did*, no *Yes, I went*."},{"h":"Preguntas con Wh- en pasado","body":"La estructura es: **Wh- + did + sujeto + verbo base?**","table":{"head":["Pregunta","Significa","Respuesta posible"],"rows":[["Where did you go?","¿Adónde fuiste?","I went to Orlando."],["What did you eat?","¿Qué comiste?","I ate a burger."],["When did she arrive?","¿Cuándo llegó ella?","She arrived yesterday."],["Who did you meet?","¿A quién conociste?","I met a new friend."],["Why did he leave?","¿Por qué se fue él?","Because he was tired."],["How did you get there?","¿Cómo llegaste allá?","I took a bus."],["What time did the movie start?","¿A qué hora empezó la película?","It started at 8."]]},"note":"Con **who** como sujeto no se usa did: **Who bought this?** (¿Quién compró esto?)."},{"h":"Tabla de los tres tiempos: go, buy y eat","table":{"head":["Verbo","Pasado","Presente","Futuro"],"rows":[["go","I went. (Fui.)","I go. (Voy.)","I will go. (Iré.)"],["buy","I bought. (Compré.)","I buy. (Compro.)","I will buy. (Compraré.)"],["eat","I ate. (Comí.)","I eat. (Como.)","I will eat. (Comeré.)"]]},"note":"La estructura negativa y la pregunta pasada siempre usan **didn't / Did** + verbo base."},{"h":"Cómo contar una historia corta","body":"Una historia en pasado sigue un orden. Usa estos conectores: **first** (primero), **then** (luego), **after that** (después de eso), **finally** (finalmente), **but** (pero), **so** (así que).\n\n*Last summer I went to Orlando. First, I bought a ticket for Magic Kingdom. Then I took a bus to the park. I saw a big castle and I ate ice cream. But it rained, so I didn't stay late. Finally, I came home and slept ten hours.*\n\nObserva: todos los verbos están en pasado y solo hay un **didn't** con el verbo base (**stay**)."},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["Mal: *I didn't went.* Bien: **I didn't go.**","Mal: *Did you went to class?* Bien: **Did you go to class?**","Mal: *Yes, I went* como respuesta corta. Bien: **Yes, I did.**","Mal: *I eated pizza.* Bien: **I ate pizza.**","Mal: *What you did yesterday?* Bien: **What did you do yesterday?**"]}],"vocab":[{"en":"went","es":"fui / fue / fueron","ex":"We went to the beach."},{"en":"saw","es":"vi / vio","ex":"I saw a movie."},{"en":"ate","es":"comí / comió","ex":"She ate a salad."},{"en":"took","es":"tomé / llevé","ex":"He took a taxi."},{"en":"made","es":"hice / hizo","ex":"I made a cake."},{"en":"came","es":"vine / vino","ex":"They came late."},{"en":"got","es":"conseguí / obtuve","ex":"I got a ticket."},{"en":"gave","es":"di / dio","ex":"She gave me a gift."},{"en":"had","es":"tuve / comí / tomé","ex":"We had lunch at noon."},{"en":"bought","es":"compré / compró","ex":"He bought a hat."},{"en":"wrote","es":"escribí / escribió","ex":"I wrote a letter."},{"en":"spoke","es":"hablé / habló","ex":"She spoke with the manager."},{"en":"slept","es":"dormí / durmió","ex":"We slept late."},{"en":"met","es":"conocí / encontré","ex":"I met a friend."},{"en":"left","es":"salí / dejé","ex":"They left early."},{"en":"didn't","es":"no (pasado)","ex":"I didn't see him."},{"en":"Did you...?","es":"¿Tú...? (pasado)","ex":"Did you eat breakfast?"},{"en":"first","es":"primero","ex":"First, I got up."},{"en":"then","es":"luego","ex":"Then I went to class."},{"en":"after that","es":"después de eso","ex":"After that, I had lunch."},{"en":"finally","es":"finalmente","ex":"Finally, I slept."},{"en":"so","es":"así que","ex":"It rained, so we stayed home."}],"examples":[{"en":"I went to Orlando last summer.","es":"Fui a Orlando el verano pasado."},{"en":"We saw the fireworks at night.","es":"Vimos los fuegos artificiales en la noche."},{"en":"She ate pizza for dinner.","es":"Ella comió pizza en la cena."},{"en":"I didn't sleep well last night.","es":"No dormí bien anoche."},{"en":"He didn't buy a ticket.","es":"Él no compró un boleto."},{"en":"Did you go to the airport?","es":"¿Fuiste al aeropuerto?"},{"en":"Yes, I did. I took a taxi.","es":"Sí. Tomé un taxi."},{"en":"Did they meet the manager?","es":"¿Ellos conocieron al gerente?"},{"en":"No, they didn't.","es":"No."},{"en":"Where did you eat lunch?","es":"¿Dónde almorzaste?"},{"en":"What did she buy at the store?","es":"¿Qué compró ella en la tienda?"},{"en":"Why did you leave early?","es":"¿Por qué te fuiste temprano?"},{"en":"First I wrote an email, then I called my mother.","es":"Primero escribí un correo, luego llamé a mi mamá."},{"en":"Finally, we came home and slept.","es":"Finalmente, volvimos a casa y dormimos."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ to the park yesterday.","options":["go","went","goed"],"answer":1,"why":"Yesterday pide pasado: went."},{"type":"choice","q":"She ___ pizza last night.","options":["eat","eated","ate"],"answer":2,"why":"El pasado irregular de eat es ate."},{"type":"choice","q":"I didn't ___ my keys.","options":["find","found","finded"],"answer":0,"why":"Después de didn't el verbo vuelve a la forma base: find."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ you see the show?","options":["Do","Did","Were"],"answer":1,"why":"Para preguntar en pasado se usa Did."},{"type":"choice","q":"Did she buy a ticket? Respuesta corta negativa:","options":["No, she didn't.","No, she didn't buy.","No, she don't."],"answer":0,"why":"La respuesta corta repite did: No, she didn't."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál oración es correcta?","options":["He didn't went.","He didn't go.","He no went."],"answer":1,"why":"Después de didn't va el verbo base: go."},{"type":"choice","q":"Where ___ you go last year?","options":["did","do","were"],"answer":0,"why":"Pregunta Wh- en pasado: Where did you go?"},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ a new friend yesterday. (meet, past)","answer":["met"],"why":"Meet - met - met."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ me a gift. (give, past)","answer":["gave"],"why":"Give - gave - given."},{"type":"fill","q":"We ___ lunch at noon. (have, past)","answer":["had"],"why":"Have - had - had."},{"type":"fill","q":"He didn't ___ the bus. (take)","answer":["take"],"why":"Después de didn't el verbo va en base."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ they arrive on time? Yes, they did.","answer":["did"],"why":"Pregunta en pasado con Did."},{"type":"fill","q":"What ___ you eat for dinner?","answer":["did"],"why":"Wh- + did + sujeto + verbo base."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ an email last night. (write, past)","answer":["wrote"],"why":"Write - wrote - written."},{"type":"order","words":["didn't","I","see","the","show"],"answer":"I didn't see the show","es":"No vi el espectáculo."},{"type":"order","words":["Did","you","eat","breakfast"],"answer":"Did you eat breakfast","es":"¿Desayunaste?"},{"type":"order","words":["Where","did","she","go"],"answer":"Where did she go","es":"¿Adónde fue ella?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Ayer compré un boleto.","answer":["I bought a ticket yesterday.","Yesterday I bought a ticket."],"why":"Buy es irregular: bought."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella no comió carne.","answer":["She didn't eat meat.","She did not eat meat."],"why":"Didn't + verbo base: eat."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Qué hiciste anoche?","answer":["What did you do last night?"],"why":"Wh- + did + sujeto + verbo base: do."}],"speak":["I went to Orlando last year.","I saw the castle.","I didn't sleep well.","Did you eat breakfast?","Yes, I did.","Where did you go yesterday?","What did you buy?","First I got up, then I went to class."],"tip":"Error típico: poner el pasado dos veces (*I didn't went*, *Did you went?*). Cuando aparece did / didn't, el pasado ya está ahí: el verbo principal vuelve a su forma base."},{"n":23,"block":"Verbos y tiempos","title":"Futuro: will y be going to","emoji":"🔮","minutes":35,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás hablar de tus planes y predicciones usando will y be going to, por ejemplo tu viaje a Orlando.","sections":[{"h":"El futuro tiene dos formas principales","body":"En inglés no existe una terminación de futuro como en español (*trabajaré*). Se forma con palabras auxiliares. Hay dos muy usadas:\n\n1. **will + verbo base**: decisiones del momento, promesas, predicciones.\n2. **be going to + verbo base**: planes que ya tienes, cosas que van a pasar.\n\nLos tres momentos con **work**:\n\n- Pasado: **I worked** last week. (Trabajé la semana pasada.)\n- Presente: **I work** every day. (Trabajo todos los días.)\n- Futuro: **I will work** tomorrow. / **I am going to work** tomorrow. (Trabajaré mañana.)"},{"h":"Will: conjugación y forma","body":"**Will** es igual para todas las personas. Después de will, el verbo va en forma base, sin -s.","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Futuro: will work","Forma corta","Significa"],"rows":[["I","will work","I'll work","Trabajaré"],["you","will work","you'll work","Trabajarás"],["he / she / it","will work","she'll work","Trabajará"],["we","will work","we'll work","Trabajaremos"],["they","will work","they'll work","Trabajarán"]]},"note":"Negativo: **will not** o **won't** (*I won't work*). Pregunta: **Will you work?** Respuesta corta: *Yes, I will.* / *No, I won't.*"},{"h":"Be going to: conjugación y forma","body":"Se forma con **am / is / are + going to + verbo base**. Aquí el verbo to be cambia según la persona.","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Futuro: be going to work","Forma corta","Significa"],"rows":[["I","am going to work","I'm going to work","Voy a trabajar"],["you","are going to work","you're going to work","Vas a trabajar"],["he / she / it","is going to work","she's going to work","Va a trabajar"],["we","are going to work","we're going to work","Vamos a trabajar"],["they","are going to work","they're going to work","Van a trabajar"]]},"note":"Negativo: *I'm not going to work*, *she isn't going to work*, *they aren't going to work*. Pregunta: **Are you going to work?** Respuesta corta: *Yes, I am.* / *No, I'm not.*"},{"h":"¿Cuándo uso will y cuándo be going to?","table":{"head":["Situación","Usa","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["Decisión en el momento","will","It's cold. I'll close the window.","Hace frío. Cerraré la ventana."],["Promesa u oferta","will","I'll help you with your homework.","Te ayudaré con la tarea."],["Predicción (opinión)","will","I think it will rain tomorrow.","Creo que lloverá mañana."],["Plan ya decidido","be going to","I'm going to study in Orlando next year.","Voy a estudiar en Orlando el próximo año."],["Prueba ahora de que algo pasará","be going to","Look at the clouds! It's going to rain.","¡Mira las nubes! Va a llover."]]},"note":"Regla fácil: si ya lo decidiste antes de hablar, usa **be going to**. Si lo decides mientras hablas, usa **will**."},{"h":"Expresiones de tiempo del futuro","table":{"head":["Expresión","Significa","Ejemplo","Traducción"],"rows":[["tomorrow","mañana","I'll call you tomorrow.","Te llamaré mañana."],["tonight","esta noche","We're going to eat out tonight.","Vamos a comer fuera esta noche."],["next week","la próxima semana","She'll arrive next week.","Ella llegará la próxima semana."],["next year","el próximo año","I'm going to work in Orlando next year.","Voy a trabajar en Orlando el próximo año."],["soon","pronto","I'll finish soon.","Terminaré pronto."],["in two months","dentro de dos meses","They'll travel in two months.","Ellos viajarán dentro de dos meses."],["in 2028","en 2028","He'll graduate in 2028.","Él se graduará en 2028."]]},"note":"**In** + tiempo = dentro de ese tiempo (futuro). **Ago** = hace ese tiempo (pasado)."},{"h":"Planes para Orlando","body":"Santiago quiere trabajar en Disney. Así podrías contar tus planes:\n\n*Next year I'm going to apply for a job at Disney. First, I'm going to study English every day. I'll practice speaking with my friends. In six months I'll take an English test. I think it will be difficult, but I'll try my best.*\n\nSi alguien te pregunta: **Are you going to travel to Orlando?** puedes responder: *Yes, I am. I'm going to leave in March.*"},{"h":"Errores típicos","list":["Mal: *I will to work.* Bien: **I will work.** (después de will no va to).","Mal: *She will works.* Bien: **She will work.** (sin -s).","Mal: *I going to study.* Bien: **I am going to study.** (falta el verbo to be).","Mal: *Tomorrow I work in Orlando* para un plan. Bien: **Tomorrow I'm going to work in Orlando.**","Mal: *Will you to go?* Bien: **Will you go?**"]}],"vocab":[{"en":"will","es":"futuro (decisión, promesa, predicción)","ex":"I will call you tomorrow."},{"en":"won't","es":"no (futuro)","ex":"I won't be late."},{"en":"be going to","es":"ir a (plan)","ex":"I am going to travel next year."},{"en":"tomorrow","es":"mañana","ex":"I'll study tomorrow."},{"en":"tonight","es":"esta noche","ex":"We're going to eat out tonight."},{"en":"next week","es":"la próxima semana","ex":"She will visit us next week."},{"en":"next year","es":"el próximo año","ex":"I'm going to live in Orlando next year."},{"en":"soon","es":"pronto","ex":"I'll see you soon."},{"en":"in two months","es":"dentro de dos meses","ex":"He will arrive in two months."},{"en":"apply for","es":"postularse a","ex":"I'm going to apply for a job."},{"en":"travel","es":"viajar","ex":"They will travel by plane."},{"en":"graduate","es":"graduarse","ex":"I'll graduate in 2028."},{"en":"visit","es":"visitar","ex":"We're going to visit Disney World."},{"en":"practice","es":"practicar","ex":"I'll practice English every day."},{"en":"help","es":"ayudar","ex":"I'll help you."},{"en":"rain","es":"llover","ex":"It's going to rain."},{"en":"I think","es":"creo que","ex":"I think it will be fun."},{"en":"maybe","es":"quizás","ex":"Maybe I'll go to Orlando."},{"en":"interview","es":"entrevista","ex":"I have an interview next week."},{"en":"visa","es":"visa","ex":"I'm going to ask for a visa."}],"examples":[{"en":"I will work tomorrow.","es":"Trabajaré mañana."},{"en":"I'm going to study in Orlando next year.","es":"Voy a estudiar en Orlando el próximo año."},{"en":"She'll call you tonight.","es":"Ella te llamará esta noche."},{"en":"They aren't going to travel in March.","es":"Ellos no van a viajar en marzo."},{"en":"I won't be late.","es":"No llegaré tarde."},{"en":"Will you help me with this email?","es":"¿Me ayudarás con este correo?"},{"en":"Yes, I will.","es":"Sí, te ayudaré."},{"en":"Are you going to apply for a job at Disney?","es":"¿Vas a postularte a un trabajo en Disney?"},{"en":"Yes, I am. I'm going to send my application soon.","es":"Sí. Voy a enviar mi solicitud pronto."},{"en":"I think it will be a great experience.","es":"Creo que será una gran experiencia."},{"en":"It's cold. I'll close the window.","es":"Hace frío. Cerraré la ventana."},{"en":"In two months I will take an English test.","es":"Dentro de dos meses haré un examen de inglés."},{"en":"When are you going to leave?","es":"¿Cuándo vas a salir?"},{"en":"Yesterday I studied. Today I study. Tomorrow I will study.","es":"Ayer estudié. Hoy estudio. Mañana estudiaré."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"She ___ call you tomorrow.","options":["will","wills","will to"],"answer":0,"why":"Will no cambia y después va el verbo base."},{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ going to study next year.","options":["am","is","will"],"answer":0,"why":"Con I se usa am: I am going to."},{"type":"choice","q":"They ___ going to travel in March.","options":["is","are","am"],"answer":1,"why":"They usa are."},{"type":"choice","q":"He ___ going to work in Orlando.","options":["are","am","is"],"answer":2,"why":"He usa is."},{"type":"choice","q":"It's cold. I ___ close the window. (decisión del momento)","options":["will","am going to","going"],"answer":0,"why":"Una decisión en el momento usa will."},{"type":"choice","q":"Look at those clouds! It ___ rain.","options":["will","is going to","going to"],"answer":1,"why":"Hay evidencia ahora, así que se usa be going to."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál oración es correcta?","options":["She will works.","She will work.","She will to work."],"answer":1,"why":"Después de will va el verbo base, sin -s ni to."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ be late. (negativo con will)","answer":["won't","will not"],"why":"Won't es la forma corta de will not."},{"type":"fill","q":"We ___ going to eat out tonight.","answer":["are","'re"],"why":"We usa are: We are going to."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ you help me? Yes, I will.","answer":["will"],"why":"Pregunta con will: Will you help me?"},{"type":"fill","q":"Are you going to travel? No, I'm ___.","answer":["not"],"why":"La respuesta corta negativa es No, I'm not."},{"type":"fill","q":"She is going ___ study English. (palabra que falta)","answer":["to"],"why":"La estructura es be going to + verbo."},{"type":"fill","q":"They will arrive ___ two months. (dentro de)","answer":["in"],"why":"In + tiempo indica dentro de ese tiempo."},{"type":"order","words":["will","I","tomorrow","call","you"],"answer":"I will call you tomorrow","es":"Te llamaré mañana."},{"type":"order","words":["going","I","to","am","travel"],"answer":"I am going to travel","es":"Voy a viajar."},{"type":"order","words":["Are","going","you","to","Orlando"],"answer":"Are you going to Orlando","es":"¿Vas a ir a Orlando?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Voy a trabajar en Orlando el próximo año.","answer":["I am going to work in Orlando next year.","I'm going to work in Orlando next year.","Next year I'm going to work in Orlando.","Next year I am going to work in Orlando."],"why":"Es un plan: be going to + verbo base."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella no llegará tarde.","answer":["She won't be late.","She will not be late.","She won't arrive late.","She will not arrive late."],"why":"El futuro negativo con will es won't."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Me ayudarás?","answer":["Will you help me?"],"why":"Para pedir ayuda se usa Will you + verbo base."}],"speak":["I will call you tomorrow.","I'm going to study English every day.","I'm going to work in Orlando next year.","She'll arrive soon.","I won't be late.","Are you going to travel in March?","Yes, I am.","I think it will be a great experience."],"tip":"Error típico: traducir 'voy a' como *I go to* (*I go to study*). En inglés es **I am going to study**. Y recuerda que después de will no se usa to ni -s: *I will go*, no *I will to go*."},{"n":24,"block":"Verbos y tiempos","title":"Presente continuo y resumen de tiempos","emoji":"🎬","minutes":40,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir qué estás haciendo ahora, distinguir presente simple de continuo y repasar pasado, presente y futuro.","sections":[{"h":"El presente continuo: lo que pasa ahora","body":"El **presente continuo** (*present continuous*) habla de lo que **está pasando ahora**, **hoy** o **en esta etapa de tu vida**.\n\nSe forma con **am / is / are + verbo con -ing**.\n\n**I am studying** English now. (Estoy estudiando inglés ahora.)\n\nPalabras típicas: **now** (ahora), **right now** (ahora mismo), **today** (hoy), **these days** (estos días), **at the moment** (en este momento).\n\nLos tres momentos con **work**:\n\n- Pasado: **I worked** yesterday. (Trabajé ayer.)\n- Presente: **I work** every day / **I am working** now. (Trabajo todos los días / Estoy trabajando ahora.)\n- Futuro: **I will work** tomorrow. (Trabajaré mañana.)"},{"h":"Conjugación completa: work","table":{"head":["Pronombre","Presente continuo","Forma corta","Significa"],"rows":[["I","am working","I'm working","Estoy trabajando"],["you","are working","you're working","Estás trabajando"],["he / she / it","is working","she's working","Está trabajando"],["we","are working","we're working","Estamos trabajando"],["they","are working","they're working","Están trabajando"]]},"note":"Negativo: *I'm not working*, *she isn't working*, *they aren't working*."},{"h":"Cómo escribir -ing","table":{"head":["Regla","Base","-ing","Significa"],"rows":[["Casi todos: + ing","work","working","trabajando"],["Casi todos: + ing","eat","eating","comiendo"],["Termina en e: quita la e","write","writing","escribiendo"],["Termina en e: quita la e","make","making","haciendo"],["Consonante-vocal-consonante (una sílaba): dobla","run","running","corriendo"],["Consonante-vocal-consonante (una sílaba): dobla","sit","sitting","sentándose"],["Termina en y: solo + ing","study","studying","estudiando"],["Termina en ie: ie → ying","lie","lying","mintiendo / acostado"]]},"note":"El verbo **go** hace **going**, y **have** hace **having**."},{"h":"Negativo y preguntas","body":"Con el presente continuo no usas do / does: el propio verbo **to be** hace todo el trabajo. Para preguntar, invierte **am / is / are** y el sujeto.","table":{"head":["Tipo","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["Afirmativo","She is studying.","Ella está estudiando."],["Negativo","She isn't studying.","Ella no está estudiando."],["Pregunta","Is she studying?","¿Ella está estudiando?"],["Respuesta corta sí","Yes, she is.","Sí."],["Respuesta corta no","No, she isn't.","No."],["Wh-","What are you doing?","¿Qué estás haciendo?"],["Wh-","Where is he working?","¿Dónde está trabajando él?"]]},"note":"Respuesta corta con I: *Yes, I am.* / *No, I'm not.* Nunca digas *No, I amn't*."},{"h":"Presente simple vs presente continuo","table":{"head":["","Presente simple","Presente continuo"],"rows":[["Idea","rutinas, hábitos, hechos","acciones ahora o temporales"],["Forma","I work / she works","I am working / she is working"],["Palabras clave","every day, always, usually, on Mondays","now, right now, today, these days, at the moment"],["Ejemplo 1","I study English every day.","I am studying English now."],["Ejemplo 2","She works in a hotel.","She is working at the hotel today."],["Pregunta","Do you work here?","Are you working now?"]]},"note":"Verbos de estado como **know**, **like**, **want**, **need**, **love** casi no se usan en continuo: se dice **I want** a coffee, no *I am wanting*."},{"h":"Resumen: pasado, presente y futuro con work, go y eat","table":{"head":["Verbo","Pasado simple","Presente simple","Presente continuo","Futuro con will","Futuro con going to"],"rows":[["work","I worked (trabajé)","I work (trabajo)","I am working (estoy trabajando)","I will work (trabajaré)","I am going to work (voy a trabajar)"],["go","I went (fui)","I go (voy)","I am going (estoy yendo)","I will go (iré)","I am going to go (voy a ir)"],["eat","I ate (comí)","I eat (como)","I am eating (estoy comiendo)","I will eat (comeré)","I am going to eat (voy a comer)"]]},"note":"Con he / she / it: she works, she is working, she will work, she is going to work, y en pasado she worked / went / ate."},{"h":"Negativo y pregunta en cada tiempo","table":{"head":["Tiempo","Negativo","Pregunta","Significa"],"rows":[["Pasado simple","I didn't eat.","Did you eat?","No comí. / ¿Comiste?"],["Presente simple","I don't eat. / She doesn't eat.","Do you eat? / Does she eat?","No como. / ¿Comes?"],["Presente continuo","I'm not eating.","Are you eating?","No estoy comiendo. / ¿Estás comiendo?"],["Futuro will","I won't eat.","Will you eat?","No comeré. / ¿Comerás?"],["Futuro going to","I'm not going to eat.","Are you going to eat?","No voy a comer. / ¿Vas a comer?"]]},"note":"Error típico: mezclar tiempos (*Yesterday I am eating*, *Tomorrow I ate*). Mira la palabra de tiempo y elige el tiempo que combina."}],"vocab":[{"en":"now","es":"ahora","ex":"I am studying now."},{"en":"right now","es":"ahora mismo","ex":"She is working right now."},{"en":"today","es":"hoy","ex":"I am working today."},{"en":"these days","es":"estos días","ex":"He is learning English these days."},{"en":"at the moment","es":"en este momento","ex":"They are eating at the moment."},{"en":"am / is / are","es":"forma de to be para el continuo","ex":"We are waiting for the bus."},{"en":"-ing","es":"terminación del continuo","ex":"I am reading."},{"en":"work","es":"trabajar","ex":"I am working at the hotel."},{"en":"go","es":"ir","ex":"They are going to the park."},{"en":"eat","es":"comer","ex":"We are eating lunch."},{"en":"study","es":"estudiar","ex":"He is studying for an exam."},{"en":"wait","es":"esperar","ex":"I am waiting for my friend."},{"en":"learn","es":"aprender","ex":"She is learning to drive."},{"en":"listen","es":"escuchar","ex":"He is listening to music."},{"en":"watch","es":"mirar","ex":"They are watching TV."},{"en":"cook","es":"cocinar","ex":"My mom is cooking dinner."},{"en":"rain","es":"llover","ex":"It is raining outside."},{"en":"talk","es":"hablar","ex":"She is talking on the phone."},{"en":"What are you doing?","es":"¿Qué estás haciendo?","ex":"What are you doing right now?"},{"en":"I'm not","es":"yo no estoy","ex":"I'm not working today."}],"examples":[{"en":"I am studying English now.","es":"Estoy estudiando inglés ahora."},{"en":"She is working at the hotel today.","es":"Ella está trabajando en el hotel hoy."},{"en":"They are eating lunch.","es":"Ellos están almorzando."},{"en":"We aren't going to class today.","es":"Hoy no vamos a ir a clase."},{"en":"Are you listening to music?","es":"¿Estás escuchando música?"},{"en":"Yes, I am.","es":"Sí."},{"en":"What is he doing?","es":"¿Qué está haciendo él?"},{"en":"He is cooking dinner.","es":"Él está cocinando la cena."},{"en":"It's raining outside.","es":"Está lloviendo afuera."},{"en":"I usually walk to class, but today I am taking a bus.","es":"Normalmente camino a clase, pero hoy estoy tomando un bus."},{"en":"She works in Orlando, but she isn't working today.","es":"Ella trabaja en Orlando, pero hoy no está trabajando."},{"en":"Yesterday I went to the mall. Now I am eating. Tomorrow I will go home.","es":"Ayer fui al centro comercial. Ahora estoy comiendo. Mañana iré a casa."},{"en":"I'm learning English these days because I'm going to work at Disney.","es":"Estos días estoy aprendiendo inglés porque voy a trabajar en Disney."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ studying now.","options":["am","is","do"],"answer":0,"why":"Con I el continuo usa am."},{"type":"choice","q":"She ___ working today.","options":["are","is","does"],"answer":1,"why":"She usa is."},{"type":"choice","q":"They ___ eating lunch right now.","options":["is","are","am"],"answer":1,"why":"They usa are."},{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ coffee every morning.","options":["drink","am drinking","drinking"],"answer":0,"why":"Every morning indica una rutina: presente simple."},{"type":"choice","q":"Look! It ___ right now.","options":["rains","is raining","rain"],"answer":1,"why":"Right now indica una acción en progreso: presente continuo."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el -ing de run?","options":["runing","running","runming"],"answer":1,"why":"Run es consonante-vocal-consonante corta: se dobla la n."},{"type":"choice","q":"¿Cuál es el -ing de write?","options":["writeing","writting","writing"],"answer":2,"why":"Termina en e: se quita la e y se agrega -ing."},{"type":"choice","q":"Yesterday I ___ to the mall.","options":["go","went","will go"],"answer":1,"why":"Yesterday pide pasado simple: went."},{"type":"fill","q":"He ___ cooking dinner now.","answer":["is","'s"],"why":"He usa is en el continuo."},{"type":"fill","q":"We ___ going to the park. (estamos yendo, am / is / are)","answer":["are","'re"],"why":"We usa are."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ working today. (negativo con is)","answer":["isn't","is not"],"why":"Negativo del continuo: isn't."},{"type":"fill","q":"Tomorrow I ___ go to class. (futuro con will)","answer":["will","'ll"],"why":"Tomorrow indica futuro; will + verbo base."},{"type":"fill","q":"Last night she ___ pizza. (eat, past)","answer":["ate"],"why":"Eat - ate - eaten."},{"type":"fill","q":"Are you studying? No, I'm ___.","answer":["not"],"why":"La respuesta corta negativa con I es I'm not."},{"type":"fill","q":"What are you ___? (do, -ing)","answer":["doing"],"why":"El -ing de do es doing."},{"type":"order","words":["am","I","English","studying","now"],"answer":"I am studying English now","es":"Estoy estudiando inglés ahora."},{"type":"order","words":["Is","working","she","today"],"answer":"Is she working today","es":"¿Ella está trabajando hoy?"},{"type":"order","words":["are","What","doing","you"],"answer":"What are you doing","es":"¿Qué estás haciendo?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Ellos están comiendo ahora.","answer":["They are eating now.","They're eating now."],"why":"They + are + eating."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella no está trabajando hoy.","answer":["She isn't working today.","She is not working today.","She's not working today."],"why":"Negativo del continuo: is not + verbo -ing."}],"speak":["I am studying English now.","She is working at the hotel today.","What are you doing right now?","They are eating lunch.","I usually walk to class, but today I am taking a bus.","Yesterday I went to the mall.","Tomorrow I will go home.","I'm learning English because I'm going to work at Disney."],"tip":"Error típico: usar el presente simple para lo que pasa ahora (*I study now*) o el continuo para rutinas (*I am studying every day*). Mira la palabra de tiempo: every day, always → simple; now, today, right now → continuo."},{"n":25,"block":"Para comunicarte","title":"Can, want, need y would like","emoji":"🙋","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás decir lo que sabes hacer, pedir permiso o ayuda con cortesía y expresar lo que quieres o necesitas, por ejemplo en un parque temático.","sections":[{"h":"Can: lo que puedes o sabes hacer","body":"**Can** significa *poder* o *saber hacer algo*. Es un verbo especial (modal): **no cambia** con he/she/it y después va el verbo en su forma base, **sin to**.\n\nSantiago puede decir **I can swim** (sé nadar) o **I can code** (sé programar). Y con tercera persona: **She can swim**, no *She cans*.","note":"Para decir que no puedes: **can't** (forma corta de cannot). I can't drive = No sé manejar / No puedo manejar."},{"h":"Afirmativo, negativo y pregunta","table":{"head":["Tipo","Estructura","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["Afirmativo","sujeto + can + verbo","I can help you.","Puedo ayudarte."],["Negativo","sujeto + can't + verbo","He can't swim.","Él no sabe nadar."],["Pregunta","Can + sujeto + verbo?","Can you speak English?","¿Hablas inglés?"],["Respuesta corta","Yes, I can. / No, I can't.","Yes, she can.","Sí, ella puede."]]},"note":"No uses do/does con can. Se dice Can you swim?, nunca Do you can swim?"},{"h":"Permiso y peticiones amables","body":"**Can I...?** sirve para pedir permiso: *Can I sit here?* (¿Puedo sentarme aquí?).\n\n**Can you...?** pide ayuda a otra persona: *Can you help me?*\n\n**Could** es más educado: **Could you...?** y **Could I...?** Úsalo con desconocidos, jefes o personal de un parque. *Could you open the door, please?* suena más amable que *Can you open the door?*. Agrega siempre **please**."},{"h":"Want, need y would like","table":{"head":["Expresión","Idea","Con sustantivo","Con verbo (to + verbo)"],"rows":[["want","querer","I want a ticket.","I want to go to Disney."],["need","necesitar","I need water.","I need to buy a ticket."],["would like","quisiera (educado)","I'd like a map.","I'd like to ask a question."]]},"note":"Con he/she/it: He wants, She needs. Pero would like no cambia: She would like a map."},{"h":"Ofrecer e invitar","body":"Para ofrecer ayuda: **Can I help you?** o **Would you like some water?**\n\nPara invitar: **Would you like to come with us?** o **Do you want to join us?**\n\nPara aceptar: **Yes, please. / I'd love to!** Para rechazar con amabilidad: **No, thank you. / Sorry, I can't.**","note":"Después de would you like va to + verbo (Would you like to sit?) o un sustantivo (Would you like a drink?)."},{"h":"Frases útiles en un parque temático","list":["Excuse me, where is the bathroom? (Disculpe, ¿dónde está el baño?)","Can I have a map, please? (¿Me da un mapa, por favor?)","Could you take a photo of us? (¿Podría tomarnos una foto?)","I need help, please. (Necesito ayuda, por favor.)","I'd like two tickets, please. (Quisiera dos boletos, por favor.)","Can I help you? How many people? (¿Puedo ayudarle? ¿Cuántas personas?)","You can't take food on this ride. (No puede subir comida a esta atracción.)","Would you like to wait here? (¿Le gustaría esperar aquí?)"]}],"vocab":[{"en":"can","es":"poder, saber","ex":"I can swim."},{"en":"can't","es":"no poder, no saber","ex":"I can't drive."},{"en":"could","es":"podría (más educado)","ex":"Could you help me, please?"},{"en":"want","es":"querer","ex":"I want a coffee."},{"en":"need","es":"necesitar","ex":"I need a map."},{"en":"would like","es":"quisiera, me gustaría","ex":"I would like some water."},{"en":"please","es":"por favor","ex":"Two tickets, please."},{"en":"help","es":"ayudar, ayuda","ex":"Can you help me?"},{"en":"ticket","es":"boleto, entrada","ex":"I need a ticket for the park."},{"en":"map","es":"mapa","ex":"Can I have a map?"},{"en":"ride","es":"atracción, paseo","ex":"I want to go on this ride."},{"en":"line","es":"fila","ex":"The line is very long."},{"en":"photo","es":"foto","ex":"Could you take a photo?"},{"en":"bathroom","es":"baño","ex":"Where is the bathroom?"},{"en":"ask","es":"preguntar, pedir","ex":"I'd like to ask a question."},{"en":"join","es":"unirse","ex":"Do you want to join us?"},{"en":"swim","es":"nadar","ex":"She can swim very well."},{"en":"drive","es":"manejar, conducir","ex":"My father can drive."},{"en":"sit","es":"sentarse","ex":"Can I sit here?"},{"en":"wait","es":"esperar","ex":"Please wait here."}],"examples":[{"en":"I can speak Spanish and a little English.","es":"Hablo español y un poco de inglés."},{"en":"She can't swim, but she can dance.","es":"Ella no sabe nadar, pero sabe bailar."},{"en":"Can you help me, please?","es":"¿Puedes ayudarme, por favor?"},{"en":"Could you repeat that, please?","es":"¿Podría repetir eso, por favor?"},{"en":"Can I sit here?","es":"¿Puedo sentarme aquí?"},{"en":"I want to work at Disney next year.","es":"Quiero trabajar en Disney el próximo año."},{"en":"I need to study more English.","es":"Necesito estudiar más inglés."},{"en":"He wants a hot dog and a soda.","es":"Él quiere un perro caliente y una gaseosa."},{"en":"I would like two tickets for today.","es":"Quisiera dos boletos para hoy."},{"en":"Would you like some water?","es":"¿Quieres un poco de agua?"},{"en":"Would you like to take a photo with us?","es":"¿Te gustaría tomarte una foto con nosotros?"},{"en":"Sorry, I can't. I have class tonight.","es":"Lo siento, no puedo. Tengo clase esta noche."},{"en":"Excuse me, can I have a map of the park?","es":"Disculpe, ¿me da un mapa del parque?"},{"en":"We need to wait in line for one hour.","es":"Necesitamos esperar en la fila una hora."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"My sister ___ swim very well.","options":["can","cans","can to"],"answer":0,"why":"Can no cambia con she y no lleva to después."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["Do you can drive?","Can you drive?","You can drive?"],"answer":1,"why":"Con can la pregunta se forma invirtiendo: Can you drive?"},{"type":"choice","q":"You are at a theme park. You ask a worker politely. You say: ___ you tell me where the bathroom is?","options":["Could","Do","Are"],"answer":0,"why":"Could you... es una petición educada, ideal para el personal."},{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ a ticket for the park.","options":["needs","need","needing"],"answer":1,"why":"Con I se usa need sin -s."},{"type":"choice","q":"He ___ to work at Disney.","options":["want","wants","wanting"],"answer":1,"why":"Con he/she/it, want lleva -s: wants."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which is the most polite way to order?","options":["I want a coffee.","Give me a coffee.","I would like a coffee, please."],"answer":2,"why":"I would like ... please es la forma más cortés."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ speak Spanish and English. (puedo)","answer":["can"],"why":"Para habilidad se usa can."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ drive, so she takes the bus. (no sabe)","answer":["can't","cannot","can not"],"why":"La forma negativa de can es can't o cannot."},{"type":"fill","q":"I need ___ buy a ticket.","answer":["to"],"why":"Need + to + verbo."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ you like some water? (oferta)","answer":["would"],"why":"Would you like...? es la forma educada de ofrecer."},{"type":"fill","q":"My brother ___ a new phone. (wants)","answer":["wants"],"why":"Con he/she/it, want lleva -s."},{"type":"order","words":["help","Can","you","me"],"answer":"Can you help me","es":"¿Puedes ayudarme?"},{"type":"order","words":["like","I","two","would","tickets"],"answer":"I would like two tickets","es":"Quisiera dos boletos."},{"type":"order","words":["can't","swim","He"],"answer":"He can't swim","es":"Él no sabe nadar."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Puedo sentarme aquí?","answer":["Can I sit here?","Could I sit here?"],"why":"Para pedir permiso se usa Can I...? o Could I...?"},{"type":"translate","es":"Necesito un mapa.","answer":["I need a map.","I need a map"],"why":"Need + sustantivo, sin to."},{"type":"translate","es":"Quiero ir a Orlando.","answer":["I want to go to Orlando.","I want to go to Orlando"],"why":"Want + to + verbo."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Quieres un poco de agua?","answer":["Would you like some water?","Do you want some water?","Would you like water?","Do you want water?"],"why":"Para ofrecer se usa Would you like...? o Do you want...?"}],"speak":["I can speak Spanish and a little English.","Can I have a map, please?","Could you help me, please?","I would like two tickets for today.","I want to work at Disney next year.","I need to practice my English every day.","Would you like some water?","Sorry, I can't, but thank you."],"tip":"Los hispanohablantes dicen a veces *Do you can swim?* o *She cans*. Recuerda: can nunca usa do/does ni lleva -s, y el verbo siguiente va sin to: Can you swim? / She can swim."},{"n":26,"block":"Para comunicarte","title":"Palabras de pregunta","emoji":"❓","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás hacer preguntas con what, where, when, why, who, which, whose y how, y mantener una conversación básica.","sections":[{"h":"Las palabras de pregunta","table":{"head":["Palabra","Pregunta por...","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["what","cosas (qué)","What is your name?","¿Cuál es tu nombre?"],["where","lugar (dónde)","Where do you live?","¿Dónde vives?"],["when","tiempo (cuándo)","When is the class?","¿Cuándo es la clase?"],["why","razón (por qué)","Why are you here?","¿Por qué estás aquí?"],["who","personas (quién)","Who is that man?","¿Quién es ese hombre?"],["which","elegir entre opciones (cuál)","Which bus is yours?","¿Cuál bus es el tuyo?"],["whose","posesión (de quién)","Whose bag is this?","¿De quién es esta mochila?"],["how","manera (cómo)","How are you?","¿Cómo estás?"]]},"note":"La palabra de pregunta va siempre al principio de la frase."},{"h":"Preguntas con to be","body":"Con **to be** (am/is/are/was/were) la estructura es sencilla: **palabra de pregunta + to be + sujeto**.\n\n**Where are you from?** (¿De dónde eres?) **What is your job?** (¿Cuál es tu trabajo?) **Why is she sad?** (¿Por qué está triste?)\n\nNo se necesita do/does con to be."},{"h":"Preguntas con do, does y did","table":{"head":["Tiempo","Estructura","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["Presente (I, you, we, they)","palabra + do + sujeto + verbo","Where do you work?","¿Dónde trabajas?"],["Presente (he, she, it)","palabra + does + sujeto + verbo","What does she study?","¿Qué estudia ella?"],["Pasado","palabra + did + sujeto + verbo","When did you arrive?","¿Cuándo llegaste?"]]},"note":"Después de do, does y did el verbo va en forma base, sin -s ni -ed: Where does he live? (no Where does he lives?). Where did you go? (no Where did you went?)."},{"h":"How + adjetivo o palabra","table":{"head":["Expresión","Pregunta por...","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["how much","precio o cantidad (no contable)","How much is the ticket?","¿Cuánto cuesta el boleto?"],["how many","cantidad (contable)","How many brothers do you have?","¿Cuántos hermanos tienes?"],["how old","edad","How old are you?","¿Cuántos años tienes?"],["how long","duración","How long is the flight?","¿Cuánto dura el vuelo?"],["how often","frecuencia","How often do you study?","¿Con qué frecuencia estudias?"]]}},{"h":"Preguntas típicas de conversación","list":["What is your name? / My name is Santiago.","Where do you live? / I live in Medellín.","Where are you from? / I'm from Colombia.","What do you do? / I'm a student.","Why are you learning English? / Because I want to work at Disney.","When did you start? / I started in January.","How old are you? / I'm 20 years old.","Who is your favorite singer? / My favorite singer is Shakira.","Which food do you like, pizza or pasta? / I like pizza."],"note":"Practica respondiendo en voz alta con frases completas."}],"vocab":[{"en":"what","es":"qué, cuál","ex":"What time is it?"},{"en":"where","es":"dónde","ex":"Where is the hotel?"},{"en":"when","es":"cuándo","ex":"When is your birthday?"},{"en":"why","es":"por qué","ex":"Why are you late?"},{"en":"because","es":"porque","ex":"Because I missed the bus."},{"en":"who","es":"quién","ex":"Who is your teacher?"},{"en":"which","es":"cuál","ex":"Which book do you want?"},{"en":"whose","es":"de quién","ex":"Whose phone is this?"},{"en":"how","es":"cómo","ex":"How do you say this in English?"},{"en":"how much","es":"cuánto (precio)","ex":"How much is this shirt?"},{"en":"how many","es":"cuántos","ex":"How many people are in your family?"},{"en":"how old","es":"qué edad","ex":"How old is your brother?"},{"en":"how long","es":"cuánto tiempo","ex":"How long is the class?"},{"en":"how often","es":"con qué frecuencia","ex":"How often do you exercise?"},{"en":"live","es":"vivir","ex":"I live in Bogotá."},{"en":"learn","es":"aprender","ex":"I learn English online."},{"en":"start","es":"empezar","ex":"When does the class start?"},{"en":"arrive","es":"llegar","ex":"When did you arrive?"},{"en":"price","es":"precio","ex":"What is the price?"},{"en":"flight","es":"vuelo","ex":"The flight is four hours long."}],"examples":[{"en":"What is your name?","es":"¿Cuál es tu nombre?"},{"en":"Where do you live?","es":"¿Dónde vives?"},{"en":"When does your class start?","es":"¿Cuándo empieza tu clase?"},{"en":"Why are you learning English?","es":"¿Por qué estás aprendiendo inglés?"},{"en":"Who is your best friend?","es":"¿Quién es tu mejor amigo?"},{"en":"Which color do you like, red or blue?","es":"¿Qué color te gusta, rojo o azul?"},{"en":"Whose jacket is this?","es":"¿De quién es esta chaqueta?"},{"en":"How do you go to the university?","es":"¿Cómo vas a la universidad?"},{"en":"How much is a ticket to Disney World?","es":"¿Cuánto cuesta un boleto para Disney World?"},{"en":"How many classes do you have today?","es":"¿Cuántas clases tienes hoy?"},{"en":"How old is your mother?","es":"¿Cuántos años tiene tu mamá?"},{"en":"How long is the flight to Orlando?","es":"¿Cuánto dura el vuelo a Orlando?"},{"en":"How often do you practice English?","es":"¿Con qué frecuencia practicas inglés?"},{"en":"Where did you go last weekend?","es":"¿A dónde fuiste el fin de semana pasado?"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"___ do you live? In Medellín.","options":["What","Where","Who"],"answer":1,"why":"Responde un lugar, así que se pregunta con where."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ is your birthday? In March.","options":["When","Why","Which"],"answer":0,"why":"In March es un momento en el tiempo: when."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ are you studying English? Because I want to travel.","options":["How","Who","Why"],"answer":2,"why":"Because responde a why."},{"type":"choice","q":"___ bag is this? It's Ana's.","options":["Who","Whose","Which"],"answer":1,"why":"Whose pregunta por el dueño de algo."},{"type":"choice","q":"Where ___ she work?","options":["do","does","is"],"answer":1,"why":"Con she en presente se usa does."},{"type":"choice","q":"How ___ brothers do you have?","options":["much","many","old"],"answer":1,"why":"Brothers es contable, así que how many."},{"type":"choice","q":"When ___ you arrive?","options":["do","does","did"],"answer":2,"why":"Arrive en pasado se pregunta con did."},{"type":"fill","q":"___ is your name? (qué)","answer":["what"],"why":"Para preguntar el nombre se usa what."},{"type":"fill","q":"How ___ are you? I'm 20.","answer":["old"],"why":"How old pregunta por la edad."},{"type":"fill","q":"How ___ is the ticket? Fifty dollars.","answer":["much"],"why":"How much pregunta por el precio."},{"type":"fill","q":"What ___ he study? (does/do)","answer":["does"],"why":"He pide does en presente."},{"type":"fill","q":"Where did you ___ yesterday? (go)","answer":["go"],"why":"Después de did el verbo va en forma base."},{"type":"order","words":["you","do","Where","live"],"answer":"Where do you live","es":"¿Dónde vives?"},{"type":"order","words":["is","How","ticket","much","the"],"answer":"How much is the ticket","es":"¿Cuánto cuesta el boleto?"},{"type":"order","words":["learning","you","English","Why","are"],"answer":"Why are you learning English","es":"¿Por qué estás aprendiendo inglés?"},{"type":"translate","es":"¿De dónde eres?","answer":["Where are you from?"],"why":"Where are you from? es la pregunta estándar de origen."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Cuántos años tienes?","answer":["How old are you?"],"why":"En inglés se usa to be: how old are you."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Quién es tu profesor?","answer":["Who is your teacher?","Who's your teacher?"],"why":"Who pregunta por personas."},{"type":"translate","es":"¿Con qué frecuencia estudias?","answer":["How often do you study?"],"why":"How often pregunta por la frecuencia y con you usa do."}],"speak":["What is your name?","Where do you live?","Why are you learning English?","How old are you?","How much is a ticket to Orlando?","When does the class start?","Who is your favorite singer?","How often do you practice English?"],"tip":"En español no necesitas ayuda para preguntar (¿Dónde vives?), pero en inglés casi siempre hace falta do/does/did. Error común: *Where you live?* o *Where does he lives?*. Correcto: Where do you live? / Where does he live?"},{"n":27,"block":"Para comunicarte","title":"Tiempo y conectores","emoji":"🔗","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás usar in, on y at para el tiempo y unir ideas con and, but, or, because, so y then para hablar con frases más largas.","sections":[{"h":"In, on y at con el tiempo","table":{"head":["Preposición","Se usa con...","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["in","meses, años, estaciones, partes del día","in May, in 2027, in summer, in the morning","en mayo, en 2027, en verano, en la mañana"],["on","días y fechas","on Monday, on July 4th, on my birthday","el lunes, el 4 de julio, en mi cumpleaños"],["at","horas y momentos exactos","at 5 pm, at noon, at night","a las 5 pm, al mediodía, en la noche"]]},"note":"Se dice in the morning/afternoon/evening, pero at night. Y atención: on the weekend (EE. UU.) o at the weekend (Reino Unido)."},{"h":"From... to, before, after y during","body":"**From ... to ...** marca el inicio y el final: *I work from 9 to 5.* (Trabajo de 9 a 5).\n\n**Before** = antes de. *I study before class.* **After** = después de. *I eat after work.*\n\n**During** = durante. *I sleep during the flight.* Se usa con un sustantivo (during the class), no con un verbo."},{"h":"For y since (lo básico)","table":{"head":["Palabra","Idea","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["for","cuánto tiempo dura algo","I study English for one hour.","Estudio inglés durante una hora."],["for","periodo de tiempo","She has lived here for two years.","Ella ha vivido aquí por dos años."],["since","desde cuándo empezó","I have studied English since January.","Estudio inglés desde enero."]]},"note":"For va con una duración (two hours, three days). Since va con un punto de inicio (Monday, 2020, January). Con for y since se usa have/has + participio (I have lived, she has studied). Por ahora solo memoriza esa forma."},{"h":"Conectores para unir ideas","table":{"head":["Conector","Función","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["and","suma ideas","I study and I work.","Estudio y trabajo."],["but","contraste","I like pizza, but I don't like cheese.","Me gusta la pizza, pero no el queso."],["or","opción","Do you want coffee or tea?","¿Quieres café o té?"],["because","da la razón","I study English because I want to work in Orlando.","Estudio inglés porque quiero trabajar en Orlando."],["so","da el resultado","I was tired, so I went to bed.","Estaba cansado, así que me fui a dormir."]]},"note":"Because responde a why y so muestra el resultado. Compara: I stayed home because I was sick. / I was sick, so I stayed home."},{"h":"First, next, then y finally","body":"Para contar pasos o una rutina usa estas palabras en orden: **First, ... Next, ... Then, ... Finally, ...**\n\n*First, I wake up at 6. Then I take a shower. Next, I have breakfast. Finally, I go to the university.*\n\nSe ponen al principio de la frase y llevan coma."},{"h":"Construyendo frases más largas","body":"Empieza con una frase simple y agrégale información paso a paso.\n\n1. I study English.\n2. I study English every day.\n3. I study English every day because I want to work at Disney.\n4. I study English every day because I want to work at Disney, so I practice at night and on weekends.\n\nAsí, con conectores, tu inglés suena mucho más natural."}],"vocab":[{"en":"in","es":"en (meses, años)","ex":"My birthday is in May."},{"en":"on","es":"en (días)","ex":"I have class on Monday."},{"en":"at","es":"a (hora)","ex":"The class starts at 5 pm."},{"en":"from","es":"desde, de","ex":"I work from 9 to 5."},{"en":"before","es":"antes de","ex":"I eat breakfast before class."},{"en":"after","es":"después de","ex":"I rest after work."},{"en":"during","es":"durante","ex":"I listen to music during the trip."},{"en":"for","es":"durante, por","ex":"I wait for ten minutes."},{"en":"since","es":"desde","ex":"I have lived here since 2020."},{"en":"and","es":"y","ex":"I like music and movies."},{"en":"but","es":"pero","ex":"I'm tired, but happy."},{"en":"or","es":"o","ex":"Tea or coffee?"},{"en":"because","es":"porque","ex":"I'm happy because it's Friday."},{"en":"so","es":"así que, entonces","ex":"It's late, so I go home."},{"en":"then","es":"luego, entonces","ex":"I eat, then I study."},{"en":"first","es":"primero","ex":"First, open the app."},{"en":"next","es":"después, a continuación","ex":"Next, choose your ticket."},{"en":"finally","es":"finalmente","ex":"Finally, I arrive home."},{"en":"morning","es":"mañana","ex":"I study in the morning."},{"en":"weekend","es":"fin de semana","ex":"I rest on the weekend."}],"examples":[{"en":"My birthday is in October.","es":"Mi cumpleaños es en octubre."},{"en":"I have class on Tuesday.","es":"Tengo clase el martes."},{"en":"The park opens at 9 am.","es":"El parque abre a las 9 am."},{"en":"I work from Monday to Friday.","es":"Trabajo de lunes a viernes."},{"en":"I brush my teeth before bed.","es":"Me cepillo los dientes antes de acostarme."},{"en":"We eat dinner after the movie.","es":"Cenamos después de la película."},{"en":"I sleep during the flight.","es":"Duermo durante el vuelo."},{"en":"I study English for two hours every day.","es":"Estudio inglés dos horas cada día."},{"en":"I have studied English since January.","es":"Estudio inglés desde enero."},{"en":"I like coffee, but I don't like tea.","es":"Me gusta el café, pero no el té."},{"en":"Do you want to walk or take the bus?","es":"¿Quieres caminar o tomar el bus?"},{"en":"I'm learning English because I want to travel.","es":"Estoy aprendiendo inglés porque quiero viajar."},{"en":"It was raining, so we stayed home.","es":"Estaba lloviendo, así que nos quedamos en casa."},{"en":"First, buy a ticket. Then, go to the gate.","es":"Primero, compra un boleto. Luego, ve a la puerta."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"My birthday is ___ June.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":0,"why":"Los meses van con in."},{"type":"choice","q":"I have class ___ Wednesday.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":1,"why":"Los días de la semana van con on."},{"type":"choice","q":"The movie starts ___ 8 pm.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":2,"why":"Las horas exactas van con at."},{"type":"choice","q":"I study ___ the morning.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":0,"why":"In the morning es una expresión fija."},{"type":"choice","q":"I'm tired ___ I worked all day.","options":["because","so","but"],"answer":0,"why":"Because da la razón del cansancio."},{"type":"choice","q":"It's late, ___ I go to bed.","options":["because","so","or"],"answer":1,"why":"So presenta el resultado."},{"type":"choice","q":"I have lived here ___ 2022.","options":["for","since","during"],"answer":1,"why":"2022 es un punto de inicio, por eso since."},{"type":"fill","q":"I eat dinner ___ night. (at)","answer":["at"],"why":"At night es una expresión fija."},{"type":"fill","q":"I like tea ___ I don't like coffee.","answer":["but"],"why":"But marca contraste."},{"type":"fill","q":"Do you want a taxi ___ a bus?","answer":["or"],"why":"Or presenta una opción."},{"type":"fill","q":"I wait for the bus ___ ten minutes.","answer":["for"],"why":"Ten minutes es una duración: for."},{"type":"fill","q":"___, I wake up. Then I take a shower.","answer":["first"],"why":"First indica el primer paso."},{"type":"order","words":["on","have","I","class","Monday"],"answer":"I have class on Monday","es":"Tengo clase el lunes."},{"type":"order","words":["from","work","I","9","to","5"],"answer":"I work from 9 to 5","es":"Trabajo de 9 a 5."},{"type":"order","words":["I","study","because","want","I","to","travel"],"answer":"I study because I want to travel","es":"Estudio porque quiero viajar."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mi cumpleaños es en mayo.","answer":["My birthday is in May."],"why":"Con meses se usa in."},{"type":"translate","es":"La clase empieza a las cinco.","answer":["The class starts at five.","The class starts at 5.","The class begins at five.","The class begins at 5."],"why":"Con horas se usa at."},{"type":"translate","es":"Estudio inglés porque quiero trabajar en Disney.","answer":["I study English because I want to work at Disney.","I study English because I want to work in Disney."],"why":"Because explica la razón."},{"type":"translate","es":"Primero desayuno y luego voy a la universidad.","answer":["First I have breakfast and then I go to the university.","First, I have breakfast and then I go to the university.","First I have breakfast, then I go to the university.","First, I have breakfast, then I go to the university.","First I eat breakfast and then I go to the university.","First, I eat breakfast and then I go to the university."],"why":"First y then ordenan los pasos."}],"speak":["My birthday is in October.","I have class on Monday at 8 am.","I work from Monday to Friday.","I study English every day because I want to work in Orlando.","I like coffee, but I don't like tea.","It was late, so I went home.","First, I wake up. Then, I have breakfast.","I have studied English since January."],"tip":"Los hispanohablantes dicen *in Monday* o *at May*. Recuerda la regla: in para meses y años, on para días y fechas, at para horas. Y no confundas for (cuánto tiempo) con since (desde cuándo)."},{"n":28,"block":"Para comunicarte","title":"Comparar, gustos y opiniones","emoji":"⚖️","minutes":30,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás comparar cosas, decir qué te gusta o qué prefieres y dar tu opinión con frases simples.","sections":[{"h":"Comparativos: más que...","body":"Para comparar dos cosas, el adjetivo cambia según su longitud.\n\nAdjetivos cortos (una sílaba): agrega **-er** y usa **than**: *Orlando is hotter than Bogotá.* (Orlando es más caliente que Bogotá.)\n\nAdjetivos largos (dos o más sílabas): usa **more ... than**: *English is more interesting than math.*","note":"Cambios de ortografía: big → bigger (se duplica la consonante), happy → happier (y cambia a i), large → larger (solo se agrega r)."},{"h":"Tabla de comparativos","table":{"head":["Adjetivo","Comparativo","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["tall","taller","My brother is taller than me.","Mi hermano es más alto que yo."],["cheap","cheaper","The bus is cheaper than a taxi.","El bus es más barato que un taxi."],["big","bigger","Disney World is bigger than my city.","Disney World es más grande que mi ciudad."],["easy","easier","Spanish is easier for me.","El español es más fácil para mí."],["expensive","more expensive","Orlando is more expensive than Cali.","Orlando es más caro que Cali."],["good","better","This pizza is better than that one.","Esta pizza es mejor que esa."],["bad","worse","The weather is worse today.","El clima está peor hoy."]]},"note":"Good y bad son irregulares: good → better, bad → worse. Nunca digas more good ni more bad."},{"h":"As... as: igual de...","body":"Para decir que dos cosas son iguales usa **as + adjetivo + as**: *I am as tall as my father.* (Soy tan alto como mi papá.)\n\nPara decir que no son iguales: **not as ... as**: *Tea is not as strong as coffee.* (El té no es tan fuerte como el café.)"},{"h":"Superlativos: el más...","table":{"head":["Tipo","Regla","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["Corto","the + adjetivo + -est","the biggest, the tallest, the cheapest","el más grande, el más alto, el más barato"],["Largo","the most + adjetivo","the most beautiful, the most expensive","el más bonito, el más caro"],["Irregular","the best / the worst","the best day, the worst food","el mejor día, la peor comida"]]},"note":"Siempre lleva the: This is the best park in Orlando. Y se dice in (in Orlando, in the world), no of."},{"h":"Gustos: like, love, hate, enjoy, prefer","body":"Estos verbos hablan de gustos. Con otro verbo, este lleva **-ing**:\n\n**I like playing soccer.** (Me gusta jugar fútbol.)\n**She loves dancing.** **We hate waiting in line.** **He enjoys listening to music.**\n\nPara elegir entre dos cosas usa **prefer**: **I prefer tea to coffee.** o **I prefer to stay home.** Para preguntar: **What is your favorite food?**","note":"Enjoy siempre necesita algo: I enjoy my job / I enjoy working. Con he/she/it agrega -s: likes, loves, hates, enjoys, prefers."},{"h":"Dar opiniones","list":["I think English is important. (Creo que el inglés es importante.)","I think it's too expensive. (Creo que es demasiado caro.)","In my opinion, Orlando is a great city. (En mi opinión...)","I agree. / I don't agree. (Estoy de acuerdo. / No estoy de acuerdo.)","What do you think? (¿Qué piensas?)","It's my favorite ride! (¡Es mi atracción favorita!)"],"note":"Para opinar se usa I think, no I believe que suena más fuerte. Para disentir con cortesía: I don't think so."}],"vocab":[{"en":"bigger","es":"más grande","ex":"This room is bigger."},{"en":"smaller","es":"más pequeño","ex":"My phone is smaller than yours."},{"en":"cheaper","es":"más barato","ex":"Buses are cheaper than taxis."},{"en":"more expensive","es":"más caro","ex":"Hotels are more expensive in summer."},{"en":"better","es":"mejor","ex":"English is better with practice."},{"en":"worse","es":"peor","ex":"The traffic is worse today."},{"en":"the best","es":"el mejor","ex":"This is the best day."},{"en":"the worst","es":"el peor","ex":"That was the worst movie."},{"en":"than","es":"que (comparación)","ex":"She is older than me."},{"en":"as ... as","es":"tan ... como","ex":"He is as tall as me."},{"en":"like","es":"gustar","ex":"I like pizza."},{"en":"love","es":"amar, encantar","ex":"I love music."},{"en":"hate","es":"odiar","ex":"I hate waiting."},{"en":"enjoy","es":"disfrutar","ex":"I enjoy walking in the park."},{"en":"prefer","es":"preferir","ex":"I prefer summer to winter."},{"en":"favorite","es":"favorito","ex":"My favorite color is blue."},{"en":"think","es":"pensar, creer","ex":"I think it's great."},{"en":"opinion","es":"opinión","ex":"In my opinion, it's fun."},{"en":"agree","es":"estar de acuerdo","ex":"I agree with you."},{"en":"boring","es":"aburrido","ex":"This movie is boring."},{"en":"interesting","es":"interesante","ex":"English is interesting."},{"en":"fun","es":"divertido","ex":"The ride is fun."}],"examples":[{"en":"My brother is taller than me.","es":"Mi hermano es más alto que yo."},{"en":"The bus is cheaper than the taxi.","es":"El bus es más barato que el taxi."},{"en":"Orlando is hotter than my city.","es":"Orlando es más caliente que mi ciudad."},{"en":"Math is more difficult than English.","es":"Las matemáticas son más difíciles que el inglés."},{"en":"This burger is better than that one.","es":"Esta hamburguesa es mejor que esa."},{"en":"I am as tired as you.","es":"Estoy tan cansado como tú."},{"en":"Magic Kingdom is the biggest park in Orlando.","es":"Magic Kingdom es el parque más grande de Orlando."},{"en":"This is the most beautiful castle in the world.","es":"Este es el castillo más hermoso del mundo."},{"en":"It is the worst traffic of the year.","es":"Es el peor tráfico del año."},{"en":"I like playing video games.","es":"Me gusta jugar videojuegos."},{"en":"She loves dancing and singing.","es":"A ella le encanta bailar y cantar."},{"en":"I hate waiting in line.","es":"Odio esperar en la fila."},{"en":"I prefer tea to coffee.","es":"Prefiero el té al café."},{"en":"I think English is very useful.","es":"Creo que el inglés es muy útil."}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"My city is ___ than Orlando.","options":["small","smaller","more small"],"answer":1,"why":"Small es corto, así que se agrega -er."},{"type":"choice","q":"This phone is ___ than that one.","options":["more expensive","expensiver","most expensive"],"answer":0,"why":"Expensive es largo, así que se usa more ... than."},{"type":"choice","q":"This pizza is ___ than that pizza.","options":["more good","gooder","better"],"answer":2,"why":"Good es irregular: better."},{"type":"choice","q":"It is ___ day of my life!","options":["the best","the goodest","the most good"],"answer":0,"why":"El superlativo de good es the best."},{"type":"choice","q":"She is ___ tall as her brother.","options":["so","as","than"],"answer":1,"why":"As tall as significa tan alto como."},{"type":"choice","q":"I enjoy ___ in the park.","options":["walk","to walks","walking"],"answer":2,"why":"Enjoy va seguido de un verbo con -ing."},{"type":"choice","q":"It's the ___ park in Florida.","options":["most big","biggest","bigger"],"answer":1,"why":"Big es corto: the biggest."},{"type":"fill","q":"My father is ___ than me. (old)","answer":["older"],"why":"Old es corto: older."},{"type":"fill","q":"English is ___ interesting than math. (more/most)","answer":["more"],"why":"Interesting es largo y se compara con more."},{"type":"fill","q":"This is the ___ movie ever! (bad)","answer":["worst"],"why":"El superlativo irregular de bad es worst."},{"type":"fill","q":"I like ___ music. (listen)","answer":["listening to"],"why":"Like va seguido de un verbo con -ing."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ it's a great idea. (opinión)","answer":["think"],"why":"I think se usa para dar opiniones."},{"type":"order","words":["are","than","Taxis","buses","more","expensive"],"answer":"Taxis are more expensive than buses","es":"Los taxis son más caros que los buses."},{"type":"order","words":["the","is","best","This","park"],"answer":"This is the best park","es":"Este es el mejor parque."},{"type":"order","words":["I","playing","love","soccer"],"answer":"I love playing soccer","es":"Amo jugar fútbol."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mi hermano es más alto que yo.","answer":["My brother is taller than me.","My brother is taller than I am.","My brother is taller than I."],"why":"Tall es corto: taller than."},{"type":"translate","es":"Es el parque más grande.","answer":["It is the biggest park.","It's the biggest park."],"why":"Big es corto: the biggest."},{"type":"translate","es":"Prefiero el té al café.","answer":["I prefer tea to coffee.","I prefer tea over coffee."],"why":"Prefer A to B."},{"type":"translate","es":"Creo que es divertido.","answer":["I think it is fun.","I think it's fun.","I think it is funny.","I think it's funny."],"why":"I think da una opinión."}],"speak":["My brother is taller than me.","English is more difficult than Spanish, but I like it.","This is the best day of my life.","I like playing soccer with my friends.","I hate waiting in line.","I prefer tea to coffee.","My favorite city is Orlando.","I think English is very useful."],"tip":"Los hispanohablantes dicen *more tall* o *more good*, o usan *of* en lugar de *in*. Correcto: taller, better, the biggest park in Orlando. Y después de like/love/hate/enjoy usa verbo con -ing: I enjoy playing, no I enjoy to play."},{"n":29,"block":"Para comunicarte","title":"Phrasal verbs y frases del día a día","emoji":"💬","minutes":35,"goal":"Al final de esta clase podrás usar 30 phrasal verbs y 30 expresiones muy comunes para sobrevivir como viajero y como trabajador en Estados Unidos.","sections":[{"h":"¿Qué es un phrasal verb?","body":"Un **phrasal verb** es un verbo + una palabra pequeña (up, down, on, off, out, back...). Juntos significan algo nuevo, a veces muy distinto del verbo solo.\n\nPor ejemplo: **look** = mirar, pero **look for** = buscar, y **give up** = rendirse.\n\nLos nativos los usan todo el día, así que son vitales para entender y hablar natural.","note":"No los traduzcas palabra por palabra. Memoriza el phrasal verb completo con una frase de ejemplo."},{"h":"Phrasal verbs de la rutina (1 a 10)","table":{"head":["Phrasal verb","Significa","Ejemplo","Traducción"],"rows":[["wake up","despertarse","I wake up at 6.","Me despierto a las 6."],["get up","levantarse","I get up at 6:30.","Me levanto a las 6:30."],["go to sleep","dormirse","I go to sleep at 11.","Me duermo a las 11."],["turn on","encender","Turn on the light, please.","Enciende la luz, por favor."],["turn off","apagar","Turn off your phone.","Apaga tu teléfono."],["put on","ponerse (ropa)","I put on my jacket.","Me pongo la chaqueta."],["take off","quitarse / despegar","Take off your shoes. The plane takes off.","Quítate los zapatos. El avión despega."],["sit down","sentarse","Please sit down.","Por favor siéntate."],["stand up","ponerse de pie","Stand up, please.","Ponte de pie, por favor."],["clean up","limpiar, ordenar","I clean up my room.","Ordeno mi cuarto."]]}},{"h":"Phrasal verbs de acción y movimiento (11 a 20)","table":{"head":["Phrasal verb","Significa","Ejemplo","Traducción"],"rows":[["look for","buscar","I look for my keys.","Busco mis llaves."],["look at","mirar","Look at the castle!","¡Mira el castillo!"],["pick up","recoger, levantar","I pick up my bag.","Recojo mi mochila."],["come back","regresar","I come back at 5.","Regreso a las 5."],["go back","volver (a un lugar)","We go back to the hotel.","Volvemos al hotel."],["come in","entrar","Come in, please.","Pasa, por favor."],["go out","salir","We go out on Friday.","Salimos el viernes."],["get in / get out","subir / bajar (de un carro)","Get in the car.","Sube al carro."],["get on / get off","subir / bajar (bus, tren)","Get off at the next stop.","Bájate en la próxima parada."],["hurry up","apurarse","Hurry up, we are late!","¡Apúrate, vamos tarde!"]]}},{"h":"Phrasal verbs de comunicación y trabajo (21 a 30)","table":{"head":["Phrasal verb","Significa","Ejemplo","Traducción"],"rows":[["give up","rendirse","Don't give up!","¡No te rindas!"],["find out","averiguar, enterarse","I want to find out the price.","Quiero averiguar el precio."],["fill out","llenar (formulario)","Fill out this form, please.","Llena este formulario, por favor."],["check in / check out","registrarse / salir del hotel","We check in at 3 pm.","Nos registramos a las 3 pm."],["try on","probarse","Can I try on this shirt?","¿Puedo probarme esta camisa?"],["call back","devolver la llamada","Please call me back.","Por favor devuélveme la llamada."],["write down","anotar","Write down your name.","Anota tu nombre."],["slow down","ir más despacio","Please slow down.","Por favor habla más despacio."],["set up","configurar, organizar","I set up my phone.","Configuro mi teléfono."],["work out","hacer ejercicio / resultar bien","I work out on Monday.","Hago ejercicio los lunes."]]},"note":"Con algunos phrasal verbs puedes separar el objeto: Turn it off (no Turn off it). Con pronombres (it, them, me), el pronombre va en medio."},{"h":"30 expresiones del día a día","list":["Hello! / Hi! (Hola)","Good morning / afternoon / evening (Buenos días / tardes / noches)","How are you? / I'm fine, thanks. (¿Cómo estás? / Bien, gracias)","What's up? (¿Qué tal? informal)","Nice to meet you. (Mucho gusto)","Please. / Thank you. / You're welcome. (Por favor / Gracias / De nada)","No problem. (No hay problema)","Of course. / Sure. (Claro)","Excuse me. (Disculpa, con permiso)","I'm sorry. (Lo siento)","Just a moment. / One moment, please. (Un momento)","Can you repeat that? (¿Puedes repetir?)","Slow down, please. (Más despacio, por favor)","I don't understand. (No entiendo)","I don't know. (No sé)","What does ... mean? (¿Qué significa...?)","How do you say ... in English? (¿Cómo se dice... en inglés?)","Take care. (Cuídate)","See you later. / See you tomorrow. (Nos vemos luego / mañana)","Have a nice day! (¡Que tengas un buen día!)","Good luck! (¡Buena suerte!)","Congratulations! (¡Felicidades!)","Bless you! (¡Salud! al estornudar)","Never mind. (Olvídalo, no importa)","It's OK. / That's fine. (Está bien)","I'm lost. (Estoy perdido)","Where is ...? (¿Dónde está...?)","How much is it? (¿Cuánto cuesta?)","I'm hungry / thirsty / tired. (Tengo hambre / sed / sueño)","Help! / I need help. (¡Ayuda!)"]},{"h":"Para sobrevivir en EE. UU.","body":"**Como viajero:** *Where is the bus stop?*, *Can I check in, please?*, *One ticket to Orlando, please*, *Is there Wi-Fi here?*, *I have a reservation.*\n\n**Como trabajador:** *Can I help you?*, *Just a moment, please.*, *I'm sorry, I don't understand. Can you repeat that?*, *I'll find out for you.*, *What time is my shift?*, *Thanks, have a nice day!*\n\nCon esas frases puedes resolver casi cualquier situación. Cuando no entiendas, di **Can you speak more slowly, please?** Es normal y nadie se molesta.","note":"En EE. UU. se espera cortesía: usa please, thank you y excuse me todo el tiempo y sonríe."}],"vocab":[{"en":"wake up","es":"despertarse","ex":"I wake up at 6."},{"en":"get up","es":"levantarse","ex":"I get up early."},{"en":"turn on","es":"encender","ex":"Turn on the TV."},{"en":"turn off","es":"apagar","ex":"Turn off the light."},{"en":"put on","es":"ponerse","ex":"Put on your jacket."},{"en":"look for","es":"buscar","ex":"I look for my phone."},{"en":"pick up","es":"recoger","ex":"Pick up your bag."},{"en":"come back","es":"regresar","ex":"Come back soon."},{"en":"give up","es":"rendirse","ex":"Never give up."},{"en":"find out","es":"averiguar","ex":"Let's find out."},{"en":"check in","es":"registrarse","ex":"We check in at 3."},{"en":"fill out","es":"llenar","ex":"Fill out the form."},{"en":"No problem","es":"no hay problema","ex":"No problem, I can help."},{"en":"Of course","es":"claro","ex":"Of course, come in."},{"en":"I'm sorry","es":"lo siento","ex":"I'm sorry I'm late."},{"en":"Excuse me","es":"disculpa, con permiso","ex":"Excuse me, where is the exit?"},{"en":"Take care","es":"cuídate","ex":"Bye, take care!"},{"en":"What's up?","es":"¿qué tal?","ex":"Hey, what's up?"},{"en":"Just a moment","es":"un momento","ex":"Just a moment, please."},{"en":"See you later","es":"nos vemos luego","ex":"Bye! See you later."},{"en":"Good luck","es":"buena suerte","ex":"Good luck tomorrow!"},{"en":"Never mind","es":"olvídalo","ex":"Never mind, it's OK."},{"en":"I'm lost","es":"estoy perdido","ex":"Excuse me, I'm lost."},{"en":"Have a nice day","es":"que tengas un buen día","ex":"Thanks, have a nice day!"}],"examples":[{"en":"I wake up at six and get up at six thirty.","es":"Me despierto a las seis y me levanto a las seis y media."},{"en":"Please turn off your phone.","es":"Por favor apaga tu teléfono."},{"en":"It is cold, so put on your jacket.","es":"Hace frío, así que ponte la chaqueta."},{"en":"I'm looking for the bathroom.","es":"Estoy buscando el baño."},{"en":"Can you pick up my bag?","es":"¿Puedes recoger mi bolso?"},{"en":"We come back to the hotel at nine.","es":"Regresamos al hotel a las nueve."},{"en":"Don't give up, your English is improving.","es":"No te rindas, tu inglés está mejorando."},{"en":"I need to find out the price of the ticket.","es":"Necesito averiguar el precio del boleto."},{"en":"Please fill out this form.","es":"Por favor llena este formulario."},{"en":"Excuse me, can you help me? I'm lost.","es":"Disculpe, ¿me puede ayudar? Estoy perdido."},{"en":"Just a moment, please. I'll check.","es":"Un momento, por favor. Voy a revisar."},{"en":"No problem. Of course I can help.","es":"No hay problema. Claro que puedo ayudar."},{"en":"I'm sorry, I don't understand. Can you repeat that?","es":"Lo siento, no entiendo. ¿Puede repetir eso?"},{"en":"Bye, take care! See you tomorrow.","es":"¡Chao, cuídate! Nos vemos mañana."},{"en":"Get off at the next stop.","es":"Bájate en la próxima parada."},{"en":"Thanks, have a nice day!","es":"Gracias, ¡que tengas un buen día!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"It's dark. Please ___ the light.","options":["turn on","turn up","get in"],"answer":0,"why":"Turn on significa encender."},{"type":"choice","q":"I can't find my keys. I'm ___ them.","options":["looking at","looking for","looking up"],"answer":1,"why":"Look for significa buscar."},{"type":"choice","q":"The test is hard, but don't ___!","options":["give up","give on","give in"],"answer":0,"why":"Give up significa rendirse."},{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ at 6 every morning. (despertarse)","options":["wake up","wake on","wake in"],"answer":0,"why":"Wake up significa despertarse."},{"type":"choice","q":"Someone says: Thank you! You answer: ___","options":["You're welcome.","I'm sorry.","Bless you."],"answer":0,"why":"You're welcome es la respuesta a thank you."},{"type":"choice","q":"You step on someone's foot. You say: ___","options":["Good luck!","I'm sorry.","See you later."],"answer":1,"why":"I'm sorry se usa para disculparse."},{"type":"choice","q":"You don't understand a word. Which is correct?","options":["Can you repeat that, please?","Where is the bus stop?","Have a nice day!"],"answer":0,"why":"Can you repeat that? sirve para pedir que repitan."},{"type":"fill","q":"Please ___ off your shoes. (quitarse)","answer":["take"],"why":"Take off significa quitarse."},{"type":"fill","q":"We ___ in at the hotel at 3 pm.","answer":["check"],"why":"Check in es registrarse en el hotel."},{"type":"fill","q":"Hurry ___, we are late!","answer":["up"],"why":"Hurry up significa apurarse."},{"type":"fill","q":"Please sit ___ and wait.","answer":["down"],"why":"Sit down significa sentarse."},{"type":"fill","q":"A: Thank you! B: No ___.","answer":["problem"],"why":"No problem es una respuesta común a thank you."},{"type":"order","words":["moment","a","Just","please"],"answer":"Just a moment please","es":"Un momento, por favor."},{"type":"order","words":["I","for","my","looking","am","keys"],"answer":"I am looking for my keys","es":"Estoy buscando mis llaves."},{"type":"order","words":["on","the","Turn","light"],"answer":"Turn on the light","es":"Enciende la luz."},{"type":"translate","es":"Apaga tu teléfono, por favor.","answer":["Turn off your phone, please.","Turn off your phone please.","Please turn off your phone.","Please, turn off your phone.","Turn your phone off, please.","Please turn your phone off."],"why":"Turn off significa apagar."},{"type":"translate","es":"Disculpe, estoy perdido.","answer":["Excuse me, I'm lost.","Excuse me, I am lost.","Excuse me I'm lost.","Excuse me I am lost.","Sorry, I'm lost.","Sorry, I am lost."],"why":"Excuse me para llamar la atención e I'm lost para decir que estás perdido."},{"type":"translate","es":"Regreso a las cinco.","answer":["I come back at five.","I come back at 5.","I'll come back at five.","I'll come back at 5.","I will come back at five.","I will come back at 5.","I'm coming back at five.","I'm coming back at 5.","I am coming back at five.","I am coming back at 5.","I go back at five.","I go back at 5."],"why":"Come back significa regresar."}],"speak":["I wake up at six and get up at six thirty.","Excuse me, I'm lost. Where is the bus stop?","Just a moment, please.","I'm sorry, I don't understand. Can you repeat that?","Can I check in, please? I have a reservation.","No problem. Of course I can help you.","Thanks, have a nice day! Take care!","Never give up. I want to work at Disney."],"tip":"Muchos hispanohablantes dicen *turn off it* o traducen palabra por palabra *look up for*. Aprende el phrasal verb completo: look for, y con pronombre separa: turn it off, pick it up. Y recuerda: *Excuse me* es para llamar la atención y *I'm sorry* para disculparte."},{"n":30,"block":"Para comunicarte","title":"Repaso general","emoji":"🔁","minutes":35,"goal":"Al final de esta clase habrás repasado todo el curso: to be, presente, pasado, futuro, presente continuo, can y las palabras de pregunta, y sabrás evitar los errores más comunes de los hispanohablantes.","sections":[{"h":"Resumen de los tiempos del curso","table":{"head":["Tema","Estructura","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["To be","I am / you are / he, she, it is / we, you, they are","She is a student.","Ella es estudiante."],["Presente simple","verbo base (+ s con he/she/it)","He works every day.","Él trabaja todos los días."],["Presente simple (neg. y preg.)","don't / doesn't + verbo base; Do / Does + sujeto + verbo?","Does she like pizza?","¿A ella le gusta la pizza?"],["Pasado simple","verbo + ed (regular) o forma irregular","I watched a movie. / I went home.","Vi una película. / Fui a casa."],["Pasado (neg. y preg.)","didn't + verbo base; Did + sujeto + verbo base?","Did you study? No, I didn't.","¿Estudiaste? No."],["Futuro con will","will + verbo base","I will call you later.","Te llamaré más tarde."],["Futuro con going to","am/is/are + going to + verbo base","We are going to travel next week.","Vamos a viajar la próxima semana."],["Presente continuo","am/is/are + verbo + ing","They are playing soccer now.","Ellos están jugando fútbol ahora."],["Can","can / can't + verbo base (sin to)","I can code. She can't swim.","Sé programar. Ella no sabe nadar."]]},"note":"Regla de oro: en preguntas y negativos con do/does/did, el verbo principal vuelve a su forma base. Did you go? (no Did you went?)."},{"h":"Palabras de pregunta","table":{"head":["Palabra","Pregunta por","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["What","cosa","What is your name?","¿Cuál es tu nombre?"],["Where","lugar","Where do you live?","¿Dónde vives?"],["When","momento","When is the class?","¿Cuándo es la clase?"],["Who","persona","Who is he?","¿Quién es él?"],["Why","razón","Why are you tired?","¿Por qué estás cansado?"],["How","manera o estado","How are you?","¿Cómo estás?"],["How many / How much","cantidad","How many brothers do you have?","¿Cuántos hermanos tienes?"],["What time","hora","What time is it?","¿Qué hora es?"]]},"note":"Estructura: palabra de pregunta + do/does/did (o is/are/can) + sujeto + verbo. Where did you go? / Why are you late?"},{"h":"Errores que debes evitar","body":"Estos son los errores más típicos de quienes hablan español. Si los corriges, tu inglés mejora muchísimo:","list":["I have 20 years. → I am 20 years old. (la edad se dice con to be)","He go to work. → He goes to work. (con he/she/it el verbo lleva -s o -es)","I am agree. → I agree. (agree ya es verbo, no necesita am)","She cans swim. → She can swim. (can nunca lleva -s)","Do you can swim? → Can you swim? (can no usa do/does)","Did you went? → Did you go? (después de did, verbo base)","I no like coffee. → I don't like coffee. (el negativo usa don't)","Is cold today. → It is cold today. (en inglés siempre hay sujeto: it, there...)","I am agree / I am go → I agree / I go (no mezcles am con otro verbo, salvo -ing)","I have hunger. → I am hungry. (hambre, sed, frío y sueño usan to be)"],"note":"Mientras hablas, hazte una pregunta rápida: ¿tengo sujeto y verbo? ¿el verbo está en la forma correcta?"},{"h":"Recordatorio: la hora","body":"Para preguntar: **What time is it?** Para responder: **It's + hora**.\n\n**It's seven o'clock.** (7:00) · **It's seven thirty.** o **half past seven.** (7:30) · **It's a quarter past seven.** (7:15) · **It's a quarter to eight.** (7:45)\n\nPara decir *a qué hora* ocurre algo usa **at**: *The class is at 6 p.m.* Usa **a.m.** para la mañana y **p.m.** para la tarde y la noche.","note":"Cuidado: It's (hora) con it, no con they. Se dice It's three o'clock, no They are three."},{"h":"Recordatorio: países y nacionalidades","table":{"head":["País","Nacionalidad","Ejemplo","Significa"],"rows":[["Colombia","Colombian","I'm from Colombia. I'm Colombian.","Soy de Colombia. Soy colombiano."],["Mexico","Mexican","She is Mexican.","Ella es mexicana."],["Spain","Spanish","He is from Spain.","Él es de España."],["the United States","American","They are American.","Ellos son estadounidenses."],["Brazil","Brazilian","My friend is Brazilian.","Mi amigo es brasileño."],["Canada","Canadian","I want to visit Canada.","Quiero visitar Canadá."]]},"note":"Los países y las nacionalidades siempre se escriben con mayúscula inicial: Colombian, Spanish, English."},{"h":"Recordatorio: números","body":"**1-10:** one, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight, nine, ten.\n\n**11-20:** eleven, twelve, thirteen, fourteen, fifteen, sixteen, seventeen, eighteen, nineteen, twenty.\n\n**Decenas:** twenty, thirty, forty, fifty, sixty, seventy, eighty, ninety, one hundred.\n\nPara unir: **twenty-one** (21), **thirty-five** (35), **ninety-nine** (99).","note":"No confundas thirteen (13) con thirty (30), ni fifteen (15) con fifty (50). Escucha dónde cae el acento: thirTEEN, THIRty."},{"h":"Cómo seguir practicando","list":["Habla en voz alta cada día: presenta tu rutina en 5 frases.","Escribe un mini diario: What did I do yesterday? What am I going to do tomorrow?","Cambia el idioma de tu teléfono o de tus apps a inglés.","Mira series con subtítulos en inglés y repite frases cortas.","Lee documentación técnica en inglés: ya conoces muchas palabras de programación.","Repasa las clases anteriores y repite los ejercicios que te costaron más."]}],"vocab":[{"en":"am / is / are","es":"soy, estoy, eres, es, somos...","ex":"She is my friend."},{"en":"have / has","es":"tener","ex":"He has two brothers."},{"en":"go / went","es":"ir / fui, fue","ex":"I went to the university yesterday."},{"en":"do / does / did","es":"auxiliares para preguntas y negativos","ex":"Did you eat breakfast?"},{"en":"don't / doesn't / didn't","es":"no (presente y pasado)","ex":"She doesn't like coffee."},{"en":"will","es":"futuro (promesa, decisión)","ex":"I will help you."},{"en":"going to","es":"ir a (plan)","ex":"I'm going to study tonight."},{"en":"can / can't","es":"poder, saber / no poder","ex":"I can't drive."},{"en":"now","es":"ahora","ex":"I'm studying English now."},{"en":"yesterday","es":"ayer","ex":"I played soccer yesterday."},{"en":"tomorrow","es":"mañana","ex":"We have class tomorrow."},{"en":"every day","es":"todos los días","ex":"I practice English every day."},{"en":"what / where / when","es":"qué / dónde / cuándo","ex":"Where do you live?"},{"en":"who / why / how","es":"quién / por qué / cómo","ex":"Why are you late?"},{"en":"how many","es":"cuántos","ex":"How many classes do you have?"},{"en":"What time is it?","es":"¿Qué hora es?","ex":"What time is it? It's five o'clock."},{"en":"years old","es":"años de edad","ex":"I am 20 years old."},{"en":"agree","es":"estar de acuerdo","ex":"I agree with you."},{"en":"I would like","es":"quisiera","ex":"I would like some water."},{"en":"please / thank you","es":"por favor / gracias","ex":"Thank you for your help."}],"examples":[{"en":"I am Santiago and I am 20 years old.","es":"Soy Santiago y tengo 20 años."},{"en":"I am from Colombia. I am Colombian.","es":"Soy de Colombia. Soy colombiano."},{"en":"He goes to the university every day.","es":"Él va a la universidad todos los días."},{"en":"She doesn't work on Sundays.","es":"Ella no trabaja los domingos."},{"en":"Yesterday I studied programming for two hours.","es":"Ayer estudié programación durante dos horas."},{"en":"Did you go to class last Monday?","es":"¿Fuiste a clase el lunes pasado?"},{"en":"I will call you tonight.","es":"Te llamaré esta noche."},{"en":"We are going to travel next month.","es":"Vamos a viajar el próximo mes."},{"en":"They are playing video games right now.","es":"Ellos están jugando videojuegos ahora mismo."},{"en":"I can write code, but I can't draw.","es":"Sé escribir código, pero no sé dibujar."},{"en":"Where do you live?","es":"¿Dónde vives?"},{"en":"What time is the class? It's at six thirty.","es":"¿A qué hora es la clase? Es a las seis y media."},{"en":"I have thirty-five classmates.","es":"Tengo treinta y cinco compañeros."},{"en":"I agree with you. Thank you very much!","es":"Estoy de acuerdo contigo. ¡Muchas gracias!"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["I am agree.","I agree.","I have agree."],"answer":1,"why":"Agree ya es un verbo: se dice I agree, sin am."},{"type":"choice","q":"I ___ 20 years old.","options":["am","have","is"],"answer":0,"why":"La edad se dice con to be: I am 20 years old, no I have 20 years."},{"type":"choice","q":"He ___ to the university every day.","options":["go","goes","going"],"answer":1,"why":"Con he/she/it en presente simple el verbo lleva -es: goes."},{"type":"choice","q":"Yesterday I ___ a movie with my friends.","options":["watch","watched","watching"],"answer":1,"why":"Yesterday indica pasado, y el pasado regular termina en -ed: watched."},{"type":"choice","q":"Look at those clouds! It ___ rain.","options":["is going to","are going to","go to"],"answer":0,"why":"Para una predicción con evidencia se usa going to; con it va is."},{"type":"choice","q":"Which question asks about a place?","options":["Where do you live?","When do you live?","Who do you live?"],"answer":0,"why":"Where pregunta por el lugar: ¿dónde?"},{"type":"choice","q":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["Do you can swim?","You can swim?","Can you swim?"],"answer":2,"why":"Con can la pregunta se forma invirtiendo el orden, sin do/does: Can you swim?"},{"type":"fill","q":"They ___ my best friends. (to be)","answer":["are"],"why":"They usa are."},{"type":"fill","q":"She ___ like coffee. (negativo)","answer":["doesn't","does not"],"why":"Con she el negativo del presente simple es doesn't."},{"type":"fill","q":"Last year I ___ in Medellín. (to be, pasado)","answer":["was"],"why":"El pasado de am es was."},{"type":"fill","q":"I ___ play the guitar. (sé tocar)","answer":["can"],"why":"Para habilidad se usa can."},{"type":"fill","q":"El número 30 en inglés es: ___","answer":["thirty"],"why":"30 es thirty; thirteen es 13."},{"type":"order","words":["is","She","to","going","study","tonight"],"answer":"She is going to study tonight","es":"Ella va a estudiar esta noche."},{"type":"order","words":["time","is","What","it"],"answer":"What time is it","es":"¿Qué hora es?"},{"type":"order","words":["you","Where","did","go","yesterday"],"answer":"Where did you go yesterday","es":"¿Adónde fuiste ayer?"},{"type":"order","words":["fish","He","doesn't","like"],"answer":"He doesn't like fish","es":"A él no le gusta el pescado."},{"type":"translate","es":"Tengo 20 años.","answer":["I am 20 years old.","I'm 20 years old.","I am 20.","I'm 20."],"why":"La edad se dice con to be: I am 20 years old."},{"type":"translate","es":"Estoy de acuerdo.","answer":["I agree.","I agree"],"why":"Agree es un verbo; no se usa am."},{"type":"translate","es":"Ella está cocinando ahora.","answer":["She is cooking now.","She's cooking now.","She is cooking right now.","She's cooking right now."],"why":"Presente continuo: is + cooking."},{"type":"translate","es":"Mañana voy a viajar a Canadá.","answer":["Tomorrow I am going to travel to Canada.","Tomorrow I'm going to travel to Canada.","I am going to travel to Canada tomorrow.","I'm going to travel to Canada tomorrow."],"why":"Un plan se expresa con am going to + verbo base."}],"speak":["I am Santiago and I am 20 years old.","I am from Colombia and I study systems engineering.","I go to the university every day.","Yesterday I studied English for one hour.","Tomorrow I am going to practice my speaking.","I can write code and I want to learn more English.","What time is it, please?","Thank you for your help!"],"tip":"Antes de decir una frase, revisa tres cosas: sujeto, verbo y tiempo. Si dudas, usa frases cortas y simples; es mejor una frase sencilla y correcta que una larga con errores. Repasa esta clase cada semana."}];
